__load("lore",[{"slug":"ancient-gear","kind":"archetype","name":"Ancient Gear","badge":{"es":"Máquinas antiguas de engranajes, el mazo de Crowler en GX","en":"Cog-built ancient machines, Crowler's deck in GX"},"origin":{"es":"Anime Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (Crowler); luego 5D's y ARC-V","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX anime (Crowler); later 5D's and ARC-V"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Las máquinas insignia de Crowler","en":"Crowler's signature machines"},"p":{"es":"En el anime de GX, los Ancient Gear son el mazo de Vellian Crowler, y también de Dimitri. Ancient Gear Golem es la carta que más se ve: aparece en los episodios 1, 2, 18 y 167, y el mazo de Crowler gira en torno a invocarlo lo antes posible, con cartas como The Trojan Horse. Su fusión, Ultimate Ancient Gear Golem, también está en ese mazo. En la carta, el Golem es un coloso de 3000 ATK que no deja al rival activar Magias ni Trampas cuando ataca y perfora monstruos en defensa.","en":"In the GX anime, Ancient Gear is the deck of Vellian Crowler, and also of Dimitri. Ancient Gear Golem is the card you see most: it appears in episodes 1, 2, 18 and 167, and Crowler's deck is built around summoning it as fast as possible, with cards like The Trojan Horse. Its fusion, Ultimate Ancient Gear Golem, is also in that deck. On the card, the Golem is a 3000 ATK colossus that stops the opponent from activating Spells or Traps when it attacks and pierces monsters in defense."},"cards":["Ancient Gear Golem","Ultimate Ancient Gear Golem"]},{"h":{"es":"El Castle y la etiqueta \"Ancient\"","en":"The Castle and the \"Ancient\" tag"},"p":{"es":"Ancient Gear Castle sale en GX en los episodios 31 y 69, en manos de Crowler. En pantalla se la describe como un refuerzo de ATK para monstruos \"Ancient\", no solo \"Ancient Gear\". Según Yugipedia, existe un arquetipo exclusivo del anime llamado \"Ancient\", respaldado únicamente por el efecto animado de Ancient Gear Tank. La carta real es distinta: da 300 ATK a los Ancient Gear, suma un contador por cada Invocación Normal o Colocación, y con suficientes contadores se puede usar como Tributo en lugar de un monstruo.","en":"Ancient Gear Castle appears in GX in episodes 31 and 69, in Crowler's hands. On screen it is described as an ATK boost for \"Ancient\" monsters, not just \"Ancient Gear\". According to Yugipedia, there is an anime-only archetype called \"Ancient\", supported solely by the anime effect of Ancient Gear Tank. The real card is different: it gives Ancient Gear monsters 300 ATK, adds a counter for each Normal Summon or Set, and with enough counters it can be Tributed in place of a monster."},"cards":["Ancient Gear Castle","Ancient Gear Tank"]},{"h":{"es":"5D's y ARC-V: espíritus antiguos","en":"5D's and ARC-V: ancient spirits"},"p":{"es":"Después de GX, el arquetipo sigue en pantalla: Rudolph Heitmann lo usa en 5D's, y en ARC-V lo usan alumnos de Duel Academy (Yuri, Dennis McField, Jean Michel Roget) y la Obelisk Force, con foco en Invocaciones por Fusión. Los cánticos de invocación de ARC-V hablan de \"espíritus antiguos\", y el fondo de Ancient Gear Advance en Master Duel dice algo parecido. Yugipedia lee de ahí que podrían ser máquinas viejas poseídas por espíritus, pero es una interpretación suya, no algo confirmado.","en":"After GX the archetype keeps appearing on screen: Rudolph Heitmann uses it in 5D's, and in ARC-V it is used by Duel Academy students (Yuri, Dennis McField, Jean Michel Roget) and by the Obelisk Force, with a focus on Fusion Summons. ARC-V's summon chants mention \"ancient spirits\", and the Ancient Gear Advance wallpaper in Master Duel says something similar. Yugipedia reads from this that they might be old machines possessed by spirits, but that is its own interpretation, not something confirmed."},"cards":["Ancient Gear Advance"]},{"h":{"es":"Diseño: esqueletos de engranajes","en":"Design: skeletons of cogs"},"p":{"es":"Todos los Ancient Gear parecen robots de cuerpo esquelético, con engranajes uniendo las partes, y los humanoides recuerdan a soldados de la Grecia antigua. Yugipedia especula que el diseño podría inspirarse en el mecanismo de Anticitera, aunque no hay confirmación. Hay un detalle que la wiki también marca como interpretación: los monstruos se mueven solos pese a su aspecto viejo, lo que sugeriría que son más avanzados de lo que parecen. En Japón el nombre es \"Antique Gear\", es decir, \"engranaje antiguo\".","en":"All Ancient Gear monsters look like robots with skeletal bodies, with cogs joining the parts, and the humanoid ones resemble ancient Greek soldiers. Yugipedia speculates that the design may be inspired by the Antikythera mechanism, though this is unconfirmed. The wiki also flags one more reading as interpretation: the monsters move on their own despite their old look, which would suggest they are more advanced than they appear. In Japan the name is \"Antique Gear\", meaning old or antique gear."},"cards":["Ancient Gear Soldier"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Ancient Gear","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Ancient_Gear","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Ancient Gear (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Ancient_Gear_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Ancient Gear Castle (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Ancient_Gear_Castle_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Vellian Crowler","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Vellian_Crowler","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"No encontramos en las fuentes leídas ninguna historia sobre una civilización antigua detrás de los Ancient Gear, así que no la incluimos. Lo del espíritu y el mecanismo de Anticitera son interpretaciones de Yugipedia. Los episodios citados corresponden a las versiones animadas de las cartas. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The sources we read contain no backstory about an ancient civilization behind Ancient Gear, so we left it out. The spirit idea and the Antikythera mechanism are Yugipedia's interpretations. The episodes cited refer to the anime versions of the cards. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"blackwing","kind":"archetype","name":"Blackwing","badge":{"es":"El mazo de Crow Hogan: aves negras que traen el viento","en":"Crow Hogan's deck: black birds that bring the wind"},"origin":{"es":"Anime Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's; debut de cartas en Crimson Crisis","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's anime; cards debuted in Crimson Crisis"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Crow, el chico de Satellite","en":"Crow, the kid from Satellite"},"p":{"es":"Crow Hogan quedó huérfano cuando sus padres murieron en el Zero Reverse y creció solo en Satellite. Encontró unas cartas en un basural, entre ellas D.D. Crow y Crow Goblin, y armó un mazo con ellas. Mientras jugaba con otros chicos conoció a Jack y a Yusei, que se volvieron su familia junto a Martha, y el juego le mejoró la lectura y las cuentas. Más tarde cuidó a chicos sin hogar, a quienes les robaba cartas y les enseñaba a duelear. De adolescente, con Jack y Yusei conoció a Kalin, y los cuatro formaron The Enforcers con Kalin de líder.","en":"Crow Hogan was orphaned when his parents died in the Zero Reverse, and grew up alone in Satellite. He found some cards in a dump, including D.D. Crow and Crow Goblin, and built a Deck with them. While playing with other kids he met Jack and Yusei, who became his family along with Martha, and the game improved his reading and arithmetic. He later looked after homeless kids, stealing cards for them and teaching them to Duel. As a teenager he, Jack and Yusei met Kalin, and the four formed The Enforcers with Kalin as leader."},"cards":["D.D. Crow","Crow Goblin"]},{"h":{"es":"Un mazo heredado y un Dragón","en":"An inherited Deck and a Dragon"},"p":{"es":"Los Blackwing los usaron Crow y Robert Pearson, y Crow heredó el mazo de Pearson. Para averiguar qué le pasó a Robert, Crow duelea contra Bolton y apuesta el legendario Black-Winged Dragon, una carta que Pearson nunca le había dejado. En pleno duelo, su Mark of the Dragon reacciona y revela un compartimento oculto en su Duel Runner con esa carta. Yusei y Jack ven reaccionar sus marcas y concluyen que es el Signer Dragon de Crow. En la carta, el Dragón convierte el daño de efecto en contadores que le restan 700 ATK cada uno.","en":"Blackwing was used by Crow and Robert Pearson, and Crow inherited Pearson's Deck. To find out what happened to Robert, Crow Duels Bolton and wagers the legendary Black-Winged Dragon, a card Pearson had never left to him. Mid-Duel, his Mark of the Dragon reacts and reveals a hidden compartment in his Duel Runner holding that card. Yusei and Jack see their Marks react and conclude it is Crow's Signer Dragon. On the card, the Dragon turns effect damage into counters that each take away 700 ATK."},"cards":["Black-Winged Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Contra un Dark Signer","en":"Against a Dark Signer"},"p":{"es":"En el arco de los Dark Signers, Crow desafía a Greiger en un Shadow Turbo Duel para vengar a los chicos de Satellite. Pide que ambos apaguen el piloto automático porque cree que va a necesitar esquivar los ataques de un Earthbound Immortal. Cuando Greiger invoca a Earthbound Immortal Chacu Challhua, Crow roba su última carta y Sincroniza a Blackwing - Silverwind the Ascendant. Con ella gana, y según Yugipedia es el primer no Signer en vencer solo a un Dark Signer.","en":"In the Dark Signers arc, Crow challenges Greiger to a Shadow Turbo Duel to avenge the kids of Satellite. He asks both players to turn off autopilot because he thinks he will need to dodge an Earthbound Immortal's attacks. When Greiger Summons Earthbound Immortal Chacu Challhua, Crow draws his last card and Synchro Summons Blackwing - Silverwind the Ascendant. With it he wins, and according to Yugipedia he is the first non-Signer to beat a Dark Signer on his own."},"cards":["Blackwing - Silverwind the Ascendant","Earthbound Immortal Chacu Challhua"]},{"h":{"es":"Los nombres: vientos y fenómenos","en":"The names: winds and phenomena"},"p":{"es":"En el anime de 5D's, los Blackwing se nombran por elementos geográficos y fenómenos naturales, sobre todo vientos y aves. Por ejemplo, Kalut the Moon Shadow toma su nombre de la luz de la luna. En el manga los nombres salen de armas míticas y fenómenos del cielo. En Japón el arquetipo se llama \"Black Feather\". En la carta, Kalut se descarta de la mano durante el Damage Step para dar 1400 ATK a un Blackwing que esté combatiendo.","en":"In the 5D's anime, Blackwing monsters are named after geographical elements and natural phenomena, mostly winds and birds. For example, Kalut the Moon Shadow takes its name from moonlight. In the manga the names come from mythical weapons and sky phenomena. In Japan the archetype is called \"Black Feather\". On the card, Kalut is discarded from your hand during the Damage Step to give a battling Blackwing 1400 ATK."},"cards":["Blackwing - Kalut the Moon Shadow","Blackwing - Gale the Whirlwind"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Blackwing","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Blackwing","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Crow Hogan","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Crow_Hogan","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Black-Winged Dragon","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Black-Winged_Dragon","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Blackwing - Kalut the Moon Shadow","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Blackwing_-_Kalut_the_Moon_Shadow","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia de Crow es del anime de 5D's; el efecto de Black-Winged Dragon y de Kalut es el de la carta del TCG. No se cuenta la historia de Robert Pearson más allá de lo que dice la ficha de Crow. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"Crow's story is from the 5D's anime; the effects of Black-Winged Dragon and Kalut are those of the TCG cards. Robert Pearson's story is not covered beyond what Crow's page says. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"blue-eyes","kind":"archetype","name":"Blue-Eyes","badge":{"es":"El dragón de Kaiba, con raíces en el Antiguo Egipto","en":"Kaiba's dragon, with roots in ancient Egypt"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga y anime) y el juego de cartas","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga and anime) and the card game"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Kaiba y su obsesión (anime)","en":"Kaiba's obsession (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, Seto Kaiba trata al Blue-Eyes White Dragon como su carta insignia y lo repite en sus pertenencias: Kaiba Land, su jet y su ropa. De chico, con un dibujo de la carta en su mazo, juró conseguir algún día un Blue-Eyes de verdad. Después llegó a tener tres de las cuatro copias y, en el episodio 1, le ganó la cuarta al abuelo de Yugi, Solomon Muto, y la rompió para que nunca pudiera usarse contra él. Tampoco tolera que otros usen las suyas: en el episodio 136 se enfurece cuando Joey usa una.","en":"In the anime, Seto Kaiba treats Blue-Eyes White Dragon as his signature card and repeats it across his belongings: Kaiba Land, his jet and his clothes. As a kid, with a drawing of the card in his Deck, he vowed to get a real Blue-Eyes one day. He later came to own three of the four copies and, in episode 1, won the fourth from Yugi's grandfather, Solomon Muto, and tore it up so it could never be used against him. He doesn't tolerate others using his either: in episode 136 he gets furious when Joey uses one."},"cards":["Blue-Eyes White Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"El pasado en Egipto (anime)","en":"The Egyptian past (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Según el anime, el sacerdote Seto, antecesor de Kaiba, salvó de chico a una niña, Kisara, de unos traficantes de esclavos. Cuando ellos mataron a la madre de Seto, ella liberó sin querer al dragón que llevaba dentro, que acabó con los traficantes. Años después Seto la encuentra apedreada por su pelo blanco y sus ojos azules, y la lleva al palacio. Kisara muere recibiendo un golpe destinado a Seto, y Aknadin sella al dragón en una tablilla. Su espíritu vuelve, libera a Seto del control mental de Aknadin y lo deja como nuevo guardián del Blue-Eyes.","en":"According to the anime, Priest Seto, Kaiba's ancestor, saved a girl named Kisara from slave traders when they were kids. When the traders killed Seto's mother, she unknowingly released the dragon inside her, which dealt with the traders. Years later Seto finds her being stoned over her white hair and blue eyes, and takes her to the palace. Kisara dies taking a blow meant for Seto, and Aknadin seals the dragon in a tablet. Her spirit returns, frees Seto from Aknadin's mind control and leaves him as the Blue-Eyes' new keeper."},"cards":["Maiden with Eyes of Blue"]},{"h":{"es":"The White Dragon (manga)","en":"The White Dragon (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga el dragón se llama The White Dragon (Shirokiryū en japonés) y es el ka de Kisara, unido a su ba, por lo que solo sale cuando ella está inconsciente. Seto lo descubre durante su cacería de ka. Akhenaden exige poner a prueba al dragón: Kisara no se defiende, Seto interviene y el dragón sale, los cubre con la cola y dispara luz que perfora el techo. En la batalla final Akhenaden mata a Kisara, posee a Seto y sella al dragón en una tablilla para usarlo contra Atem. Vence al Dark Magician, pero el espíritu de Kisara lo vuelve contra Akhenaden.","en":"In the manga the dragon is called The White Dragon (Shirokiryū in Japanese) and is Kisara's spirit ka, united with her ba, so it only comes out when she is unconscious. Seto finds it during his ka hunt. Akhenaden demands the dragon be tested: Kisara puts up no resistance, Seto steps in and the dragon emerges, shields them with its tail and fires a light blast through the ceiling. In the final battle Akhenaden kills Kisara, possesses Seto and seals the dragon in a tablet to use against Atem. It beats the Dark Magician, but Kisara's spirit turns it on Akhenaden."},"cards":["Maiden of White"]},{"h":{"es":"De Seto a Kaiba, y a las cartas","en":"From Seto to Kaiba, and into the cards"},"p":{"es":"Takahashi dijo que quiso explorar más la relación entre Seto y Kisara, pero lo recortó por plazos de entrega, y que el cariño de Seto por ella está detrás de la obsesión actual de Kaiba con el dragón. En el anime, el duelo de Kaiba contra Ishizu en Battle City le muestra la visión de Seto sosteniendo el cuerpo de Kisara ante la tablilla. Las cartas lo repiten: las tres copias de Kaiba se fusionan en el Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon, y Kisara inspiró a Maiden of White además de a Maiden with Eyes of Blue.","en":"Takahashi said he wanted to explore Seto and Kisara's relationship further but cut it to meet a deadline, and that Seto's feelings for her are the basis of Kaiba's modern obsession with the dragon. In the anime, Kaiba's Battle City Duel against Ishizu shows him the vision of Seto holding Kisara's body before the tablet. The cards echo this: Kaiba's three copies fuse into Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon, while Kisara inspired Maiden of White as well as Maiden with Eyes of Blue."},"cards":["Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon","Blue-Eyes Spirit Dragon"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Blue-Eyes White Dragon","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Blue-Eyes_White_Dragon","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Seto Kaiba","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Seto_Kaiba","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Kisara","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Kisara","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The White Dragon (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_White_Dragon_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"El texto de la carta solo habla de un dragón legendario casi invencible; el resto es lore de anime o manga. Los nombres cambian entre ambos (Aknadin en el anime, Akhenaden en el manga). No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The card text only describes a legendary, near-invincible dragon; the rest is anime or manga lore. Names differ between the two (Aknadin in the anime, Akhenaden in the manga). We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"branded","kind":"archetype","name":"Branded","badge":{"es":"Un dragón caído del cielo, una vestal desterrada y una nación vuelta tragedia","en":"A dragon fallen from the sky, an exiled vestal and a nation turned into tragedy"},"origin":{"es":"Series 11 (The Fallen & The Virtuous): guías Valuable Book EX 2, 3 y 6","en":"Series 11 (The Fallen & The Virtuous): Valuable Book EX 2, 3 and 6 guides"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Una bondad que le costó el cargo","en":"A kindness that cost her office"},"p":{"es":"Ecclesia perdió su puesto por un gesto de compasión. Según las guías Valuable Book EX, se abrió un Hole (una grieta en el cielo) sobre Dogmatika y de él cayó un dragón, al que Fleurdelis abatió. En el cráter había un chico malherido, Albaz, y Ecclesia, entonces al frente de las Vestales Virtuosas, decidió cubrirlo. La nación lo tomó como una falta contra su doctrina: le quitó el cargo y mandó perseguir a los dos. La Tri-Brigade, un grupo antes hostil, los sacó de ahí, y así empezó el viaje que hicieron juntos.","en":"Ecclesia lost her post over an act of compassion. According to the Valuable Book EX guides, a Hole (a rift in the sky) opened over Dogmatika and a dragon dropped out of it, and Fleurdelis shot it down. In the crater lay a badly hurt boy, Albaz, and Ecclesia, then at the head of the Virtuous Vestals, chose to shield him. The nation took that as a transgression against its doctrine: it stripped her of the office and sent hunters after both. The Tri-Brigade, a formerly hostile group, pulled them out, and the journey they made together began there."},"cards":["Fallen of Albaz","Dogmatika Ecclesia, the Virtuous","Tri-Brigade Shuraig the Ominous Omen"]},{"h":{"es":"Maximus, Dramaturge y Aluber","en":"Maximus, Dramaturge and Aluber"},"p":{"es":"Maximus llevaba tiempo esperando el Día del Evangelio. Los stigmata (marcas sagradas) que había repartido entre su gente eran brands (sellos malditos) escondidos, y su ritual prohibido los despertó. Desde el Hole del cielo bajó una onda que alcanzó a civiles y soldados por igual y los volvió Despias, un pueblo condenado a representar un drama ajeno. Dogmatika se rompió y del subsuelo subió una mole con forma de castillo. Maximus absorbió la oscuridad y quedó convertido en Dramaturge. Un chico lo miraba todo como quien mira teatro, hasta que se volvió un dragón bufón y subió a escena: Aluber, enmascarado.","en":"Maximus had been waiting a long time for the Day of Gospel. The stigmata he handed out to his people were hidden brands, and his forbidden ritual woke them. A wave came down from the Hole in the sky, reached civilians and soldiers alike and turned them into Despias, a people condemned to perform someone else's drama. Dogmatika broke apart and a mass shaped like a castle rose from underground. Maximus took in the darkness and became Dramaturge. A boy watched it all the way one watches theater, until he became a jester dragon and stepped on stage: Aluber, wearing a mask."},"cards":["Dogmatika Maximus","Dramaturge of Despia","Aluber the Jester of Despia"]},{"h":{"es":"Un nombre nuevo en el Great Sand Sea","en":"A new name in the Great Sand Sea"},"p":{"es":"Los Springans recibieron a los fugitivos en el Great Sand Sea. Albaz ya no recordaba ni su nombre, de modo que Ecclesia le dio el que usa hoy, que significa blanco. Cuando la energía del ritual de Maximus llegó hasta el desierto, su gobernante enloqueció, y Albaz, atrapado en esa ola, se volvió el dragón Albion y arrasó con todo, aliados incluidos. Ecclesia caminó hacia él sin miedo, y al oír el nombre que ella le había puesto, Albaz volvió en sí. Fleurdelis les contó los crímenes de Maximus, y ellos supieron que los stigmata eran brands malditos y salieron a buscar cómo sellarlos.","en":"The Springans took the fugitives in at the Great Sand Sea. Albaz no longer remembered his own name, so Ecclesia gave him the one he uses today, which means white. When the energy of Maximus's ritual reached the desert, its ruler went mad, and Albaz, caught in that wave, became the dragon Albion and tore through everything, allies included. Ecclesia walked toward him unafraid, and upon hearing the name she had given him, Albaz came back to himself. Fleurdelis told them about Maximus's crimes, and they learned the stigmata were cursed brands, so they set off to find a way to seal them."},"cards":["Albion the Branded Dragon","Dogmatika Fleurdelis, the Knighted","Springans Kitt"]},{"h":{"es":"Sacred Summit: Mirrorjade, Lubellion y Alba-Lenatus","en":"Sacred Summit: Mirrorjade, Lubellion and Alba-Lenatus"},"p":{"es":"En el Sacred Summit, los Icejades lograron que los stigmata no se volvieran brands por un tiempo, pero llegaron los Despias y Longyuan traicionó a los Swordsoul. Aluber inmovilizó a Albaz, le sacó la capacidad de volverse dragón y la usó para transformarse en Lubellion, cuyas llamas quemaron a Chengying y a Kosmochlor. Con lo último que les quedaba, esos dos despertaron en Albaz el poder Swordsoul, y así nació Mirrorjade, un dragón de espadas que maneja hielo y fuego. Cuando Mirrorjade y Lubellion chocaron, sus fuerzas opuestas se unieron en una sola y apareció un dragón nuevo, Alba-Lenatus.","en":"At the Sacred Summit, the Icejades managed to keep the stigmata from becoming brands for a while, but the Despias arrived and Longyuan betrayed the Swordsoul. Aluber pinned Albaz down, took his ability to turn into a dragon and used it to become Lubellion, whose flames burned Chengying and Kosmochlor. With the last strength they had, those two awakened the Swordsoul power in Albaz, and Mirrorjade was born, a dragon of swords that wields ice and fire. When Mirrorjade and Lubellion collided, their opposing forces joined into one and a new dragon appeared, Alba-Lenatus."},"cards":["Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon","Lubellion the Searing Dragon","Alba-Lenatus the Abyss Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Cartesia y las llamas de Sanctifire","en":"Cartesia and the Sanctifire flames"},"p":{"es":"Cartesia, armada con 666 almas puras que el amor y la desesperanza habían quebrado, despertó dentro del teatro de Despia, y Dramaturge usó ese impulso para abrir Holes por todo el cielo. De ellos salieron dragones colosales del Abyss. Albaz volvió al Great Sand Sea, donde lo esperaba la Tri-Brigade para atacar el castillo. Después, Cartesia se interpuso en un disparo dirigido a Lubellion; Albaz la alcanzó, recuperó a Ecclesia y apareció Albion the Sanctifire Dragon, en llamas doradas. Una historia adicional de la VBEX 6 lo cuenta distinto: Ecclesia, cambiada por los Despias, se une a Albaz y ese dragón quema a los Despias.","en":"Cartesia, assembled from 666 pure souls that love and hopelessness had broken, awoke inside the Despia theater, and Dramaturge used that surge to open Holes across the sky. Colossal dragons of the Abyss poured out of them. Albaz returned to the Great Sand Sea, where the Tri-Brigade waited to attack the castle. Later, Cartesia stepped into a shot aimed at Lubellion; Albaz reached her, got Ecclesia back, and Albion the Sanctifire Dragon appeared in golden flames. A VBEX 6 side story tells it differently: Ecclesia, changed by the Despia, joins hands with Albaz and that dragon burns the Despia away."},"cards":["Blazing Cartesia, the Virtuous","Albion the Sanctifire Dragon","Despia, Theater of the Branded"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"[VBEX Lore] Number 1: Albaz & Ecclesia Part 1","url":"https://ygorganization.com/howtotameyourdragonboyfriend/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de la historia de Albaz y Ecclesia de la Valuable Book EX","en":"English translation of the Albaz and Ecclesia story from the Valuable Book EX"}},{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"Story 10: Branded Addendum Story [VBEX6]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-10-branded-addendum-story-vbex6/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción de las historias adicionales de Branded de la Valuable Book EX 6","en":"Translation of the Branded side stories from Valuable Book EX 6"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Branded","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Branded","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 2 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_2_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 3 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_3_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Todo sale de las guías oficiales Valuable Book EX (texto y arte de cartas), en la traducción no oficial de Yugipedia. Las guías 3 y 6 cuentan distinto el origen de Albion the Sanctifire Dragon, y acá se señalan ambas versiones. No cubre el anime THE CHRONICLES, que también tiene personajes de The Fallen & The Virtuous.","en":"Everything comes from the official Valuable Book EX guides (card text and art), in Yugipedia's unofficial translation. Guides 3 and 6 tell the origin of Albion the Sanctifire Dragon differently, and both versions are flagged here. It does not cover the THE CHRONICLES anime, which also features The Fallen & The Virtuous characters."}},{"slug":"dark-magician","kind":"archetype","name":"Dark Magician","badge":{"es":"El mago de Yugi: el espíritu de un sacerdote egipcio","en":"Yugi's magician: the spirit of an Egyptian priest"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga y anime) y el juego de cartas","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga and anime) and the card game"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Mahad, el sacerdote (anime)","en":"Mahad, the priest (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, Mahad es sacerdote de Atem, su amigo de la infancia, maestro de magia de Mana y portador del Millennium Ring. Cuando el Rey Ladrón Bakura ataca el palacio, Mahad lo enfrenta en una tumba. Herido de gravedad, sacrifica su vida y fusiona su ba con su ka, Illusion Magician, para crear al Dark Magician, y con una explosión deja a Bakura por muerto. Sigue sirviendo a Atem en esa forma, destruye al Diabound de Bakura en Kul Elna y cae junto a la Dark Magician Girl contra Zorc.","en":"In the anime, Mahad is Atem's priest, his childhood friend, Mana's magic teacher and the bearer of the Millennium Ring. When Thief King Bakura attacks the palace, Mahad confronts him in a tomb. Gravely wounded, he sacrifices his life and fuses his ba with his ka, Illusion Magician, to create the Dark Magician, and a blast leaves Bakura believed dead. He keeps serving Atem in that form, destroys Bakura's Diabound at Kul Elna and falls alongside Dark Magician Girl against Zorc."},"cards":["Dark Magician","Palladium Oracle Mahad"]},{"h":{"es":"Mahado y el Magus of Illusion (manga)","en":"Mahado and the Magus of Illusion (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga se llama Mahado y su ka es el Magus of Illusion. Gasta tanta magia en contener el mal del Millennium Ring que su ka parece débil, y Seto se lo reprocha. Decide enfrentar a Bakura solo, usándose como parte de una trampa en la tumba. Cuando el Diabound lo supera, deja que lo golpee una trampa de hachas y, al morir, fusiona su alma con el Magus: nace el Dark Magician, que aparece en la losa que sus soldados levantaron. Usa ataques como Black Magic y Afterworld Warp, que redirige golpes por portales.","en":"In the manga he is called Mahado and his ka is the Magus of Illusion. He spends so much magic holding back the evil of the Millennium Ring that his ka looks weak, and Seto criticizes him for it. He decides to face Bakura alone, using himself as part of a tomb trap. When Diabound overwhelms him, he lets a swinging axe trap hit him and, in death, fuses his soul with the Magus: the Dark Magician is born, appearing on the slab his soldiers erected. He uses attacks like Black Magic and Afterworld Warp, which redirects hits through portals."},"cards":["Dark Magician"]},{"h":{"es":"Mana y la Dark Magician Girl","en":"Mana and Dark Magician Girl"},"p":{"es":"Mana es la aprendiz de Mahad y amiga de infancia de Atem. Tras la muerte de su maestro jura convertirse en una gran maga y llega a invocar su propio ka, la Dark Magician Girl. En el anime ese ka cae junto a Mahad frente a Zorc. En el manga la Dark Magician Girl tiene piel morena, como Mana, y salva a Mahado de un ataque del Diabound en Kul Elna: como todavía no puede combatir, le cede su heka (energía mágica).","en":"Mana is Mahad's apprentice and a childhood friend of Atem. After her teacher's death she vows to become a great magician and eventually summons her own ka, Dark Magician Girl. In the anime that ka falls alongside Mahad against Zorc. In the manga Dark Magician Girl has tanned skin, like Mana, and saves Mahado from a Diabound attack at Kul Elna: since she can't fight yet, she gives him her heka (magical energy)."},"cards":["Dark Magician Girl","Palladium Oracle Mana"]},{"h":{"es":"Yugi y el espíritu de la carta","en":"Yugi and the spirit of the card"},"p":{"es":"El Dark Magician es la carta por la que más se conoce el mazo de Yugi. En el manga, Sugoroku Mutou le pasó una copia. En el anime, Yugi dice que le queda mejor al otro Yugi. En la película The Dark Side of Dimensions, Atem crea Palladium Oracle Mahad, y se muestra con mucha fuerza que el alma de Mahado está en esa carta, igual que en el Dark Magician.","en":"Dark Magician is the card Yugi's Decks are best known for. In the manga, Sugoroku Mutou passed a copy to Yugi. In the anime, Yugi says it suits the other Yugi better. In the film The Dark Side of Dimensions, Atem creates Palladium Oracle Mahad, and the film shows with great force that Mahado's soul lives in that card, as in Dark Magician."},"cards":["Dark Magician","Palladium Oracle Mahad"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Mahad","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Mahad","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Dark Magician (manga character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Dark_Magician_(manga_character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Dark Magician Girl (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Dark_Magician_Girl_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yugi Muto","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yugi_Muto","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Mahad (anime) y Mahado (manga) son el mismo personaje con detalles distintos; el ka es Illusion Magician en el anime y Magus of Illusion en el manga. El texto de la carta Dark Magician no trae lore propio. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"Mahad (anime) and Mahado (manga) are the same character with different details; the ka is Illusion Magician in the anime and Magus of Illusion in the manga. The Dark Magician card text carries no lore of its own. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"darklord","kind":"archetype","name":"Darklord","badge":{"es":"Ángeles caídos de tipo Hada, ligados al manga GX","en":"Fallen angels of the Fairy Type, tied to the GX manga"},"origin":{"es":"Cartas OCG/TCG, manga Yu-Gi-Oh! GX y manga OCG Structures","en":"OCG/TCG cards, the Yu-Gi-Oh! GX manga and the OCG Structures manga"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Ángeles caídos con nombre propio (cartas)","en":"Fallen angels by name (cards)"},"p":{"es":"En Japón el arquetipo se llama Datenshi, \"ángel caído\", y casi todos son monstruos DARK de Tipo Hada con efecto. Muchos se inspiran en figuras de la teología abrahámica: Desire viene de Mammon, Nasten de Mastema, Marie de María, y Morningstar, Eveningstar, The First y Nurse Reficule remiten a Lucifer. Superbia es \"soberbia\" en latín. La excepción de tipo es Marie, que es DARK pero Demonio. Hay otros basados en religiones paganas, como Ixchel, Nergal o Tezcatlipoca, y tres que salen del arte de cartas Forbidden y Solemn. La historia de la doncella que robó los tesoros de Dios y terminó como Darklord tiene su propia entrada, The Forbidden Maiden.","en":"In Japan the archetype is called Datenshi, \"fallen angel\", and almost all of them are DARK Fairy Effect Monsters. Many draw on figures from Abrahamic theology: Desire comes from Mammon, Nasten from Mastema, Marie from Mary, and Morningstar, Eveningstar, The First and Nurse Reficule point to Lucifer. Superbia is \"pride\" in Latin. The Type exception is Marie, who is DARK but a Fiend. Others are based on pagan religions, such as Ixchel, Nergal or Tezcatlipoca, and three come from the artwork of Forbidden and Solemn cards. The story of the maiden who stole God's treasures and ended up a Darklord has its own entry, The Forbidden Maiden."},"cards":["Darklord Nasten","Darklord Morningstar"]},{"h":{"es":"Del \"Fallen One\" a Darklord (TCG)","en":"From Fallen One to Darklord (TCG)"},"p":{"es":"Hay cartas del arquetipo desde 2001, pero no tuvo apoyo hasta 2016, con Booster SP: Destiny Soldiers en el OCG y Destiny Soldiers en el TCG. Muchos miembros tempranos del OCG salieron como promos de V Jump. En inglés, Marie y Nurse Reficule se llamaron al principio \"the Fallen One\", lo que sugiere que ese iba a ser el nombre del arquetipo. Desde Darklord Zerato en la versión TCG de Phantom Darkness, todo lo nuevo en inglés lleva Darklord, y las dos primeras se rebautizaron al reimprimirse en Destiny Soldiers.","en":"Cards of the archetype date back to 2001, but it got no support until 2016, when Destiny Soldiers arrived, as Booster SP in the OCG and a regular set in the TCG. Many early OCG members came out as V Jump promotional cards. In English, Marie and Nurse Reficule were first named \"the Fallen One\", which suggests that was meant to be the archetype's name. From Darklord Zerato onward (TCG Phantom Darkness), everything new in English carries Darklord, and the first two were renamed when reprinted in Destiny Soldiers."},"cards":["Darklord Marie","Darklord Nurse Reficule"]},{"h":{"es":"Midori Hibiki y Anna Des (manga)","en":"Midori Hibiki and Anna Des (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga de GX, Midori Hibiki, la hermana de Koyo, es la encargada de los alumnos de primer año de Slifer Red y usa un mazo Darklord. Su estilo es invocar monstruos de nivel alto con Cartas de Trampa, y avisa cada activación chasqueando los dedos. Entre sus cartas aparecen Asmodeus, Desire, Edeh Arae, Superbia y Fallen Angel in Darkness. Pierde contra Reggie MacKenzie en los capítulos 35 a 37, tras estar cerca de ganar. En el manga OCG Structures, Anna Des también arma un Darklord para un torneo por equipos con Shoma Yusa y Jukyu Goriki.","en":"In the GX manga, Midori Hibiki, Koyo's sister, runs the first-year Slifer Red students and plays a Darklord Deck. Her style is to Summon high-Level monsters through Trap Cards, and she marks each activation by snapping her fingers. Her cards include Asmodeus, Desire, Edeh Arae, Superbia and Fallen Angel in Darkness. She loses to Reggie MacKenzie in chapters 35 to 37, after coming close to winning. In the OCG Structures manga, Anna Des also builds a Darklord Deck for a team event with Shoma Yusa and Jukyu Goriki."},"cards":["Darklord Asmodeus","Darklord Edeh Arae","Fallen Angel in Darkness"]},{"h":{"es":"Tres monstruos de alto nivel (cartas)","en":"Three high-Level monsters (cards)"},"p":{"es":"Darklord Superbia, de Nivel 8, tiene un efecto que se dispara cuando entra por Invocación Especial desde el Cementerio: elige a otro monstruo Hada de ahí y lo Invoca de Modo Especial. Darklord Desire, de Nivel 10 y 3000 ATK, no se puede Invocar de Modo Especial; se Invoca por Tributo sacrificando a un Hada, y una vez por turno pierde 1000 ATK para mandar al Cementerio a un monstruo rival. Darklord Zerato se Invoca por Tributo con un monstruo DARK si hay 4 o más DARK de nombres distintos en tu Cementerio.","en":"Darklord Superbia, a Level 8, has a trigger effect for when it comes back by Special Summon out of the Graveyard: it picks a different Fairy monster in that pile and Special Summons it. Darklord Desire, a Level 10 with 3000 ATK, cannot be Special Summoned; it is Tribute Summoned by Tributing a Fairy, and once per turn it loses 1000 ATK to send an opponent's monster to the Graveyard. Darklord Zerato is Tribute Summoned with a DARK monster once your Graveyard holds 4 or more DARK monsters, each under a different name."},"cards":["Darklord Superbia","Darklord Desire","Darklord Zerato"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Midori Hibiki","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Midori_Hibiki","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Anna Des","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Anna_Des","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord Superbia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord_Superbia","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord Desire","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord_Desire","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord Zerato","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord_Zerato","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord Morningstar","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord_Morningstar","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord Marie","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord_Marie","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los bloques de cartas describen texto y datos reales de cartas; Midori Hibiki y Anna Des son del manga. La historia de la doncella que termina como Condemned Darklord está en la entrada The Forbidden Maiden. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The card blocks describe real card text and card data; Midori Hibiki and Anna Des are from manga. The story of the maiden who ends up as Condemned Darklord is in the Forbidden Maiden entry. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"dream-mirror","kind":"archetype","name":"Dream Mirror","badge":{"es":"Espejos que arrastran a los humanos a los sueños de Oneiros","en":"Mirrors that pull humans into Oneiros' dreams"},"origin":{"es":"Historias de las cartas: Valuable Book EX y Master Duel","en":"Card storylines: Valuable Book EX and Master Duel"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Los espejos de Oneiros","en":"Oneiros' mirrors"},"p":{"es":"Según la historia de las cartas, Oneiros atrae a los humanos con espejos especiales hacia dos mundos: el de los sueños de buen augurio, de luz deslumbrante, y el de las pesadillas, de oscuridad repulsiva. A través de esos espejos pretende dominar los sueños. Quien los trae al mundo real es Neiroy, su enviado, y los espejos tienen significados especiales: una vez en la realidad, llevan a los humanos al mundo de Dream Mirror.","en":"According to the card storyline, Oneiros lures humans with special mirrors into two worlds: that of auspicious dreams, of dazzling light, and that of nightmares, of repulsive darkness. Through those mirrors he plans to dominate the dreams. The one who brings them into the real world is Neiroy, his envoy, and the mirrors carry special meanings: once in reality, they lead humans into the world of Dream Mirror."},"cards":["Dream Mirror of Joy","Neiroy, the Dream Mirror Disciple","Dream Mirror of Terror"]},{"h":{"es":"Cada espejo, un sueño distinto","en":"Each mirror, a different dream"},"p":{"es":"Lo que pasa adentro depende del espejo que se visite. Según el mundo de Dream Mirror al que entran, el aspecto de las personas cambia y viven historias fantásticas dentro de los sueños. En las cartas, esos dos lados aparecen con Ikelos en sus dos formas, la Sprite y la Mara, y con Dream Mirror Oneiromancy. Ya nadie entra como era: los cambios de aspecto son parte de lo que se experimenta en el sueño.","en":"What happens inside depends on the mirror visited. Depending on the Dream Mirror world they enter, people's appearances change and they live fantastic stories inside the dreams. In the cards, those two sides appear with Ikelos in both of its forms, the Sprite and the Mara, and with Dream Mirror Oneiromancy. No one enters as they were: the change of appearance is part of what is experienced in the dream."},"cards":["Ikelos, the Dream Mirror Sprite","Dream Mirror Oneiromancy","Ikelos, the Dream Mirror Mara"]},{"h":{"es":"Oneiros, el soberano de los sueños","en":"Oneiros, ruler of dreams"},"p":{"es":"Detrás de los espejos está Oneiros, el soberano de los sueños. Aumenta su poder según los sueños que tienen los humanos, y así consolida su dominio sobre ellos. Quienes visitan el mundo de Dream Mirror todas las noches terminan hechizados por él. Mientras el espejo que se llevó a la realidad no se rompa, no se despiertan nunca más, o eso se dice. Las cartas de Oneiros lo muestran en dos formas: Erlking y Tormentor.","en":"Behind the mirrors is Oneiros, ruler of dreams. He amplifies his power according to the dreams humans have, which strengthens his rule over them. Those who visit the world of Dream Mirror every night end up charmed by it. As long as the mirror brought into reality is not broken, they will never wake again, or so it is said. Oneiros' cards show him in two forms: Erlking and Tormentor."},"cards":["Oneiros, the Dream Mirror Erlking","Dream Mirror Phantasms","Oneiros, the Dream Mirror Tormentor"]},{"h":{"es":"¿Sueño o realidad?","en":"Dream or reality?"},"p":{"es":"La escena que cierra el relato muestra a una chica atraída hacia el espejo que cuenta su sueño de la noche anterior. Por pura casualidad, un chico tuvo el mismo sueño, y según parece también el perro. La sección termina con la pregunta de si fue un sueño o fue real, y deja abierta cuál será la conclusión. Las cartas que acompañan la escena son Dream Mirror Recap, Phantasos, el Amigo, y Morpheus, el Caballero Blanco.","en":"The scene that closes the story shows a girl lured into the mirror telling of her dream from the night before. Purely by chance, a boy had that very dream as well, and the pet dog seems to have too. The section ends on the question of whether it was a dream or real, and leaves the conclusion open. The cards that accompany the scene are Dream Mirror Recap, Phantasos the Friend and Morpheus the White Knight."},"cards":["Dream Mirror Recap","Phantasos, the Dream Mirror Friend","Morpheus, the Dream Mirror White Knight"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: la adivina del callejón","en":"Master Duel: the fortune teller in the alley"},"p":{"es":"La versión de Master Duel arranca en un callejón escondido de un pueblo, donde una persona camina como en trance. Una adivina la llama y le dice que quienes pasan por ese pueblo están perdidos en un sueño. Le pregunta qué ve al soñar, y la persona lo cuenta todo. Entonces la adivina explica que hay sueños de buen augurio y de mal augurio, y que quizá un solo ser los domina a todos. Ese ser parece ángel en los buenos y demonio en los malos.","en":"The Master Duel version opens in a hidden alley of a town, where a person walks as if in a trance. A fortune teller calls out to them and says that everyone who visits the town is lost in a dream. She asks what they see when they dream, and the person tells everything. The fortune teller then explains that there are good-omen and bad-omen dreams, and that perhaps a single being dominates them all. That being looks like an angel in good dreams and a demon in bad ones."},"cards":["Oneiros, the Dream Mirror Erlking","Oneiros, the Dream Mirror Tormentor"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: el sol y la luna","en":"Master Duel: the sun and the moon"},"p":{"es":"Según la adivina, los discípulos del soberano aparecen en el mundo real y dejan un espejo misterioso junto a la cama del soñador. Los motivos de sol y luna grabados en el espejo deciden el sueño: si el sol está arriba, llega un buen presagio; si la luna, una pesadilla. El mundo del sol es luminoso, con bestias sagradas y caballeros valientes. El de la luna es oscuro y sin esperanza, con bestias demoníacas y segadores sin piedad.","en":"According to the fortune teller, the ruler's disciples show up in waking life and set a strange mirror beside the dreamer's bed. Sun and moon carvings on its surface determine which dream follows: if the sun is above, a good omen arrives; if the moon is, a nightmare. The sun world is bright, with holy beasts and gallant knights. The moon world is dark and hopeless, with demonic beasts and merciless reapers."},"cards":["Dream Mirror Oneiromancy","Morpheus, the Dream Mirror White Knight","Morpheus, the Dream Mirror Black Knight"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: los niños que despertaron","en":"Master Duel: the children who woke"},"p":{"es":"El soberano maneja ambos mundos y gana poder con la gente que atrae, y se dice que quien ya no distingue sueño de realidad nunca despierta. La persona se asusta, pero la adivina la tranquiliza: el relato de los dos mundos se transmite hace generaciones y mucha gente los visita. Entre los relatos, el mejor es el de un grupo de niños que no quedó atrapado, despertó y contó con alegría sus aventuras. Su consejo es confiar en uno mismo, la mayor fuerza frente al soberano.","en":"The ruler handles both worlds and gains power from the people he draws in, and it is said that whoever can no longer tell dream from reality never wakes. The person is frightened, but the fortune teller calms them: the tale of the two worlds has been passed down for generations and many people visit them. Among the accounts, the best is that of a group of children who were not trapped, woke up and joyfully told of their adventures. Her advice is to have faith in oneself, the greatest strength against the ruler."},"cards":["Dream Mirror Phantasms","Dream Mirror Recap"]},{"h":{"es":"Los dos lados en las cartas (diseño)","en":"The two sides in the cards (design)"},"p":{"es":"Fuera del relato, la wiki explica el diseño. Los monstruos que se corresponden con Dream Mirror of Joy son LIGHT, y los de Dream Mirror of Terror son DARK. Cada uno tiene su pareja: Morpheus Caballero Blanco y Caballero Negro, Phantasos Amigo y Enemigo, Neiroy Discípulo y Traidor. Los nombres vienen de figuras grecorromanas del sueño. El arquetipo se inspira en las puertas de cuerno y de marfil, que separan los sueños verdaderos de los engañosos.","en":"Outside the story, the wiki explains the design. Joy-side monsters are LIGHT, and their Terror-side counterparts are DARK. Each has its counterpart: Morpheus the White and Black Knight, Phantasos the Friend and the Foe, Neiroy the Disciple and the Traitor. The names come from Greco-Roman figures of sleep. Its inspiration is the Greek image of the gates of horn and ivory, used to tell true dreams from deceptive ones."},"cards":["Neiroy, the Dream Mirror Traitor","Phantasos, the Dream Mirror Foe"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"[VBEX] Number 3: Dream Mirrors","url":"https://ygorganization.com/vbex-number-3-dream-mirrors/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de esta historia de la Valuable Book EX, para leerla completa","en":"English translation of this Valuable Book EX story, to read it in full"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Dream Mirror","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Dream_Mirror","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Duel card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Duel_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los primeros cuatro bloques son la historia de la Valuable Book EX y los tres siguientes la versión de Master Duel; el último es diseño de las cartas, no del relato. La wiki no dice quién es la chica, el chico ni el perro. La versión de Master Duel termina con un consejo de la adivina y no resuelve la pregunta de la primera.","en":"The first four blocks are the Valuable Book EX story and the next three the Master Duel version; the last is card design, not part of the story. The wiki does not say who the girl, the boy or the dog are. The Master Duel version ends with the fortune teller's advice and does not settle the first story's question."}},{"slug":"egyptian-gods","kind":"archetype","name":"Egyptian Gods","badge":{"es":"Las tres bestias divinas de Pegasus, ligadas al Faraón","en":"Pegasus's three divine beasts, tied to the Pharaoh"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga y anime), arco de Battle City y recuerdos del Faraón","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga and anime), Battle City arc and the Pharaoh's memories"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Tres bestias en una tablilla","en":"Three beasts on a tablet"},"p":{"es":"Las cartas se inspiran en tres bestias divinas talladas alrededor del Millennium Puzzle, en la Tablet of Lost Memories. Sus nombres salen de la mitología egipcia: Osiris en el original japonés de Slifer, el monumento en el caso de Obelisk y el dios del sol en el de Ra. Ishizu Ishtar cuenta que representan polaridades del universo, mientras que el Faraón las llama por sus títulos. El nombre Slifer es un guiño a Roger Slifer, productor de la versión en inglés del anime. En el manga en inglés suelen llamarlas simplemente Dios.","en":"The cards are modeled on three divine beasts that appear around the Millennium Puzzle in the Tablet of Lost Memories. Their names come from Egyptian myth: Osiris in Slifer's original Japanese name, the monument for Obelisk and the sun god for Ra. Ishizu Ishtar says they stand for polarities of the universe, while the Pharaoh refers to them by their titles. The name Slifer is a wink at Roger Slifer, producer of the English version of the anime. In the English manga they are often just called God."},"cards":["Slifer the Sky Dragon","Obelisk the Tormentor","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"Pegasus las crea y las entierra (anime)","en":"Pegasus makes and buries them (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, Maximillion Pegasus diseña las cartas de los tres dioses para Duel Monsters, pero las almas de las bestias pasan a habitar las cartas y las vuelven armas poderosas. Slifer ataca al camarógrafo que cubría el hallazgo y Obelisk al fotógrafo que estaba con Pegasus. Él terminó viendo su creación como uno de sus mayores errores. No se animó a destruirlas, así que pidió al consejo supremo de antigüedades egipcio que las enterrara en distintos puntos del Valle de los Reyes.","en":"In the anime, Maximillion Pegasus designs the cards of the three gods for Duel Monsters, but the beasts' souls move into the cards and turn them into powerful weapons. Slifer lashes out at the cameraman who covered the find and Obelisk at the photographer who stood beside Pegasus. He came to see their creation as one of his biggest mistakes. He could not bring himself to destroy them, so he asked Egypt's supreme council of antiquities to bury them at separate spots in the Valley of the Kings."},"cards":["Slifer the Sky Dragon","Obelisk the Tormentor"]},{"h":{"es":"Otra versión (anime): Shadi y la tablilla","en":"Another account (anime): Shadi and the tablet"},"p":{"es":"Otra página del anime cuenta el origen de otro modo. En un segundo viaje a Egipto, Shadi lleva a Pegasus a una ciudad subterránea, a una cámara con una tablilla donde están tallados los tres dioses. Pegasus vuelve a América y basa las cartas en esa imagen. Quienes trabajaban con él mueren (en el doblaje, desaparecen), pero sigue pintándolas solo. Sueña con los dioses destruyendo una ciudad, y Shadi le advierte que debe devolverlas a su lugar de reposo. Ishizu las entierra entonces en la tumba del Faraón. La wiki no concilia esto con el Valle de los Reyes del bloque anterior.","en":"Another anime page tells the origin differently. On a second trip to Egypt, Shadi takes Pegasus to an underground city, into a chamber with a tablet that carries carvings of the three gods. Pegasus returns to America and bases the cards on that image. The people working with him die (they just disappear in the dub), yet he keeps painting them alone. He dreams of the gods wrecking a city, and Shadi warns him to return them to their resting place. Ishizu then buries them in the Pharaoh's tomb. The wiki does not reconcile this with the Valley of the Kings in the previous block."},"cards":["The Winged Dragon of Ra","Obelisk the Tormentor"]},{"h":{"es":"Quién tuvo cada dios en Battle City","en":"Who held each god in Battle City"},"p":{"es":"Marik, líder de los Rare Hunters, consigue a Slifer y a Ra con el poder del Millennium Rod, pero Ishizu protege a Obelisk y se lo entrega a Kaiba para que organice Battle City. Yami Yugi gana a Slifer cuando Marik se queda sin cartas en el mazo, y más tarde Obelisk pasa a él porque pierde Kaiba. Ra lo consigue al vencer a Yami Marik. Una copia falsa de Ra, usada por Odion, terminó golpeando con un rayo a los dos duelistas.","en":"Marik, leader of the Rare Hunters, gets Slifer and Ra thanks to the Millennium Rod, yet Ishizu protects Obelisk and hands it to Kaiba so he will host Battle City. Yami Yugi wins Slifer when Marik runs out of cards in his Deck, and Obelisk later moves to him because Kaiba loses the Duel. He gets Ra by beating Yami Marik. A counterfeit Ra, played by Odion, ended up striking both Duelists down with lightning."},"cards":["Slifer the Sky Dragon","Obelisk the Tormentor","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"Jerarquía en el manga, debilidades en el anime","en":"Hierarchy in the manga, weaknesses in the anime"},"p":{"es":"En el manga los tres dioses tienen una Jerarquía: Ra queda arriba, Slifer y Obelisk abajo como iguales, y el de mayor rango no recibe daño de batalla de uno inferior. También resisten Trampas y Cartas Virus, y Divine Evolution sube su rango: en Yu-Gi-Oh! R lo usa Obelisk para igualar la Jerarquía de The Wicked Avatar. El anime elimina la Jerarquía: Slifer y Obelisk sí pueden dañar a Ra, y Pyramid of Light los desterró en la película. Además, solo duelistas ligados al pasado egipcio pueden controlarlos.","en":"In the manga the three gods have a Hierarchy: Ra sits on top, Slifer and Obelisk below as equals, and the higher rank takes no battle damage from a lower one. They also resist Trap Cards and Virus Cards, and Divine Evolution raises a god's rank: in Yu-Gi-Oh! R, Obelisk uses it to match the Hierarchy of The Wicked Avatar. The anime drops Hierarchy: Slifer and Obelisk can hurt Ra, and Pyramid of Light banished them in the movie. Also, only Duelists linked to the Egyptian past can control them."},"cards":["Divine Evolution","Pyramid of Light","The Wicked Avatar"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Egyptian God","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Egyptian_God","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Slifer the Sky Dragon (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Slifer_the_Sky_Dragon_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Obelisk the Tormentor (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Obelisk_the_Tormentor_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Winged Dragon of Ra (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Winged_Dragon_of_Ra_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Maximillion Pegasus","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Maximillion_Pegasus","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Todo esto es lore de la serie. Los textos de las cartas reales no cuentan nada de esta historia: son los efectos del juego. La Jerarquía es del manga y el anime la elimina. Los bloques sobre Pegasus salen de páginas del anime, y esas páginas no coinciden del todo entre sí (Valle de los Reyes en unas, tumba del Faraón en otra). En lo que leímos no hay un relato del manga sobre cómo se crearon las cartas. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido sobre este lore que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"All of this is series lore. The real card texts do not tell this story: they are game effects. Hierarchy belongs to the manga and the anime removes it. The Pegasus blocks come from anime pages, and those pages do not fully agree with each other (Valley of the Kings in some, the Pharaoh's tomb in another). In what we read there is no manga account of how the cards were made. We did not find a content-creator piece on this lore that could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"eldlich","kind":"archetype","name":"Eldlich","badge":{"es":"De una piedra alquímica a un rey inmortal que quiere el mundo","en":"From an alchemists' stone to an immortal king who wants the world"},"origin":{"es":"Historias oficiales de las cartas (Master Guide y Master Duel)","en":"Official card storylines (Master Guide and Master Duel)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Los alquimistas y la piedra","en":"The alchemists and the stone"},"p":{"es":"Alquimistas famosos de varias tierras se reúnen en una isla desierta para estudiar la Piedra Filosofal, la cima de sus ambiciones. Sacrifican primero ganado y luego animales salvajes, y arman lo que creen que es el núcleo de la piedra, pero el avance se frena. Entonces el mar deja en la orilla un cadáver humano. Tras ofrecerlo, la piedra late débilmente, aunque el cuerpo aún respiraba. Siguen con esclavos y criminales hasta lograr el Eldlixir oscuro de la carta Eldlixir of Black Awakening.","en":"Famed alchemists from several lands gather on a deserted island to study the Philosopher's Stone, the peak of their ambitions. They sacrifice livestock first and wild animals later, and build what they believe is the stone's core, yet progress stalls. Then the sea leaves a human corpse on the shore. Once it is offered, the stone pulses faintly, although the body still breathed. They carry on with slaves and criminals until they obtain the dark Eldlixir of the card Eldlixir of Black Awakening."},"cards":["Eldlixir of Black Awakening"]},{"h":{"es":"La piedra despierta y nace la leyenda","en":"The stone wakes and the legend is born"},"p":{"es":"El Eldlixir devora esclavos, plebeyos y nobles, y emite una luz blanca cegadora. Al absorber la esencia de tanta vida se tiñe de carmesí y despierta como Eldlixir of Scarlet Sanguine. Sus maldiciones nacen del deseo de vida, riqueza y poder. Convierte lo que lo rodea en oro para atraer más ofrendas, y es Cursed Eldland. Entre los marineros corre el rumor de una isla dorada. Los buscadores de tesoros llegan y sus cuerpos no se pudren: se vuelven muertos vivientes.","en":"The Eldlixir consumes slaves, commoners and nobles, and gives off a blinding white light. Having absorbed the essence of so many lives, it turns deep crimson and awakens as Eldlixir of Scarlet Sanguine. Its curses grow out of the wish for life, wealth and might. It turns its surroundings to gold to draw more offerings, which is Cursed Eldland. Sailors begin whispering about a golden island. Treasure seekers arrive and their bodies do not rot: they become the undead."},"cards":["Eldlixir of Scarlet Sanguine","Cursed Eldland"]},{"h":{"es":"El mercenario que llega al castillo","en":"The mercenary who reaches the castle"},"p":{"es":"Con los años la isla pasa a ser la Ciudad sin Retorno. Unos eruditos de un reino lejano llegan a investigarla con mercenarios de escolta. Uno de ellos es callado y muy fuerte, con una voluntad firme en la mirada. Pelea contra las bestias y los condenados, entre ellos los de Guardian of the Golden Land y Conquistador of the Golden Land. Al llegar al portón del castillo no queda nadie detrás. Ya sin empleadores, entra igual y, en el sótano, toca una piedra roja flotando en el aire.","en":"As the years pass, the island becomes the City of No Return. Scholars from a far-off kingdom arrive to investigate, escorted by mercenaries. One of them is quiet and very strong, with a firm will in his eyes. He fights the beasts and the cursed dead, among them those shown on Guardian of the Golden Land and Conquistador of the Golden Land. At the castle gates nobody is left behind him. With no employers left, he goes in anyway and, in the basement, touches a red stone floating in the air."},"cards":["Guardian of the Golden Land","Conquistador of the Golden Land"]},{"h":{"es":"Nace el Golden Lord (Master Duel)","en":"The Golden Lord is born (Master Duel)"},"p":{"es":"Siguiendo el relato de Master Duel: al tocar la piedra, el mercenario oye los gritos de miles de almas. Unas no quieren morir, otras odian a todos los humanos, otras solo ven oro. Su espíritu no se quiebra: libera la ambición enorme que guardaba y se traga esos deseos. Ese día nace Eldlich the Golden Lord, que se sienta en el trono como si fuera suyo, en Golden Land Forever! Quiere más guerras y más vida, y el Eldlixir brilla en respuesta. Con todo el poder oscuro de Eldland en él, se vuelve un rey demonio enloquecido: Seven Cities of the Golden Land.","en":"Following the Master Duel account: on touching the stone, the mercenary hears the screams of thousands of souls. Some do not want to die, some hate every human, some see only gold. His spirit does not break: he releases the huge greed he had kept hidden and swallows those desires. That day Eldlich the Golden Lord is born, and he sits on the throne as if it were his, in Golden Land Forever! He wants more wars and more life, and the Eldlixir shines in answer. With all of Eldland's dark power in him, he becomes a mad demon king: Seven Cities of the Golden Land."},"cards":["Eldlich the Golden Lord","Golden Land Forever!","Seven Cities of the Golden Land"]},{"h":{"es":"La misma leyenda según The Valuable Book EX, n.º 5","en":"The same legend in The Valuable Book EX, no. 5"},"p":{"es":"Otra versión oficial, el n.º 5 del primer The Valuable Book EX, cuenta el origen distinto. Unos sabios codiciosos ofrecen miles de almas a la piedra hasta que despierta, brilla en carmesí y vuelve dorada la tierra, mientras todo ser vivo se convierte en muerto viviente. Eldlixir of White Destiny es una de las tres cartas Eldlixir del relato. Cazatesoros como Huaquero of the Golden Land, ejércitos llegados por mar y las bestias del lugar quedan convertidos en oro eterno. Un hombre de voluntad inhumana se apodera de la piedra y es Eldlich. Con un ritual enfoca la maldición en sí y parte a conquistar el mundo.","en":"Another official version, no. 5 of the first volume of The Valuable Book EX, tells the origin differently. Greedy sages offer thousands of souls to the stone until it awakens, shines crimson and makes the land golden, while every living thing turns undead. Eldlixir of White Destiny is one of the story's three Eldlixir cards. Treasure hunters such as Huaquero of the Golden Land, armies arriving by sea and the local beasts end up as eternal gold. A man of inhuman will seizes the stone and is Eldlich. Through a ritual he focuses the curse on himself and sets out to conquer the world."},"cards":["Eldlixir of White Destiny","Huaquero of the Golden Land","Eldlich the Golden Lord"]},{"h":{"es":"La invasión (The Valuable Book EX 5, n.º 9)","en":"The invasion (The Valuable Book EX 5, no. 9)"},"p":{"es":"Según The Valuable Book EX 5, el Eldlixir convierte toda la materia en oro y a los vivos en muertos vivientes, y de Eldland nadie volvió. Su primer rey eterno venció esa maldición con su propia codicia. Para invadir el exterior, Eldlich forja soldados dorados con Pot of Extravagance, una olla de transmutación hecha de deseo. Su arma definitiva es Fallen Angel of the Golden Land, que baja al campo de batalla y arrasa ciudades. Cuanto más conquista, más crece su ambición, y el Eldlixir of the Glorious Golden Land vuelve a brillar en carmesí: la invasión empieza otra vez.","en":"According to The Valuable Book EX 5, the Eldlixir makes everything material gold and every living being undead, and no one came back from Eldland. Its first, eternal king overcame that curse with his own greed. To invade the outside, Eldlich forges golden soldiers with Pot of Extravagance, a transmutation pot made of desire. His ultimate weapon is Fallen Angel of the Golden Land, which descends on the battlefield and razes cities. The more he conquers, the more his ambition grows, and the Eldlixir of the Glorious Golden Land glows crimson again: the invasion begins once more."},"cards":["Pot of Extravagance","Fallen Angel of the Golden Land","Eldlixir of the Glorious Golden Land"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"[VBEX Lore] Number 5: Eldlich","url":"https://ygorganization.com/bothbothisgood/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Relato original en inglés con la galería de ilustraciones de cada carta.","en":"Original story in English, with the illustration gallery of every card."}},{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"Story 09: The Eldlich Invasion [VBEX5]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-09-the-eldlich-invasion-vbex5/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Relato original en inglés de la invasión, con las ilustraciones de sus cartas.","en":"Original English story of the invasion, with the illustrations of its cards."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Eldlich","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Eldlich","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Duel card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Duel_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Cada bloque sigue una versión oficial y lo dice en el texto. Los bloques 1 a 4 son el relato de Master Duel: alquimistas, mercenario y Golden Lord. El bloque 5 es el n.º 5 de The Valuable Book EX (primer volumen), que cuenta el origen de otra forma (sabios y un hombre de voluntad inhumana), y el bloque 6 es The Valuable Book EX 5, número 9, sobre la invasión. Los enlaces del creador cubren solo los bloques 5 y 6, el n.º 5 de The Valuable Book EX y el n.º 9 de The Valuable Book EX 5. Los efectos de las cartas son aparte: acá solo se cuenta el relato. El nombre Eldlich combina Eldritch, lich y El Dorado.","en":"Each block follows one official version and says so in the text. Blocks 1 to 4 are the Master Duel story: alchemists, mercenary and the Golden Lord. Block 5 is no. 5 of The Valuable Book EX (first volume), which tells the origin another way (sages and a man of inhuman will), and block 6 is The Valuable Book EX 5, number 9, about the invasion. The creator links cover only blocks 5 and 6, no. 5 of The Valuable Book EX and no. 9 of The Valuable Book EX 5. Card effects are a different matter: only the story is told here. The name Eldlich combines Eldritch, lich and El Dorado."}},{"slug":"elemental-hero","kind":"archetype","name":"Elemental HERO","badge":{"es":"Superhéroes de cómic que se fusionan: el mazo de Jaden Yuki en GX","en":"Comic-book heroes that fuse together: Jaden Yuki's deck in GX"},"origin":{"es":"Anime y manga de Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (diseño de Kazuki Takahashi)","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX anime and manga (designed by Kazuki Takahashi)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Superhéroes hechos de naturaleza","en":"Superheroes made of nature"},"p":{"es":"Kazuki Takahashi creó a los Elemental HERO, y de dónde salen depende del medio. El anime los arma como superhéroes de cómic occidental, mientras que el manga de GX parte de elementos naturales. De cualquier forma, cada héroe encarna una faceta del mundo natural que va más allá de fuego, agua y tierra: Wildheart, por ejemplo, encarna lo salvaje y sin domar. Cuando se fusionan varios, el resultado suele reunir las facetas de sus ingredientes. En su mayoría son Guerreros, y los mazos se apoyan fuerte en la Invocación por Fusión.","en":"Kazuki Takahashi created the Elemental HERO, and where they come from depends on the medium. The anime builds them as western-comic superheroes, while the GX manga starts from natural elements. Either way each hero embodies a facet of the natural world that reaches past plain fire, water and earth; Wildheart, for instance, embodies untamed wilderness. When several are fused, the result tends to merge the facets of its ingredients. Most are Warriors, and the decks lean hard on Fusion Summoning."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Wildheart","Elemental HERO Clayman"]},{"h":{"es":"Jaden, Aster y la lógica de la Fusión","en":"Jaden, Aster and the logic of Fusion"},"p":{"es":"Jaden Yuki lleva el arquetipo en el anime, y todo su enfoque se apoya en una idea: un héroe solo rinde poco, dos juntos ya son otra cosa. Avian y Burstinatrix se fusionan en Flame Wingman, a quien nombra su carta favorita. Con ese monstruo y Skyscraper venció al Dr. Crowler en el duelo del examen de ingreso a Duel Academy. Aster Phoenix también jugó Elemental HERO antes de pasarse a Destiny HERO. El manga reparte el mazo en dos manos: la de Jaden y la de su mentor, Koyo Hibiki.","en":"Jaden Yuki carries the archetype in the anime, and his whole approach rests on one idea: a hero alone is modest, two together are not. Avian and Burstinatrix fuse into Flame Wingman, who he names as his favorite card. He used that monster plus Skyscraper to beat Dr. Crowler in the Duel Academy entrance exam duel. Aster Phoenix ran Elemental HERO as well before moving on to Destiny HERO. The manga puts the deck in two hands: Jaden's and that of his mentor, Koyo Hibiki."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Flame Wingman","Elemental HERO Avian","Elemental HERO Burstinatrix"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Neo-Spacians y la carta insignia","en":"The Neo-Spacians and the signature card"},"p":{"es":"Según el anime, Jaden inventó a los Neo-Spacians de chico: mandó diseños a un concurso de KaibaCorp, ganó, y las cartas se lanzaron al espacio para absorber energía del espacio. Más adelante la Luz de la Destrucción de Sartorius le quitó la capacidad de leer el rostro de sus cartas, y la recuperó en Neo Space al conseguir a sus Neo-Spacians, lo que trajo un nuevo monstruo insignia. Es Elemental HERO Neos, cuyo texto dice que llegó desde el Neo-Space y libera poderes desconocidos al hacer Fusión por Contacto con un Neo-Spacian, como Grand Mole. Son seis monstruos de Nivel 3, cada uno con Atributo y Tipo propios.","en":"In the anime, Jaden invented the Neo-Spacians as a kid: he sent designs to a KaibaCorp contest, won, and the cards were shot into space to soak up energy from space. Later Sartorius's Light of Destruction cost him the ability to read his cards' faces, and he regained it in Neo Space after getting his Neo-Spacians, which brought a new signature monster. That is Elemental HERO Neos, whose card text says he came from Neo-Space and unleashes unknown powers when he Contact Fuses with a Neo-Spacian, such as Grand Mole. They are six Level 3 monsters, each with its own Attribute and Type."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Neos","Neo-Spacian Grand Mole"]},{"h":{"es":"La oscuridad de la tercera temporada","en":"The darkness of season 3"},"p":{"es":"La tercera temporada es el giro oscuro. En el Mundo Dimensional, Brron sacrifica a los amigos de Jaden para crear Super Polymerization, y el Rey Supremo, un ancestro de quien Jaden es la reencarnación, toma el control de él. Bajo esa influencia juega Evil HERO: versiones Demonio de sus héroes, como Evil HERO Inferno Wing en lugar de Flame Wingman, salidas por Dark Fusion. Cuando el Eye of Orichalcum lo libera, la culpa lo lleva a evitar la Fusión por completo. El arco cierra cuando usa Super Polymerization para unir su alma con la de Yubel.","en":"Season 3 is the dark turn. In the Dimension World, Brron sacrifices Jaden's friends to produce Super Polymerization, and the Supreme King, an ancestor of whom Jaden is the reincarnation, takes control of him. Under that influence he plays Evil HERO: Fiend versions of his heroes, like Evil HERO Inferno Wing standing in for Flame Wingman, brought out by Dark Fusion. Once the Eye of Orichalcum frees him, guilt makes him avoid Fusion altogether. The arc closes when he uses Super Polymerization to join his soul with Yubel's."},"cards":["Evil HERO Inferno Wing","Super Polymerization","Yubel"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Elemental HERO","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Elemental_HERO","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Jaden Yuki","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Jaden_Yuki","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Neo-Spacian","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Neo-Spacian","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Elemental HERO Neos (card)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Elemental_HERO_Neos","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia de Neo-Spacians, Neos y el Rey Supremo es del anime de GX. Que Neos llegue del Neo-Space es texto de la carta. El manga usa otra versión de los héroes. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The Neo-Spacian, Neos and Supreme King story is from the GX anime. Neos arriving from Neo-Space is card text. The manga uses a different take on the heroes. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"exodia","kind":"archetype","name":"Exodia","badge":{"es":"Cinco piezas selladas que ganan el duelo si juntás todas","en":"Five sealed pieces that win the Duel if you gather them all"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga y anime) y el juego de cartas","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga and anime) and the card game"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Cinco piezas, una victoria","en":"Five pieces, one victory"},"p":{"es":"Exodia the Forbidden One se compone de cinco cartas, cada una una parte de su cuerpo: la cabeza y cuatro miembros. Según la wiki, era una bestia tan poderosa que la partieron y encadenaron en cinco sellos, para que su poder no volviera a usarse. En el juego, si juntás las cinco piezas en la mano ganás el duelo sin importar la situación. Su efecto no depende del ataque ni de estar en el campo, y por eso es de los monstruos más inusuales de Duel Monsters.","en":"Exodia the Forbidden One is made of five cards, each a body part: the head and four limbs. According to the wiki, it was a beast so mighty that it was split up and chained inside five seals so its power could never be used again. In the game, gathering all five pieces in your hand wins the Duel regardless of the situation. Its effect does not rely on ATK or on being on the field, so it counts among the strangest monsters of Duel Monsters."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One","Right Leg of the Forbidden One","Left Arm of the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"El as de Yugi contra Kaiba (anime)","en":"Yugi's ace against Kaiba (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el episodio 1, Yami Yugi se enfrenta a Kaiba. Yugi arma las cinco piezas, y Exodia aparece y lanza un ataque que elimina a todos los Blue-Eyes White Dragon de Kaiba a la vez. Según Yugi, las cartas eran un experimento de los creadores del juego y nadie las había armado nunca. En el episodio 3, Weevil Underwood las tira al mar camino a Duelist Kingdom, Joey rescata solo dos y Yugi no vuelve a usarlas.","en":"In episode 1, Yami Yugi faces Kaiba. Yugi assembles all five pieces, and Exodia appears and fires an attack that takes down every Blue-Eyes White Dragon on Kaiba's side at once. Yugi says the cards were an experiment by the game's creators that nobody had ever managed to assemble. In episode 3, Weevil Underwood tosses them overboard on the way to Duelist Kingdom, Joey saves only two and Yugi never uses them again."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One","Blue-Eyes White Dragon","Right Arm of the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"La versión del manga: Haga y el nivel 7","en":"The manga version: Haga and Level 7"},"p":{"es":"En el manga la escena del barco es parecida, pero el villano es Insector Haga: pide ver las cartas de Exodia que Yugi usó para vencer a Kaiba y las tira al agua. Jonouchi se zambulle y rescata dos de las cinco, y Dark Yugi jura sacar primero a Haga del torneo. La carta del manga también cambia: es de nivel 7, con tipo desconocido, mientras que la del anime es de nivel 3 y Spellcaster. Su texto habla de abatir a cualquier enemigo en un solo instante.","en":"In the manga the ship scene is similar, but the villain is Insector Haga: he demands a look at the Exodia cards that won Yugi his Duel against Kaiba, then throws them overboard. Jonouchi dives in and saves two of the five, and Dark Yugi vows to knock Haga out of the tournament first. The manga card also differs: it is Level 7 with an unknown Type, while the anime card is Level 3 and a Spellcaster. Its text speaks of striking down any enemy in a single instant."},"cards":["Left Leg of the Forbidden One","Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"El ka de Shimon en el Antiguo Egipto","en":"Shimon's ka in ancient Egypt"},"p":{"es":"En los recuerdos del Faraón, Exodia es un ka que invocan los sacerdotes poco después de forjar los Millennium Items, y defiende el reino de los invasores. La leyenda dice que derrotó a mil soldados en una noche (mil ejércitos en el manga). Shimon, llamado Siamun en el manga, lo selló en cinco tablillas por miedo a su poder. Contra Zorc lo invoca con la Millennium Key: Zorc lo parte al medio con su Dark Phenomenon y Shimon muere.","en":"In the Pharaoh's memories, Exodia is a ka summoned by the priests shortly after the Millennium Items were forged, and it defends the kingdom from invaders. Legend says it beat a thousand soldiers in one night (a thousand armies in the manga). Shimon, called Siamun in the manga, sealed it in five slabs out of fear of its power. Against Zorc he summons it with the Millennium Key: Zorc splits it down the middle with his Dark Phenomenon and Shimon dies."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"Ecos en el anime: Seeker, Gozaburo y GX","en":"Echoes in the anime: Seeker, Gozaburo and GX"},"p":{"es":"Después de Yugi, otros usan Exodia en el anime. Seeker, de los Rare Hunters, la usa contra Joey, pero Yami Yugi destruye todas sus copias con Chain Destruction. Gozaburo Kaiba manda las piezas al Cementerio para invocar a Exodia Necross, y Seto las destierra con Soul Demolition y lo deja sin habilidades. En GX, Marcel Bonaparte, poseído por Yubel, quiso usar dos Break the Seal para sumar a Exodia a su mano, pero el duelo se cortó antes.","en":"After Yugi, others use Exodia in the anime. Seeker of the Rare Hunters plays it against Joey, but Yami Yugi destroys every copy with Chain Destruction. Gozaburo Kaiba sends the pieces to the Graveyard to Summon Exodia Necross, and Seto banishes them with Soul Demolition, leaving it powerless. In GX, Marcel Bonaparte, possessed by Yubel, meant to use two Break the Seal to add Exodia to his hand, but the Duel ended before he could."},"cards":["Chain Destruction","Exodia Necross","Break the Seal"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Forbidden One","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Forbidden_One","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Exodia the Forbidden One (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Exodia_the_Forbidden_One_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Exodia the Forbidden One (manga character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Exodia_the_Forbidden_One_(manga_character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yugi Mutou (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yugi_Mutou_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Exodia the Forbidden One (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Exodia_the_Forbidden_One_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Exodia the Forbidden One (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Exodia_the_Forbidden_One_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"El texto real de la carta solo dice que las cinco piezas en la mano ganan el duelo; el resto es historia del anime o del manga. Los nombres cambian (Shimon en el anime, Siamun en el manga; Weevil en el anime, Haga en el manga). No encontramos una fuente que ligue a Exodia con Pegasus, así que no se afirma nada de eso. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The real card text only says that the five pieces in hand win the Duel; the rest is anime or manga story. Names change (Shimon in the anime, Siamun in the manga; Weevil in the anime, Haga in the manga). We found no source linking Exodia to Pegasus, so nothing of that is claimed. We did not find a content-creator piece that could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"gogiga-gagagigo","kind":"archetype","name":"Gogiga Gagagigo","badge":{"es":"Del joven Gigobyte al monstruo que perdió el rumbo","en":"From young Gigobyte to the monster that lost its way"},"origin":{"es":"Cartas OCG/TCG, manga de Yu-Gi-Oh!, anime GX y World Championship 2008","en":"OCG/TCG cards, the Yu-Gi-Oh! manga, the GX anime and World Championship 2008"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"El cambio de rumbo de Gagagigo (cartas)","en":"Gagagigo's change of heart (cards)"},"p":{"es":"Gagagigo es un Reptil Normal de Nivel 4, 1850 de ATK. El texto de la carta lo describe como un joven que tenía un corazón malvado hasta que conoció a alguien especial y descubrió la justicia. En el relato de las cartas OCG/TCG, ese cambio ocurre cuando lo salva el Marauding Captain; la carta My Body as a Shield recuerda un gesto del Capitán que se interpone para proteger a un soldado. Después Gagagigo se mete en muchas batallas.","en":"Gagagigo is a Level 4 Reptile Normal Monster with 1850 ATK. The card text describes a young creature who had an evil heart until meeting a special person, and discovering justice. In the OCG/TCG card storyline, that change comes when Marauding Captain saves him; the card My Body as a Shield recalls the Captain stepping in to shield a soldier. Afterwards Gagagigo fights in many battles."},"cards":["Gagagigo","Marauding Captain","My Body as a Shield"]},{"h":{"es":"De Gigobyte a Gogiga (cartas)","en":"From Gigobyte to Gogiga (cards)"},"p":{"es":"La línea sigue un camino cuesta abajo. Gigobyte, de Nivel 1, tiene un alma tranquila pero un destino de corazón manchado por el mal. Giga Gagagigo, de Nivel 5, ganó un poder enorme reconstruyendo su cuerpo para enfrentar un mal enorme, pero perdió el corazón y la redención. Gogiga Gagagigo, Nivel 8 con 2950 ATK, ya tiene el alma quebrada, y su cuerpo avanza descontrolado en busca de más poder, sin parecerse a lo que fue.","en":"The line follows a downward path. Gigobyte, at Level 1, has a calm soul but a destiny of a heart stained by evil. Giga Gagagigo, at Level 5, gained great power by rebuilding his body to face a tremendous evil, but lost his heart and his redemption. Gogiga Gagagigo, Level 8 with 2950 ATK, has a shattered soul, and his body advances out of control in search of more power, no longer resembling what he was."},"cards":["Gigobyte","Giga Gagagigo","Gogiga Gagagigo"]},{"h":{"es":"Rivales y redención (historia de las cartas)","en":"Rivals and redemption (card storyline)"},"p":{"es":"Según la Master Guide 1, la gente empezó a llamarlo Giga Gagagigo y al final se puso una armadura, aunque ya no se sentía vivo en combate. Tuvo un rival, Freed, con quien se peleaba a golpes y acabó formando una amistad extraña; el marcador era de 24 victorias y 26 derrotas para Gagagigo. Ese relato termina con su alma quebrada y la duda de si volverá a ser el de antes. Otro relato lo hace recuperar el juicio y volverse bueno de nuevo como Gagagigo the Risen, un Xyz de Rango 4.","en":"According to Master Guide 1, people began calling him Giga Gagagigo and he finally put on armor, though he no longer felt alive in battle. He had a rival, Freed, whom he fought with his fists, and a strange friendship formed; the score was 24 wins and 26 losses for Gagagigo. That story ends with his soul shattered and a question of whether he will ever be himself again. Another account has him regain his senses and turn good again as Gagagigo the Risen, a Rank 4 Xyz Monster."},"cards":["Freed the Matchless General","Gagagigo the Risen"]},{"h":{"es":"Gagagigo en el manga y el anime","en":"Gagagigo in the manga and anime"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Gagagigo es un Monstruo Espíritu Egipcio: en la batalla final contra Zorc Necrophades, Hiroto Honda lo invoca junto al Dark Magician de Yugi y el Red-Eyes de Joey, en el capítulo 54 de Millennium World. En el anime, la carta aparece en el episodio 185 de Duel Monsters y en varios de GX. La wiki lista como usuarios a Luke, de Duel Monsters, a Wheeler y a los Duel Ghouls (zombis de duelo). Wheeler es un mono de laboratorio en GX, y se ve un Gagagigo en su mano al final del duelo con Jaden.","en":"In the manga, Gagagigo is an Egyptian Spirit Monster: Hiroto Honda summons it in the last fight against Zorc Necrophades, next to Yugi's Dark Magician and Joey's Red-Eyes (Millennium World chapter 54). In the anime, the card appears in Duel Monsters episode 185 and in several GX episodes. The wiki lists Luke from Duel Monsters, Wheeler and the Duel Ghouls as users. Wheeler is a lab monkey in GX, and a Gagagigo is seen in his hand at the end of his Duel against Jaden."},"cards":["Gagagigo"]},{"h":{"es":"Gogiga en pantalla y en los juegos","en":"Gogiga on screen and in the games"},"p":{"es":"Según la wiki, Gogiga Gagagigo figura en el mazo de mezclas al azar de Aster Phoenix en GX, y la carta se ve en el opening de la segunda temporada. No hay un duelo suyo documentado en lo que consultamos. En el videojuego World Championship 2008 es un personaje, y forma con Mobius the Frost Monarch el equipo Water Splash, que se enfrenta en el mundo de duelo de Oscuridad (Darkness). Ahí solo emite gruñidos y chillidos.","en":"According to the wiki, Gogiga Gagagigo is in Aster Phoenix's random-pack Deck in GX, and the card can be seen in the second season's opening. No Duel of his own is documented in what we consulted. In the World Championship 2008 video game it is a character, and teams up with Mobius the Frost Monarch as Water Splash, faced in the Darkness Duel World. There it only utters growls and yelps."},"cards":["Gogiga Gagagigo"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Gagagigo","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gagagigo","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gogiga Gagagigo","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gogiga_Gagagigo","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gagagigo (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gagagigo_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 1 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_1_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gagagigo (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gagagigo_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Wheeler","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Wheeler","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gogiga Gagagigo (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gogiga_Gagagigo_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Aster Phoenix","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Aster_Phoenix","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Duel Ghoul","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Duel_Ghoul","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gagagigo the Risen","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gagagigo_the_Risen","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Giga Gagagigo","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Giga_Gagagigo","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Gigobyte","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gigobyte","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"El relato del Marauding Captain, de Freed y de la recuperación como Gagagigo the Risen es historia de las cartas (Master Guide 1 y la ficha del personaje en la wiki), no del anime ni del manga. El manga y GX solo muestran a Gagagigo en pantalla; Gogiga aparece sin un duelo documentado. La wiki no documenta un duelo concreto de Gogiga con Aster, y el episodio 185 con Luke figura solo en la ficha de la carta. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The Marauding Captain, Freed and Gagagigo the Risen recovery stories are card storyline (Master Guide 1 and the wiki's character page), not anime or manga. The manga and GX only show Gagagigo on screen; Gogiga appears with no documented Duel. The wiki documents no specific Duel of Gogiga with Aster, and episode 185 with Luke appears only on the card's entry. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"gusto","kind":"archetype","name":"Gusto","badge":{"es":"El clan del viento que defiende los pantanos junto a las aves","en":"The wind clan that guards the marshlands beside its birds"},"origin":{"es":"Historias oficiales de las cartas (Duel Terminal, Master Guide y Valuable Book EX)","en":"Official card storylines (Duel Terminal, Master Guide and Valuable Book EX)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Un clan pacífico en Mist Valley","en":"A peaceful clan in Mist Valley"},"p":{"es":"Los Gusto son un clan pacífico de los pantanos de Mist Valley, amantes de la naturaleza, que viven entre las aves y las bestias de la región. El jefe y sus parientes de sangre son amigos de esos animales, y quien tiene el lazo más hondo se convierte en el próximo jefe. En la casa principal, Windaar, Sage of Gusto, es el patriarca, y Winda, Priestess of Gusto, lo reemplaza como matriarca cuando él va a la guerra. En la casa sacerdotal, Musto, Oracle of Gusto, aconseja al patriarca cuando falta.","en":"The Gusto are a peaceful clan of the Mist Valley marshlands who love nature and live among the region's birds and beasts. The chief and his blood relatives are friends of those animals, and whoever has the deepest bond becomes the next chief. In the main house, Windaar, Sage of Gusto, is the patriarch, and Winda, Priestess of Gusto, stands in as matriarch when he goes to war. In the priest house, Musto, Oracle of Gusto, advises the patriarch when he is away."},"cards":["Windaar, Sage of Gusto","Winda, Priestess of Gusto","Musto, Oracle of Gusto"]},{"h":{"es":"Amigos con alas y un secreto del clan","en":"Winged friends and a clan secret"},"p":{"es":"Desde chicos, los miembros del clan se entrenan con dureza en Mist Valley, y al llegar a adultos sellan un vínculo con un ave o una bestia, que pasa a ser su amigo, como Gusto Egul o Gusto Gulldo. Un secreto que se hereda en el clan potencia mucho las capacidades físicas de esos amigos, y así surge un guerrero mitad ave y mitad humano, como Daigusto Gulldos. Con ese estilo, donde corazón y mente se funden con los de las aves, el clan defiende siempre sus tierras fértiles de quienes quieren quedárselas.","en":"From childhood, clan members train hard in Mist Valley, and on reaching adulthood they seal a bond with a bird or beast, who becomes their friend, like Gusto Egul or Gusto Gulldo. A secret passed down in the clan greatly boosts those friends' physical abilities, and the result is a warrior both bird and human, like Daigusto Gulldos. With this style, where heart and mind merge with the birds', the clan always defends its fertile lands from those who want to take them."},"cards":["Gusto Egul","Gusto Gulldo","Daigusto Gulldos"]},{"h":{"es":"Kamui, Reeze y Falco","en":"Kamui, Reeze and Falco"},"p":{"es":"Kamui nace en plena guerra y recibe el nombre Hope, por ser quien guiará a la generación siguiente. Su compañero es Gusto Falco, con quien se sincroniza a la perfección y ejecuta muchos ataques combinados. Reeze, de la casa guerrera, sale a combatir con un bastón de pelea que solo puede usar su casa, para proteger la aldea, y mantiene una relación con su amigo de la infancia, Kamui.","en":"Kamui is born in the middle of a war and is named Hope, as the one who will lead the next generation. His partner is Gusto Falco, with whom he syncs perfectly and pulls off many combined attacks. Reeze, of the warrior house, goes into battle with a combat staff that only her house may wield, to protect the village, and is in a relationship with her childhood friend Kamui."},"cards":["Kamui, Hope of Gusto","Gusto Falco","Reeze, Whirlwind of Gusto"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Gishki invaden el pantano","en":"The Gishki invade the marsh"},"p":{"es":"Los Gishki, liderados por Noellia, quieren los recursos del pantano y lanzan una invasión contra los Gusto. El clan, que antes había ayudado a Noellia, se confunde, pero se defiende con guerreros como Daigusto Eguls. El verdadero fin es otro: Noellia busca el poder de Dios, que según se cree duerme allí y es venerado en el Shrine of Mist Valley, y los pensamientos de los Steelswarm en su mente la empujan. Además quiere romper el sello de los Steelswarm, sus compañeros, que están cerca. Al liberarlos, los depredadores devoran incluso a los aliados Gishki.","en":"The Gishki, led by Noellia, want the marsh's resources and launch an invasion of the Gusto. The clan, which had helped Noellia before, is bewildered but fights back with warriors like Daigusto Eguls. The real goal is different: Noellia seeks the power of God, said to sleep there and worshiped at the Shrine of Mist Valley, and the Steelswarm thoughts in her mind drive her. She also wants to break the seal on the Steelswarm, her comrades, who lie nearby. Once freed, the predators devour even their Gishki allies."},"cards":["Gishki Noellia","Shrine of Mist Valley","Daigusto Eguls"]},{"h":{"es":"La guerra contra los Vylon y Disigma","en":"The war against the Vylon and Disigma"},"p":{"es":"Para frenar a los Steelswarm, los Vylon se acoplan como equipo a las fuerzas de cada tribu. Reeze se destaca en el combate y recibe de ellos su poder: Vylon Sphere, que da lugar a Daigusto Sphreez. Pero Noellia contagia los pensamientos Steelswarm a los Vylon, que enloquecen y atacan a todas las tribus. Cuatro tribus se alían y despiertan el poder Xyz, pero Vylon Disigma absorbe a seis guerreros. Daigusto Falcos, a cargo de Kamui, se deja absorber para salvarlo. Gem-Knight Pearl logra destruir a Disigma.","en":"To stop the Steelswarm, the Vylon attach themselves as equipment to each tribe's main forces. Reeze stands out in combat and receives their power: Vylon Sphere, which gives rise to Daigusto Sphreez. But Noellia spreads the Steelswarm thoughts to the Vylon, who go mad and attack every tribe. Four tribes ally and awaken Xyz power, but Vylon Disigma absorbs six warriors. Daigusto Falcos, handled by Kamui, lets himself be absorbed to save him. Gem-Knight Pearl manages to destroy Disigma."},"cards":["Vylon Sphere","Daigusto Sphreez","Daigusto Falcos"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Vientos Venenosos","en":"The Poisonous Winds"},"p":{"es":"Cuando Noellia se recupera, retoma el ataque a los Gusto. Esta vez libera un veneno mortal en el viento que baja de Mist Valley hacia los pantanos: Poisonous Winds. La mayoría del clan muere. Caam, al borde de la muerte, no puede mantenerse en pie, y Winda va al Shrine of Mist Valley a rogar ayuda. Su padre Windaar carga contra los Gishki y detiene el veneno por un rato con Dust Storm of Gusto. Entonces llegan los Gem-Knights, que también quieren paz: de la fusión de Gem-Knight Emerald con un Gusto sale Daigusto Emeral, que barre el viento envenenado.","en":"When Noellia recovers, she resumes the attack on the Gusto. This time she lets a deadly poison loose in the wind that flows from Mist Valley to the marshes: Poisonous Winds. Most of the clan dies. Caam, near death, cannot stand, and Winda goes to the Shrine of Mist Valley to beg for help. Her father Windaar charges the Gishki and halts the poison for a while with Dust Storm of Gusto. Then the Gem-Knights arrive, who also want peace: from the fusion of Gem-Knight Emerald with a Gusto comes Daigusto Emeral, who sweeps the poisoned wind away."},"cards":["Poisonous Winds","Dust Storm of Gusto","Daigusto Emeral"]},{"h":{"es":"La guerra Evilswarm y el Divine Wind","en":"The Evilswarm war and the Divine Wind"},"p":{"es":"Cuando surgen los Evilswarm y amenazan al mundo, los Gusto se suman a los Gem-Knights y a los Constellar para detenerlos. El choque final de Constellar Ptolemy M7 contra Evilswarm Ouroboros ocurre sobre los pantanos de Mist Valley, y deja arrasadas las zonas vecinas. En ese cielo se forma el Divine Wind of Mist Valley, que llega hasta el santuario, donde Dios decide purificar el mundo. La guerra termina con la derrota de Sophia, Goddess of Rebirth. La página Gusto dice que solo sobreviven Kamui y Reeze, mientras Master Guide suma a los más jóvenes como guardianes del pantano; la wiki no lo concilia.","en":"When the Evilswarm appear and threaten the world, the Gusto join the Gem-Knights and the Constellars to stop them. The final clash of Constellar Ptolemy M7 against Evilswarm Ouroboros takes place above the Mist Valley marshlands, and leaves the neighboring areas devastated. In that sky the Divine Wind of Mist Valley forms and reaches the shrine, where God decides to purify the world. The war ends with the defeat of Sophia, Goddess of Rebirth. The Gusto page says only Kamui and Reeze survive, while Master Guide adds the youngest as guardians of the marsh; the wiki does not reconcile this."},"cards":["Divine Wind of Mist Valley","Constellar Ptolemy M7","Sophia, Goddess of Rebirth"]},{"h":{"es":"Pilica y una nueva tribu","en":"Pilica and a new tribe"},"p":{"es":"Poco después, Kamui y Reeze forman una familia y nace Pilica, del linaje del jefe que protege los pantanos. Lleva el bastón heredado, con una estatuilla que Kamui talló por su compañero caído en la gran guerra. Su cintillo, regalo de su mejor amiga Gishki, simboliza la paz entre ambas tribus. Se ignora qué fue de Reeze. Kamui funda con Pilica una tribu nueva, los Ritual Beast, a la que se suman al final de la guerra contra Tierra Winda y Falco, revividos. En la Star War, Pilica usa el poder Zefra: Ritual Beast Tamer Zeframpilica y Daigusto Laplampilica.","en":"Soon after, Kamui and Reeze form a family and Pilica is born, in the lineage of the chief who protects the marshes. She carries the inherited staff, topped by a statuette Kamui carved to remember the companion he lost in the great war. Her hairband, a gift from her best Gishki friend, symbolizes peace between both tribes. What became of Reeze is unknown. Kamui founds a new tribe with Pilica, the Ritual Beasts, which Winda and Falco, revived, join once the war against Tierra ends. In the Star War, Pilica wields the Zefra power: Ritual Beast Tamer Zeframpilica and Daigusto Laplampilica."},"cards":["Pilica, Descendant of Gusto","Ritual Beast Tamer Zeframpilica","Daigusto Laplampilica"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness","title":"[VBEX2 Lore] Number 14: Other Cards","url":"https://ygorganization.com/leavingyouthebusinesswithoutleavingyouthebusiness/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Relato original en inglés del último bloque (Pilica en la Star War), con las ilustraciones de esas cartas.","en":"Original English story behind the last block (Pilica in the Star War), with the illustrations of those cards."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Gusto","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Gusto","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Duel Terminal Master Guide card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Duel_Terminal_Master_Guide_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 4 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_4_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 2 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_2_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia junta tres relatos oficiales: Duel Terminal Master Guide (el clan, los Gishki, los Vylon, los Evilswarm), Master Guide 4 (Pilica y la tribu) y The Valuable Book EX 2 (Pilica en la Star War). El enlace del creador cubre solo el bloque 8; la wiki no cita publicaciones de creadores para los bloques 1 a 7. Gusto Gulldo aparece como amigo alado del clan, sin trama propia. La muerte de Winda no se cuenta aquí: la página Gusto solo dice que ella y Falco regresan, y eso se menciona en el bloque 8. El destino de Reeze no se aclara. Los efectos de las cartas quedan aparte.","en":"The story joins three official storylines: Duel Terminal Master Guide (the clan, the Gishki, the Vylon, the Evilswarm), Master Guide 4 (Pilica and the tribe) and The Valuable Book EX 2 (Pilica in the Star War). The creator link covers block 8 only; the wiki cites no creator posts for blocks 1 to 7. Gusto Gulldo appears as the clan's winged friend, with no plot of his own. Winda's death is not told here: the Gusto page only says she and Falco return, which block 8 mentions. Reeze's fate is not made clear. Card effects are kept apart."}},{"slug":"invoked","kind":"archetype","name":"Invoked","badge":{"es":"Las bestias que invoca Aleister, el mago borrado de la historia","en":"The beasts summoned by Aleister, the sorcerer erased from history"},"origin":{"es":"Guía oficial Master Guide 6, anime THE CHRONICLES y manga OCG Stories","en":"Official Master Guide 6, THE CHRONICLES anime and OCG Stories manga"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Aleister, el hechicero que la historia olvidó","en":"Aleister, the sorcerer history forgot"},"p":{"es":"La Master Guide 6, la guía oficial, arranca con una pérdida. Aleister, hechicero genial de una era lejana, aprendió un arte prohibido llamado Invocation, con el que se podían traer espíritus, conjuraciones e incluso dioses desde reinos que nadie conocía. Después se fundó La Maison y todo registro del hombre y de sus estudios desapareció de la historia de la magia. La misma guía agrega la verdad: un experimento lo dejó fusionado en parte con uno de esos seres. Hoy yace bajo La Maison, conectado a sus máquinas y exprimido como fuente de energía, y si despierta del todo será su peor peligro.","en":"Master Guide 6, the official guidebook, starts with a loss. A sorcerer of genius from a distant age, Aleister, learned a banned art named Invocation, through which spirits, conjurations and even gods could be fetched from realms nobody knew. Then La Maison was founded, and every record of the man and his studies vanished from magical history. The same guide adds what really happened: an experiment left him partly fused with one such being. Today he sits far below La Maison, wired to its machinery and drained for power, and the guide warns that if he ever wakes properly he turns into its worst danger."},"cards":["Aleister the Invoker","Invocation","Crowley, the First Propheseer"]},{"h":{"es":"Anime: los Tres Sabios y una deuda pendiente","en":"Anime: the Three Sages and an unpaid debt"},"p":{"es":"THE CHRONICLES le da a Aleister otro pasado. Fue uno de tres sabios, con Endymion y Rilliona, y juntos sellaron a Zoroa, que pretendía acabar con el mundo tras recibir poder de Vahram. Más tarde Aleister se fundió con un espíritu que había convocado, perdió el control y Endymion lo encerró en la Grand Spellbook Tower. En la serie rompe su tubo de estasis en el sótano, decidido a saldar cuentas con Endymion. Llega a una aldea dominada por un farsante, cuya bestia funciona con un prototipo defectuoso de uno de sus libros. Aleister salva a una nena y liquida a la bestia invocando por completo a Cocytus.","en":"THE CHRONICLES gives Aleister a different past. He was one of three sages, with Endymion and Rilliona, who together sealed Zoroa, a would-be destroyer of the world empowered by Vahram. At some later point Aleister fused with a spirit he had called up, lost himself, and Endymion locked him away inside the Grand Spellbook Tower. In the series he escapes his stasis tube in the basement, set on settling accounts with Endymion. He reaches a village ruled by a fraud whose beast runs on a defective prototype of one of Aleister's spellbooks. Aleister saves a girl from it and destroys the beast by fully summoning Cocytus."},"cards":["Invoked Cocytus","Aleister the Invoker"]},{"h":{"es":"Anime: la cueva de Zoroa","en":"Anime: Zoroa's cave"},"p":{"es":"El cierre del arco pasa en la cueva donde tienen preso a Zoroa. Endymion y Rilliona están perdiendo contra él cuando aparece Aleister, frena un golpe casi mortal invocando a un caballero (Invoked Mechaba) y les pide que ganen tiempo mientras termina una invocación nueva. Zoroa lo alcanza igual, pero tarde: surge un dragón negro y lo derriba, y los tres sabios lo sellan otra vez. Al día siguiente, riéndose de las peleas de sus amigos, Aleister confiesa que nunca les guardó rencor: su deuda consistía en volver a sellar a Zoroa si regresaba. Después su cuerpo ilusorio se disuelve en el cielo.","en":"The anime arc ends in the cave where Zoroa is held. Endymion and Rilliona are losing to him when Aleister turns up, blocks a near-lethal strike by summoning a knight (Invoked Mechaba), and asks them to stall while he completes a fresh invocation. Zoroa hits him anyway, but too late: a black dragon appears and brings Zoroa down, and the three sages seal him once more. The next day, laughing at his friends' bickering, Aleister admits he never resented them: his debt meant sealing Zoroa again should he return. His illusory body then dissolves into the sky."},"cards":["Invoked Mechaba","Invoked De Anima"]},{"h":{"es":"Manga: Crowley, el joven que investiga otros mundos","en":"Manga: Crowley, the young researcher of other worlds"},"p":{"es":"OCG Stories es un relato aparte. Su protagonista es Aleister Crowley, un joven alegre y despreocupado del mundo de Astrodia, la versión personaje de Crowley, the Magistus of Grimoires. Estudia la invocación: espíritus que llegan desde otros mundos siguiendo un flujo de poder mágico. Endymion lo toma por un disparate. Entonces uno de los círculos de Crowley, pensado para contener una energía extraña, junta unas formas diminutas y crea a Cocytus, un espíritu que ataca al grupo. Crowley, Endymion, Rilliona y Zoroa terminan siendo Magistus, y cuando Zoroa los traiciona Crowley llama a su deidad guardiana, Aiwass.","en":"OCG Stories is a separate telling. Its lead is Aleister Crowley, a cheerful, easygoing young man of the world of Astrodia, the character form of Crowley, the Magistus of Grimoires. He studies invocation: spirits arriving from other worlds along a flow of magic power. Endymion calls the idea absurd. Then one of Crowley's circles, meant to contain a strange energy, merges tiny shapes into Cocytus, a spirit that attacks the group. Crowley, Endymion, Rilliona and Zoroa eventually all rank as Magistus, and when Zoroa turns on them Crowley calls his guardian deity, Aiwass."},"cards":["Crowley, the Magistus of Grimoires","Invoked Cocytus"]},{"h":{"es":"Diseño: una bestia por Atributo","en":"Design: one beast per Attribute"},"p":{"es":"Fuera de la historia, los Invoked son monstruos de Fusión dibujados como si los hechiceros los hubieran llamado. Cada uno toma un Atributo y presta su nombre de una figura o un lugar histórico o mitológico vinculado a él: Raidjin remite a Raijin, Mechaba remite a Merkabah. En Japón el arquetipo se llama Invoked Beast. En cada ilustración se esconde una copia del báculo de Aleister, más luminosa que la original. En el juego, Invocation hace la Fusión desterrando a Aleister the Invoker y a un segundo monstruo de tu mano, tu campo o cualquiera de los Cementerios.","en":"Outside the story, the Invoked are Fusion Monsters drawn to look as if sorcerers called them. Each takes one Attribute and borrows its name from a historical or mythological figure or place linked to it: Raidjin echoes Raijin, Mechaba echoes Merkabah. In Japan the archetype is called Invoked Beast. Every artwork hides a copy of Aleister's staff, glowing brighter than the original. In play, Invocation does the Fusion by banishing Aleister the Invoker plus a second monster from hand, field or either Graveyard."},"cards":["Invoked Raidjin","Invoked Mechaba","Invocation"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Invoked","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Invoked","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Aleister (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Aleister_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Aleister Crowley","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Aleister_Crowley","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Hay tres fuentes distintas: la guía oficial (Master Guide 6), el anime THE CHRONICLES y el manga OCG Stories. No forman una sola cronología y las versiones de Aleister difieren entre sí. El origen de los nombres de las bestias (último bloque) es un dato de diseño, no de la historia. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido que profundice en este lore y que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"There are three separate sources: the official guidebook (Master Guide 6), the THE CHRONICLES anime and the OCG Stories manga. They are not one timeline and the versions of Aleister differ. The origin of the beasts' names (last block) is a design note, not story. We did not find a content-creator piece that goes deeper into this lore and could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"jaden-yuki","kind":"character","name":"Jaden Yuki","badge":{"es":"De Slifer Red a Supreme King, y de vuelta: la historia de Jaden","en":"From Slifer Red to Supreme King and back: Jaden's story"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (anime) y la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (anime) and the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Un niño con una carta peligrosa (anime)","en":"A boy with a dangerous card (anime)"},"p":{"es":"De chico, Jaden adoraba Duel Monsters y su carta preferida era Yubel, un regalo de su padre. Como sus padres casi nunca estaban en casa, pasaba los días jugando con los chicos del barrio, pero el espíritu de la carta lo cuidaba de más y lastimaba a sus rivales: su amigo Osamu quedó en coma después de un duelo. Desde entonces nadie quería enfrentarlo. Por esos años ganó un concurso de diseño de KaibaCorp con sus propios monstruos, entre ellos los Neo-Spacians, y pidió que Yubel viajara al espacio en otra cápsula, con la esperanza de que las ondas espaciales la calmaran.","en":"As a boy, Jaden loved Duel Monsters, and his favorite card was Yubel, a gift from his father. With his parents almost never home, he spent his days playing the neighborhood kids, but the card's spirit was overprotective and hurt his opponents: his friend Osamu fell into a coma after a Duel. After that, nobody wanted to face him. Around then he won a KaibaCorp card design contest with his own monsters, the Neo-Spacians among them, and asked for Yubel to travel into space in a separate capsule, hoping the space waves would calm them."},"cards":["Yubel"]},{"h":{"es":"Slifer Red y el primer año (anime)","en":"Slifer Red and the first year (anime)"},"p":{"es":"El día del examen de ingreso a Duel Academy, Jaden iba con el tiempo justo, tropezó con Yugi Muto en plena calle y recibió de él un Winged Kuriboh. Aun llegando tarde lo dejaron rendir: el Dr. Crowler lo enfrentó con su mazo personal y Jaden ganó con Elemental HERO Flame Wingman, su carta favorita. Por sus notas quedó en Slifer Red, la residencia de menor rango, junto a Syrus Truesdale y Chumley. Ahí empezó su rivalidad con Chazz Princeton, a quien venció en los exámenes de promoción gracias a Winged Kuriboh LV10.","en":"On the morning of his Duel Academy entrance exam Jaden was cutting it close, crashed into Yugi Muto in the street and received a Winged Kuriboh from him. Even arriving late, he got to take the exam: Dr. Crowler faced him with a personal Deck and Jaden won with Elemental HERO Flame Wingman, his favorite card. His grades put him in Slifer Red, the lowest-ranked dorm, alongside Syrus Truesdale and Chumley. There began his rivalry with Chazz Princeton, whom he beat in the promotion exams thanks to Winged Kuriboh LV10."},"cards":["Winged Kuriboh","Elemental HERO Flame Wingman"]},{"h":{"es":"Shadow Riders y Kagemaru (anime)","en":"The Shadow Riders and Kagemaru (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Durante ese año Jaden descubrió que algunos duelos de la isla eran Shadow Duels, con dolor real. Gravekeeper's Chief le dio la mitad de un Shadow Charm y la otra mitad la tenía Nightshroud, primero de los Shadow Riders, que sellan almas en cartas. Con el amuleto completo, Jaden venció a Camula con Elemental HERO Shining Flare Wingman y devolvió las almas de Crowler y Zane. El último Rider era el profesor Banner, y detrás de todo estaba el director Kagemaru, que quería las Sacred Beasts. Jaden lo venció multiplicando con Sabatiel el ataque de Elemental HERO Electrum.","en":"During that year Jaden found out that some Duels on the island were Shadow Duels, with real pain. Gravekeeper's Chief gave him half of a Shadow Charm, and the other half belonged to Nightshroud, the first of the Shadow Riders, who seal souls in cards. With the complete charm, Jaden beat Camula with Elemental HERO Shining Flare Wingman and restored the souls of Crowler and Zane. The last Rider was Professor Banner, and behind it all was Chairman Kagemaru, who wanted the Sacred Beasts. Jaden beat him by using Sabatiel to multiply the ATK of Elemental HERO Electrum."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Shining Flare Wingman","Elemental HERO Electrum","Sabatiel - The Philosopher's Stone"]},{"h":{"es":"Cartas en blanco y Neo Space (anime)","en":"Blank cards and Neo Space (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el segundo año llegó Aster Phoenix, un duelista profesional con un mazo de Destiny Heroes, y venció a Jaden. Tras el duelo, Jaden vio sus cartas en blanco y decidió irse de la academia. Un cometa lo llevó a Neo Space, donde conoció a Aquos, el espíritu de Neo-Spacian Aqua Dolphin, y volvió a ver las cartas: eran los diseños de su concurso infantil, guardados en un satélite de KaibaCorp. Con ese mazo nuevo, basado en Elemental HERO Neos y en la Contact Fusion, regresó a la academia y ganó la revancha contra Aster cuando el ataque Dogma de este se le volvió en contra.","en":"In his second year Aster Phoenix arrived, a professional Duelist with a Destiny Hero Deck, and beat Jaden. After the Duel, Jaden saw his cards as blank and decided to leave the academy. A comet carried him to Neo Space, where he met Aquos, the spirit of Neo-Spacian Aqua Dolphin, and he could see his cards again: they were the designs from his childhood contest, kept in a KaibaCorp satellite. With that new Deck, built around Elemental HERO Neos and Contact Fusion, he returned to the academy and won the rematch against Aster when his Dogma attack backfired."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Neos","Neo-Spacian Aqua Dolphin","Elemental HERO Flare Neos"]},{"h":{"es":"La Luz de la Destrucción (anime)","en":"The Light of Destruction (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Sartorius, el manager de Aster, lideraba la Society of Light, que sumaba alumnos derrotándolos en duelo. Más tarde, en el torneo Genex, intentó hacerse con el control del satélite SORA del reino de Misgarth. Detrás estaba la Luz de la Destrucción (Light of Destruction), que fue pasando de Sartorius al príncipe Ojin. Jaden tuvo que elegir entre su llave del satélite y la vida de Aster, y entregó la llave. Elemental HERO Neos le dijo que solo él tenía el poder gentil de la Oscuridad (Gentle Darkness). Jaden ganó el duelo final contra Sartorius mientras Glow Neos y Hassleberry destruían SORA.","en":"Sartorius, Aster's manager, led the Society of Light, which recruited students by beating them in Duels. Later, in the Genex Tournament, he tried to take control of SORA, the satellite of the Misgarth Kingdom. Behind it was the Light of Destruction, which passed from Sartorius to Prince Ojin. Jaden had to choose between his satellite key and Aster's life, and he handed over the key. Elemental HERO Neos told him that only he held the power of the Gentle Darkness. Jaden won the final Duel against Sartorius while Glow Neos and Hassleberry destroyed SORA."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Glow Neos","Neo-Spacian Glow Moss"]},{"h":{"es":"Dimension World y el Supreme King (anime)","en":"Dimension World and the Supreme King (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el tercer año Duel Academy cayó en otra dimensión, y Jesse Anderson, amigo de Jaden, pareció sacrificarse para que todos volvieran. Jaden regresó a buscarlo y su obsesión terminó con Alexis, Hassleberry, Chazz y Atticus sacrificados por Brron para crear Super Polymerization. Hundido en la culpa, aceptó al espíritu de su antepasado, el Supreme King, y con un mazo Evil HERO oprimió pueblos hasta que Axel lo liberó. Después Yubel reveló que lo cuidaba desde chico y que él era la reencarnación del Supreme King. Jaden fusionó su alma con la de Yubel.","en":"In his third year Duel Academy fell into another dimension, and Jesse Anderson, Jaden's friend, seemed to sacrifice himself so everyone could return. Jaden went back to find him, and his obsession ended with Alexis, Hassleberry, Chazz and Atticus being sacrificed by Brron to create Super Polymerization. Sunk in guilt, he accepted the spirit of his ancestor, the Supreme King, and with an Evil HERO Deck he oppressed villages until Axel freed him. Afterward Yubel revealed that they had watched over him since childhood and that he was the Supreme King's reincarnation. Jaden fused his soul with Yubel's."},"cards":["Super Polymerization","Evil HERO Inferno Wing"]},{"h":{"es":"Oscuridad, Nightshroud y Yugi (anime)","en":"Darkness, Nightshroud and Yugi (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el cuarto año Jaden volvió más callado y se alejó de sus amigos para no exponerlos. Recuperó las ganas de duelear en un duelo en pareja con Alexis. Enfrentó a Trueman, una entidad que arrastraba gente a la oscuridad, y al verdadero Nightshroud, que usaba el cuerpo de Yusuke Fujiwara. En el duelo final, con el mundo en juego, invocó a Neos Wiseman con Yubel y venció con Elemental HERO Divine Neos. Tras la graduación, Winged Kuriboh lo llevó al pasado a duelear con Yugi, y Jaden partió de viaje con una carta de sus amigos.","en":"In his fourth year Jaden came back quieter and kept away from his friends so as not to put them at risk. He regained his love of Dueling in a Tag Duel with Alexis. He faced Trueman, an entity that pulled people into darkness, and the real Nightshroud, who was using Yusuke Fujiwara's body. In the final Duel, with the world at stake, he Summoned Neos Wiseman using Yubel and won with Elemental HERO Divine Neos. After graduation, Winged Kuriboh took him back in time to Duel Yugi, and Jaden set off on a journey with a letter from his friends."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Divine Neos","Neos Wiseman"]},{"h":{"es":"Película 3D Bonds Beyond Time","en":"Film: 3D Bonds Beyond Time"},"p":{"es":"En la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time, Paradox ataca a Jaden en Venecia con Cyber End Dragon, Rainbow Dragon y Stardust Dragon, y Yusei Fudo y el Crimson Dragon lo salvan. Juntos viajan al pasado y suman a Yugi. En su turno, Jaden fusiona a Neos con el Junk Gardna de Yusei para formar Elemental HERO Neos Knight, que destruye dos monstruos Malefic de Paradox. Más tarde, él y Yami Yugi convencen a Yusei de no rendirse ante Malefic Truth Dragon y le dan a Stardust Dragon el poder para vencerlo.","en":"In the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time, Paradox attacks Jaden in Venice with Cyber End Dragon, Stardust Dragon and Rainbow Dragon, and Yusei Fudo and the Crimson Dragon save him. Together they travel to the past and bring Yugi on board. On his turn, Jaden fuses Neos with Yusei's Junk Gardna to form Elemental HERO Neos Knight, which destroys two of Paradox's Malefic monsters. Later, he and Yami Yugi convince Yusei not to give up against Malefic Truth Dragon and give Stardust Dragon the power to beat it."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Neos Knight","Stardust Dragon"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Jaden Yuki - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Jaden_Yuki","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Neo-Spacian - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Neo-Spacian","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Historia del anime GX y de la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time, según Yugipedia. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"Story of the GX anime and the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time, per Yugipedia. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}},{"slug":"joey-wheeler","kind":"character","name":"Joey Wheeler","badge":{"es":"De matón de barrio a duelista que se para después del golpe de Ra","en":"From street kid to the Duelist who stands up after Ra's blast"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga y anime): Jonouchi en Japón, Joey en el doblaje inglés","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (manga and anime): Jonouchi in Japan, Joey in the English dub"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"De matón a duelista novato (anime)","en":"From bully to novice Duelist (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Joey y su hermana Serenity crecen separados: cuando los padres se divorcian, él tiene 10 años, ella se va con la madre y él se queda con el padre. En la escuela hostiga a Yugi y arroja a la pileta una pieza del Millennium Puzzle. Ushio los golpea, Yugi los defiende y Joey rescata la pieza y se la devuelve. El odio hacia Kaiba nace cuando este rompe el Blue-Eyes del abuelo de Yugi. Como el mazo de Joey solo tiene monstruos, Yugi le propone tomar clases con Solomon.","en":"Joey and his sister Serenity end up apart: when their parents divorce he is 10, she goes with their mother and he stays with their father. At school he bullies Yugi and drops a piece of the Millennium Puzzle into the pool. Ushio beats them up, Yugi defends them, and Joey retrieves the piece and returns it. His hatred of Kaiba begins when Kaiba tears up the Blue-Eyes of Yugi's grandfather. Since Joey's Deck holds only monsters, Yugi proposes lessons with Solomon."},"cards":["Blue-Eyes White Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Duelist Kingdom (anime)","en":"Duelist Kingdom (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Joey va con Yugi a Duelist Kingdom: Yugi le da un Star Chip y él quiere el premio para pagar la operación de ojos de Serenity. Apostando el Time Wizard que Yugi le regaló, le gana a Rex Raptor y se queda con su Red-Eyes Black Dragon. Yami Bakura lo atrapa en la carta de Flame Swordsman y Joey se sacrifica por Yugi, hasta que lo reviven. Kaiba lo derrota, pero vence a Keith gracias a una tarjeta de Mai. En la final pierde con Yugi, que le da el premio para Serenity.","en":"Joey goes with Yugi to Duelist Kingdom: Yugi gives him a Star Chip and he wants the prize money for Serenity's eye operation. Betting the Time Wizard that Yugi gave him, he beats Rex Raptor and takes his Red-Eyes Black Dragon. Yami Bakura traps him in the Flame Swordsman card and Joey sacrifices himself for Yugi, until he is revived. Kaiba defeats him, but he beats Keith thanks to a card from Mai. In the final he loses to Yugi, who gives him the prize money for Serenity."},"cards":["Time Wizard","Red-Eyes Black Dragon","Flame Swordsman"]},{"h":{"es":"Battle City y Marik (anime)","en":"Battle City and Marik (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Kaiba le da una clasificación baja, pero un funcionario ve su Red-Eyes Black Dragon, la corrige y avisa a los Rare Hunters. Camino a la operación de Serenity, Seeker lo vence con Exodia y se queda con el Red-Eyes; Yugi vence a Seeker y la recupera, pero Joey insiste en que Yugi la conserve. Después Marik, con el Millennium Rod, lo posee y lo obliga a duelear con Yugi, encadenados a un ancla. Joey se libera, Yugi se dirige Meteor of Destruction a sí mismo, Joey fuerza el empate y Serenity lo rescata.","en":"Kaiba gives him a low rating, but an official spots his Red-Eyes Black Dragon, corrects it and tips off the Rare Hunters. On his way to Serenity's operation, Seeker beats him with Exodia and takes the Red-Eyes; Yugi beats Seeker and wins it back, but Joey insists Yugi keep it. Then Marik, with the Millennium Rod, possesses him and forces him to Duel Yugi, chained to an anchor. Joey breaks free, Yugi aims Meteor of Destruction at himself, Joey forces a draw and Serenity rescues him."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One","Meteor of Destruction"]},{"h":{"es":"De pie después de Ra (anime)","en":"Standing after Ra (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En los cuartos de final, Joey enfrenta a Odion, que se hace pasar por Marik. El Ra de Odion es falso, el verdadero se enfurece y tumba a los dos; gana quien se pare primero, y Joey, soñando con sus amigos, se levanta. En la semifinal, Marik invoca a The Winged Dragon of Ra y Joey sigue de pie tras el golpe, roba Gearfried the Iron Knight y cae antes de atacar. Kaiba reconoce que Joey no es un aficionado cualquiera.","en":"In the quarter-finals, Joey faces Odion, who poses as Marik. Odion's Ra is a fake, the real one is angered and strikes down both players; whoever stands up first wins, and Joey, dreaming of his friends, gets up. In the semi-final, Marik Summons The Winged Dragon of Ra and Joey is still standing after the blast, draws Gearfried the Iron Knight and collapses before attacking. Kaiba admits Joey is no mere amateur."},"cards":["The Winged Dragon of Ra","Gearfried the Iron Knight"]},{"h":{"es":"Hermos, Mai y el Grand Championship (anime)","en":"Hermos, Mai and the Grand Championship (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En Waking the Dragons, Joey saca una espada de un dragón sellado en cristal y The Claw of Hermos entra a su mazo. Contra Mai, bajo el Seal of Orichalcos, la usa para tomar ventaja, hasta que Valon interviene. Más adelante, agotado por el duelo con Valon, empuja a Mai fuera del Seal mientras le quitan el alma; la recupera cuando Yami Yugi vence a Dartz. En el Grand Championship, Yugi dice que Heart of the Underdog le recuerda a un amigo, y llamar underdog a Joey se vuelve un chiste constante.","en":"In Waking the Dragons, Joey pulls a sword from a dragon sealed in crystal and The Claw of Hermos joins his Deck. Against Mai, under the Seal of Orichalcos, he uses it to gain the advantage, until Valon interrupts. Later, exhausted from his Duel with Valon, he pushes Mai out of the Seal as his soul is taken; it returns when Yami Yugi defeats Dartz. In the Grand Championship, Yugi says Heart of the Underdog reminds him of a friend, and calling Joey an underdog becomes a running gag."},"cards":["The Claw of Hermos","Heart of the Underdog"]},{"h":{"es":"Jonouchi hasta Duelist Kingdom (manga)","en":"Jonouchi up to Duelist Kingdom (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Jonouchi vive entre las deudas de su papá y pasa por la banda de Hirutani. Molesta a Yugi y tira una pieza del Puzzle a la pileta. Tras ver un video de Shizuka, cuenta que ella está por perder la vista, y Yugi reparte sus Star Chips con él. Contra Keith, Mai le da su tarjeta de clasificación y Jonouchi gana convirtiendo su Red-Eyes en Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon (copia Metalmorph) con ayuda de Dragon Nails. No juega la final: le pasa a Yugi The Honor of the King's Right.","en":"In the manga, Jonouchi lives amid his dad's debts and spends time in Hirutani's gang. He picks on Yugi and throws a piece of the Puzzle into the pool. After watching a video from Shizuka, he explains she is close to losing her sight, and Yugi splits his Star Chips with him. Against Keith, Mai hands him her qualification card and Jonouchi wins by turning his Red-Eyes into Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon (copying Metalmorph) with help from Dragon Nails. He skips the final and gives Yugi The Honor of the King's Right."},"cards":["Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon","Dragon Nails"]},{"h":{"es":"Battle City y Marik (manga)","en":"Battle City and Marik (manga)"},"p":{"es":"Un empleado corrige la clasificación de Jonouchi al ver su Red-Eyes y avisa a los Rare Hunters. El del Exodia lo vence; Yugi recupera la carta con la regla de ante, pero Jonouchi la rechaza hasta ganársela y juega con Time Wizard; contra Roba gana a Jinzo. Marik lo posee y lo obliga a duelear con Yugi, encadenados a un ancla. Poseído, usa Rocket Warrior para debilitar el Red-Eyes de Yugi; se libera y fuerza el empate, y Kaiba le tira la otra llave al agua.","en":"A clerk corrects Jonouchi's rating on seeing his Red-Eyes and tips off the Rare Hunters. The Exodia one defeats him; Yugi wins the card back through the ante rule, but Jonouchi refuses it until he earns it and plays with Time Wizard; against Roba he wins Jinzo. Marik possesses him and forces him to Duel Yugi, chained to an anchor. Possessed, he uses Rocket Warrior to weaken Yugi's Red-Eyes; he breaks free and forces a draw, and Kaiba drops the other key into the water."},"cards":["Jinzo","Rocket Warrior"]},{"h":{"es":"Rishid y el golpe de Ra (manga)","en":"Rishid and Ra's blast (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En los cuartos de final, Jonouchi enfrenta a Rishid, que dice ser Marik. Rishid contesta su Giant Trunade con Judgment of Anubis, y después sus Embodiment of Apophis lo dejan en 50 puntos de vida. El Ra de Rishid es falso, el verdadero se enfurece y tumba a los dos; gana quien se pare primero, y Jonouchi, soñando con sus amigos, se levanta. Rishid cuenta que es la sombra de Marik. Luego, Dark Marik convierte en Shadow Game el duelo de Mai y Jonouchi intenta liberarla de Ra, hasta que Dark Yugi lo protege.","en":"In the quarter-finals, Jonouchi faces Rishid, who claims to be Marik. Rishid answers his Giant Trunade with Judgment of Anubis, and then his Embodiment of Apophis cards leave him at 50 Life Points. Rishid's Ra is a fake, the real one is angered and strikes down both players; whoever stands up first wins, and Jonouchi, dreaming of his friends, gets up. Rishid says he is Marik's shadow. Then Dark Marik turns Mai's Duel into a Shadow Game and Jonouchi tries to free her from Ra, until Dark Yugi shields him."},"cards":["Giant Trunade","Judgment of Anubis"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Joey Wheeler","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Joey_Wheeler","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Katsuya Jonouchi (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Katsuya_Jonouchi_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Primero va el relato del anime y después el del manga; cada bloque dice en el título cuál sigue. Los nombres cambian (Joey y Serenity en el anime en inglés, Jonouchi y Shizuka en el manga). La wiki marca como incompleto el relato del manga desde Battle City, así que ahí es parcial. Las películas (Pyramid of Light, The Dark Side of Dimensions y Bonds Beyond Time) no se cuentan acá. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"The anime story comes first and the manga story after it; each block says in its title which one it follows. Names differ (Joey and Serenity in the English dub, Jonouchi and Shizuka in Japanese). The wiki marks its manga account from Battle City onward as incomplete, so that part is partial. The films (Pyramid of Light, The Dark Side of Dimensions and Bonds Beyond Time) are not covered here. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}},{"slug":"lightsworn","kind":"archetype","name":"Lightsworn","badge":{"es":"Ejecutores de la justicia que cruzan el espacio y el tiempo","en":"Enforcers of justice who cross space and time"},"origin":{"es":"Cartas OCG/TCG, Master Guide 3 y modo Solo de Master Duel","en":"OCG/TCG cards, Master Guide 3 and Master Duel Solo mode"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"El llamado de los que rezan","en":"The call of those who pray"},"p":{"es":"Según el Master Guide 3, los Lightsworn son un grupo que hace cumplir la justicia. Los convoca desde más allá del espacio y el tiempo el deseo de paz de la gente y el llanto genuino de doncellas. La versión de Master Duel agrega los gritos de quienes viven bajo un tirano y las lágrimas de niños. Irrumpen de repente, como un ejército de luz que rompe la barrera entre mundos, y ayudan a cada persona con una forma de justicia distinta.","en":"According to Master Guide 3, the Lightsworn are a group that enforces justice. What summons them from beyond space and time is the public's wish for peace and the genuine weeping of maidens. The Master Duel version adds the cries of people living under a tyrant and the tears of children. They burst in without warning, like an army of light tearing through the barrier between worlds, and help each person with a different form of justice."},"cards":["Charge of the Light Brigade"]},{"h":{"es":"Cada quien ve un rostro distinto","en":"Each person sees a different face"},"p":{"es":"Según Master Duel, la ayuda llega con la apariencia que cada quien alcanza a percibir. Unos ven a un caballero de armadura reluciente, otros a una hechicera elegante, otros a un ángel divino, y otros a un dragón tan grande que con una sola ala tapa una montaña, o eso aseguran. La misión no cambia con la forma: aniquilar a los malvados y desaparecer sin dejar rastro. El texto lo cuenta con la voz de los testigos, no con una descripción fija de cada uno.","en":"According to Master Duel, help arrives looking like whatever each person is able to perceive. Some see a knight in gleaming armor, others an elegant sorceress, others a divine angel, and others a dragon so vast that one wing blocks out a mountain, or so they claim. The mission does not change with the shape: wipe out the wicked and vanish without a trace. The text tells it through the witnesses' voices, not as a fixed description of each one."},"cards":["Jain, Lightsworn Paladin","Lyla, Lightsworn Sorceress","Celestia, Lightsworn Angel"]},{"h":{"es":"Michael, fundador y juez","en":"Michael, founder and judge"},"p":{"es":"Una traducción de YGOrganization, que la wiki cita, dice que Michael creó la orden y tiene a Judgment Dragon a su lado en todo momento. Fundador o no, parece reclutar los espíritus de héroes que merecen un lugar entre ellos. La secuencia que propone esa pieza es esta: los clamores de paz llaman a los Lightsworn, Michael desciende y dicta sentencia, los héroes de ese mundo también mueren, y sus almas pasan a engrosar las filas. Es un relato de fans traducido, no un texto oficial.","en":"A YGOrganization translation, which the wiki cites, says Michael started the order and has Judgment Dragon at his side at all times. Founder or not, he appears to enlist the spirits of heroes who deserve a place among them. The sequence that piece lays out is this: cries for peace call the Lightsworn, Michael descends and passes judgment, the heroes of that world die too, and their souls join the ranks. It is a translated fan piece, not an official text."},"cards":["Michael, the Arch-Lightsworn","Judgment Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Un ejército con cuatro cuerpos","en":"An army with four branches"},"p":{"es":"El Master Guide 3 reparte a los Lightsworn por funciones. La vanguardia (Ryko, Jain, Ehren, Garoth, Wulf) sale primero al mundo real para entender al enemigo, y muchas veces alcanza para resolver todo. Si la situación es demasiado dura, entran los magos (Lumina, Lyla, Aurkus, Jenis), que atacan desde atrás y anulan los hechizos rivales. La fuerza aérea (Shire, Celestia, Gragonith) toma el cielo. Rinyan integra una división de operaciones encubiertas. Judgment Dragon queda como su arma máxima.","en":"Master Guide 3 sorts the Lightsworn by role. The vanguard (Ryko, Jain, Ehren, Garoth, Wulf) goes into the real world first to understand the enemy, and often that is enough to settle everything. If the situation is too hard, the mages step in (Lumina, Lyla, Aurkus, Jenis), attacking from behind and neutralizing enemy spells. The air force (Shire, Celestia, Gragonith) takes the sky. Rinyan belongs to a covert operations unit. Judgment Dragon stays as their ultimate weapon."},"cards":["Garoth, Lightsworn Warrior","Lumina, Lightsworn Summoner","Gragonith, Lightsworn Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"El Realm of Light","en":"The Realm of Light"},"p":{"es":"Los Lightsworn viven en el Realm of Light, un mundo bañado de luz cuyas leyes están separadas del resto del espacio y el tiempo. Ahí siguen entrenando mientras esperan el día en que haya que impartir justicia. Master Duel agrega que algunos afinan su técnica en ese reino hasta recibir nuevos papeles como ejecutores. Es el punto de partida de cada misión y también el lugar al que vuelven una vez que el mal fue destruido.","en":"The Lightsworn live in the Realm of Light, a world flooded with light, ruled by laws that have nothing to do with ordinary space and time. There they keep training while they wait for the day justice must be handed out. Master Duel adds that some sharpen their skills in that realm until they receive new roles as enforcers. It is the starting point of every mission and also the place they return to once the evil has been destroyed."},"cards":["Realm of Light"]},{"h":{"es":"El cofre sellado y Twilight Cloth","en":"The sealed chest and the Twilight Cloth"},"p":{"es":"Master Duel cuenta que a veces el mal que aparece es demasiado grande incluso para ellos. En lo más profundo del Realm of Light hay un cofre muy bien sellado, y cuando llega un enemigo poderoso su pesada tapa se abre. Dentro esperan unas túnicas negras, plegadas, con poder de oscuridad: el Twilight Cloth. Quien lo viste recibe luz y oscuridad a la vez y no tiene piedad con el mal. Después se suman al negro Punishment Dragon y no cesan hasta limpiar el mundo.","en":"Master Duel says that sometimes the evil that appears is too great even for them. Deep in the Realm of Light lies a tightly sealed chest, and when a mighty enemy arrives its heavy lid opens. Inside wait neatly folded black robes with the power of darkness: the Twilight Cloth. Whoever wears it receives light and darkness together and shows no mercy to evil. They then join forces with the black Punishment Dragon and do not stop until the world is cleansed."},"cards":["Twilight Cloth","Jain, Twilightsworn General","Punishment Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Un precio, una partida y una esperanza","en":"A price, a departure and a hope"},"p":{"es":"Los Lightsworn no pueden quedarse mucho en este mundo, porque mantener cuerpo y mente fuera de su reino consume una enorme cantidad de magia. Por eso, en cuanto derrotan a los malvados, se retiran en haces de luz hacia el Realm of Light. El Master Guide 3 agrega que quien cae abatido en el mundo real vuelve al reino, y como las almas no mueren, la justicia sigue por medio de otro cuerpo pasajero. Su deseo final es que algún día el mundo ya no los necesite.","en":"The Lightsworn cannot stay long in this world, because keeping body and mind outside their realm burns an enormous amount of magic. So the moment the wicked are defeated, they retreat in beams of light to the Realm of Light. Master Guide 3 adds that one who is struck down in the real world is sent back to the realm, and since souls cannot die, justice carries on through some other short-lived body. Their final wish is that someday the world will no longer need them."},"cards":["Glorious Illusion","Lightsworn Sanctuary"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"[OCG] Lore on the Geargias and Lightsworn!","url":"https://ygorganization.com/geargia-lightsworn-lore/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-08","why":{"es":"Traducción de lore OCG que cita la wiki: Michael como fundador y el reclutamiento de almas de héroes.","en":"OCG lore translation the wiki cites: Michael as founder and the recruiting of heroes' souls."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Lightsworn","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Lightsworn","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Twilightsworn","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Twilightsworn","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Duel card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Duel_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 3 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_3_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-08"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia sale de dos guías de cartas, el Master Guide 3 del OCG y el texto Enforcers of Justice del modo Solo de Master Duel (en inglés), más una traducción de fans de lore OCG. No hay una narración corrida de personajes: la wiki es escasa y casi todo describe al grupo, no a cada miembro. Según esa traducción, Ryko sería el perro de Jain y Rinyan el gato de Lumina; Raiden es un infiltrado que desea terminar el conflicto y Minerva una aprendiz de maga con un búho. Las guías no lo confirman. Que los Twilightsworn destierren monstruos Lightsworn y que los Lightsworn manden cartas al Cementerio en la End Phase son reglas de juego; la wiki ata solo el descarte de fin de turno al costo en magia, y el destierro no lo relaciona con la historia. No se cubre el anime (ARC-V figura en el cuadro de la wiki sin trama asociada) ni el nombre OCG Lightroad. No se enlazan más piezas de creadores.","en":"The story comes from two card guides, the OCG's Master Guide 3 and the Enforcers of Justice text in Master Duel's Solo mode (in English), plus a fan translation of OCG lore. There is no continuous narrative about individual characters: the wiki is sparse and nearly everything describes the group, not each member. According to that translation, Ryko would be Jain's dog and Rinyan Lumina's cat; Raiden is an infiltrator who wants the conflict ended and Minerva an apprentice mage with an owl. The guides do not confirm that. That the Twilightsworn banish Lightsworn monsters and that the Lightsworn send cards to the GY in the End Phase are game rules; the wiki ties only the End Phase milling to the magic cost, and links the banishing to no story. Not covered: the anime (ARC-V appears in the wiki's infobox with no plot attached) and the OCG name Lightroad. No further creator pieces are linked."}},{"slug":"live-evil-twin","kind":"archetype","name":"Live☆Twin and Evil★Twin","badge":{"es":"Streamers de día, ladronas fantasma de noche","en":"Streamers by day, phantom thieves by night"},"origin":{"es":"Historias de las cartas: Valuable Book EX, EX 3 y EX 5","en":"Card storylines: Valuable Book EX, EX 3 and EX 5"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Live☆Twin: las streamers traviesas","en":"Live☆Twin: the impish streamers"},"p":{"es":"Para el público son Live☆Twin, un dúo de streamers muy popular cuya premisa es ser angelitos traviesos que subieron del inframundo para ser lo más tiernas. Triunfan porque nunca hacen las cosas a medias y porque su aspecto choca con su forma de hablar. Ki-sikil ama los zapatos, el baile y los animales, y por sus disfraces extravagantes la ven como una rara entre los demonios. Lil-la prefiere los tiburones, el dinero y las visitas, y hace disfraces feos, asquerosos y tiernos a la vez.","en":"To the public they are Live☆Twin, a hugely popular streamer duo whose premise is being impish angels who ascended from the underworld to be the cutest. They succeed because they never half-do their projects and because their looks clash with how they talk. Ki-sikil loves shoes, dancing and animals, and because of her wacky costumes she is seen as something of a weirdo among demons. Lil-la prefers sharks, money and views, and makes costumes that are ugly, gross and cute all at once."},"cards":["Live☆Twin Ki-sikil","Live☆Twin Lil-la"]},{"h":{"es":"El sitio y los disfraces virales","en":"The site and the viral costumes"},"p":{"es":"Live☆Twin Home es la página de acceso de su canal, con una animación que recibe quejas porque estorba, y Live☆Twin Channel es la página principal, donde tienen fama de esforzarse de más. Ahí despegan con disfraces: Ki-sikil prefiere ropa tierna, pero Lil-la la enreda con disfraces de payaso, y Lil-la tiene como pasatiempo fabricar los suyos. Gracias a cómo los modela Ki-sikil se vuelven virales y se acercan a ser número 1 en el ranking mundial de streamers.","en":"Live☆Twin Home is their channel's log-in page, with an animation that gets complaints for being in the way, and Live☆Twin Channel is the homepage, where they are known as tryhards. There they take off with costumes: Ki-sikil prefers cute clothes, but Lil-la talks her into clown costumes, and Lil-la has a hobby of making her own. Thanks to how Ki-sikil models them they go viral and get closer to being number 1 in the World Streamer Rankings."},"cards":["Live☆Twin Home","Live☆Twin Ki-sikil Frost","Live☆Twin Lil-la Treat"]},{"h":{"es":"De noche: las ladronas Evil★Twin","en":"By night: the Evil★Twin thieves"},"p":{"es":"De noche, Live☆Twin es en realidad Evil★Twin, famosas ladronas fantasma. En el lado oscuro del mundo hay trabajos que se hacen aunque rompan la ley, y para eso se contratan agentes libres, el plan B de agencias de inteligencia que no quieren que nada las vincule. Evil★Twin subió como un cometa en el ranking mundial de agentes y se motiva más si el objetivo es algo tierno, como las joyas. Su ropa tiene generadores holográficos que arman atuendos de ladrona.","en":"By night, Live☆Twin is really Evil★Twin, infamous phantom thieves. In the world's dark underbelly some jobs get done even if they break the law, and for that Free Agents are hired, the plan B of intelligence agencies who want no trace leading back to them. Evil★Twin climbed the World Agent Rankings at comet speed and gets more motivated if the target is something cute, like jewelry. Their clothes have holographic generators that create phantom thief outfits."},"cards":["Evil★Twin Ki-sikil","Evil★Twin Lil-la"]},{"h":{"es":"El pedido de la Gran Joya","en":"The Big Jewel request"},"p":{"es":"Los pedidos solo llegan por el canal de streaming, que sirve de camuflaje. Últimamente se siente que la administración del sitio se puso más agresiva. En este trabajo les tocó robar la Gran Joya, que se compra y se vende por vías poco legales. Estaba custodiada con seguridad muy estricta, pero para ellas fue facilísimo, más fácil que decidir las miniaturas de los videos.","en":"Requests can only be made through their streamer channel, which serves as camouflage. Lately it feels as if the site's management has become more aggressive. This time the job was to take the Big Jewel, a prize traded through shady channels. It was guarded by very strict security, but for them it was super easy, simpler than picking thumbnails for their videos."},"cards":["Secret Password","Evil★Twin Challenge","Evil★Twin GG EZ"]},{"h":{"es":"Un rap con Magicaluna (EX 3)","en":"A rap with Magicaluna (EX 3)"},"p":{"es":"En una transmisión posterior, Live☆Twin lanza un desafío de rap con Magicaluna como invitada y pide que se suscriban. El chat se divide: alguien nota que Lil-la tartamudeó, otros celebran el beatbox, uno dice que Sunny es más tierna y otro pide más estrellas. Un espectador descifra la letra: si querés un duelo, vengan; lo volverán viral, y los comentarios negativos solo alimentan el contenido. El número se llama Lil-la Rap.","en":"In a later stream, Live☆Twin sets a rap challenge with Magicaluna as a guest and asks viewers to subscribe. The chat splits: someone notes Lil-la stuttered, others praise the beatboxing, one says Sunny is cuter and another asks for more stars. A viewer deciphers the lyrics: if a Duel is what you want, bring it, they will make it viral, and negative comments only fuel content. The number is called Lil-la Rap."},"cards":["Lil-la Rap"]},{"h":{"es":"Rivales y crisis de Live☆Twin (EX 5)","en":"Rivals and a Live☆Twin crisis (EX 5)"},"p":{"es":"Los rankings de streamers entran en una etapa turbulenta y el reinado del dúo empieza a ceder ante otros géneros. Lil-la teme a los M-Warrior, que resuelven todo con músculos; a Zombina y Zombino, los únicos ya muertos del rubro; y a Lady Sunny con Magicaluna, siempre en polémicas. Para el próximo evento planea el atuendo y la pose definitivos, pero sin verse desesperada, porque eso no es tierno: tiene que ser algo frío y sin emoción.","en":"The Streamer Rankings enter a turbulent stretch and the duo's reign begins to give way to other genres. Lil-la fears the M-Warriors, who solve everything with muscle; Zombina and Zombino, the only ones in the business already dead; and Lady Sunny with Magicaluna, always mired in controversy. For the next event she plans the ultimate outfit and pose, but without looking desperate, since that is not cute: it has to be cold and unemotional."},"cards":["Live☆Twin Lil-la"]},{"h":{"es":"La racha de Evil★Twin (EX 5)","en":"Evil★Twin's slump (EX 5)"},"p":{"es":"El mundo criminal también cambió. Evil★Twin llegó a ser número 2 en el ranking de agentes, pero ahora anda por el puesto 200. Ki-sikil se preocupa porque no entran encargos: antes su nombre equivalía a gobernar el hampa e incluso la contraseña secreta valía como moneda de cambio. Decide ir con todo en el próximo trabajo, un pedido de un viejo conocido, un mensajero, que toca un lado todavía más turbio del hampa. Cuanto más peligroso es el trabajo, más dulce la recompensa.","en":"The criminal world has shifted too. Evil★Twin once reached number 2 in the agent rankings, but now floats around the 200 range. Ki-sikil worries because no gigs come in: their name used to equal ruling the underworld, and even their secret password was a bargaining chip. She decides to go all out on the next job, a request from a courier she used to know, touching an even shadier side of the underworld. The more dangerous the job, the sweeter the reward."},"cards":["Evil★Twin Ki-sikil","Secret Password"]},{"h":{"es":"Trabajo principal o pasatiempo (EX 5)","en":"Main job or side gig (EX 5)"},"p":{"es":"Todo se complica porque las dos no coinciden en qué es lo principal. Ki-sikil se deja convencer con facilidad por Lil-la, que quiere darlo todo como streamer, y Lil-la insiste en que cada día tienen menos trabajo como agentes. El relato deja ese conflicto abierto, sin decir cuál de las dos actividades terminan priorizando ni cómo les va en el pedido del mensajero.","en":"Everything gets complicated because the two disagree on which is the main job. Ki-sikil is easily swayed by Lil-la, who wants to give it all as a streamer, and Lil-la keeps pointing out that they get less work as agents each day. The story leaves that conflict open, without saying which of the two activities they end up putting first or how the courier's request goes."},"cards":["Evil★Twin Lil-la","Evil★Twin Ki-sikil"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia (YGOrganization)","title":"[VBEX Lore] Number 4: Live☆Twin & Evil★Twin","url":"https://ygorganization.com/vbex-lore-number-4-live%E2%98%86twin-evil%E2%98%85twin","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de esta historia de la Valuable Book EX, para leerla completa","en":"English translation of this Valuable Book EX story, to read it in full"}},{"author":"NeoArkadia (YGOrganization)","title":"Story 08: The Frustrations of the Live☆Twins & Evil★Twins [VBEX5]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-08-the-frustrations-of-the-live%e2%98%86twins-evil%e2%98%85twins-vbex5/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de la secuela de la Valuable Book EX 5, con la crisis de las dos identidades","en":"English translation of the Valuable Book EX 5 sequel, covering the crisis of both identities"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Evil★Twin","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Evil★Twin","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Live☆Twin","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Live☆Twin","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 3 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_3_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los primeros cuatro bloques son de la Valuable Book EX; el quinto es una transmisión de la Valuable Book EX 3 y los últimos tres son la secuela de la Valuable Book EX 5. La wiki no fecha el rap respecto de la secuela. La historia termina sin resolver la crisis ni el pedido del mensajero.","en":"The first four blocks are from the Valuable Book EX; the fifth is a stream from the Valuable Book EX 3 and the last three are the Valuable Book EX 5 sequel. The wiki does not date the rap relative to the sequel. The story ends without resolving the crisis or the courier's request."}},{"slug":"machina","kind":"archetype","name":"Machina","badge":{"es":"El arsenal viejo despierta contra la generación nueva","en":"The old arsenal wakes up against the new generation"},"origin":{"es":"The Valuable Book EX (guía oficial de historias de cartas)","en":"The Valuable Book EX (official card storylines guide)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Las armas nuevas relevan a las viejas","en":"New weapons relieve the old ones"},"p":{"es":"Los Machina son cuerpos blindados que pelean en territorios en disputa. Cuanto más se agravan los conflictos, más dinero juntan los gobiernos para armarlos. Machina Fortress, un arma de nueva generación, se fabrica en serie y toma el lugar de los Machina anteriores en la línea de fuego. Esos modelos viejos, dañados en batallas pasadas, como Machina Soldier y Machina Defender, se guardan inactivos en el arsenal, donde se suponía que dormirían para siempre.","en":"The Machina are armored corps fighting in disputed territories. The worse the conflicts get, the more money governments pool to arm them. Machina Fortress, a new-generation weapon, is built in volume and takes the previous Machina's place on the firing line. Those old models, damaged in earlier battles, such as Machina Soldier and Machina Defender, are stored inactive in the arsenal, where they were supposed to sleep forever."},"cards":["Machina Fortress","Machina Soldier","Machina Defender"]},{"h":{"es":"Una generación armada a partir de Fortress","en":"A generation built on Fortress"},"p":{"es":"Los datos de combate de las Fortress sirven para construir Machina Citadel, un arma de última tecnología pensada para decidir los combates. Machina Air Raider recicla la tecnología de la Fortress, y esa unidad y Machina Irradiator pueden acoplarse a ella. Machina Redeployment completa el equipo: está hecha para llevar por aire a Machina y Fortress a zonas de operaciones, les da energía y la elogiaron por su adaptabilidad. Con todo esto en pie, enfrentan a un enemigo nuevo.","en":"The Fortresses' combat data is used to build Machina Citadel, a cutting-edge weapon meant to decide battles. Machina Air Raider recycles the Fortress's technology, and that unit and Machina Irradiator can link up with it. Machina Redeployment completes the kit: it is built to carry Machina and Fortresses by air into operation zones, feeds them power, and drew praise for its adaptability. With all this in place, they face a new enemy."},"cards":["Machina Air Raider","Machina Irradiator","Machina Redeployment"]},{"h":{"es":"Un intruso en el depósito","en":"An intruder in the depot"},"p":{"es":"El nuevo enemigo no viene del frente: el Unauthorized Bootup Device, una forma de vida mecánica autónoma y compacta, se mete en el depósito de armas. Allí se prende desde afuera a los Machina inactivos y los hace funcionar a la fuerza. Según el arte secreto, parasita a las máquinas dormidas tomando por completo esa función, y las cartas Unauthorized Reactivation y Machina Possesstorage lo reflejan.","en":"The new enemy does not come from the front: the Unauthorized Bootup Device, an autonomous, compact mechanical lifeform, slips into the weapons depot. There it latches onto the inactive Machina from outside and makes them run by force. According to the secret artwork notes, it parasitizes the dormant machines by taking over that function completely, and the cards Unauthorized Reactivation and Machina Possesstorage reflect it."},"cards":["Unauthorized Bootup Device","Unauthorized Reactivation","Machina Possesstorage"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Machina contra los Machina","en":"Machina against Machina"},"p":{"es":"Los Machina reactivados, ya bajo el mando del dispositivo, se vuelven contra el ejército que antes los usaba. El cuerpo de Citadel debería ganarles sin problema a esos modelos de tecnología vieja, pero el dispositivo les multiplica el rendimiento varios órdenes de magnitud y pueden pelear de igual a igual con las máquinas más modernas. El resultado es que los conflictos se agravan todavía más.","en":"The reactivated Machina, now under the device's command, turn on the army that used to field them. Citadel's corps should beat those old-technology models easily, but the device multiplies their output by several orders of magnitude and they can fight on equal terms with the most modern machines. The result is that the conflicts get even worse."},"cards":["Machina Citadel"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness","title":"[VBEX] Number 9: Machina","url":"https://ygorganization.com/warwarneverchanges/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"La historia traducida con las cartas en orden y las notas de diseño de las ilustraciones secretas.","en":"The storyline translated with the cards in order and design notes on the secret artwork."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"El relato sale de la historia oficial de Machina en The Valuable Book EX; las cartas no cuentan una trama por sí solas. La guía no da nombres de personajes: los protagonistas son las máquinas. Aquí el orden está reagrupado: el retiro de los modelos viejos va antes de Citadel, para que el intruso aparezca después de las armas nuevas. Las notas del arte secreto vienen de la misma página.","en":"The account comes from the official Machina storyline in The Valuable Book EX; the cards do not tell a plot on their own. The guide gives no character names: the machines are the protagonists. The order is regrouped here: the retirement of the old models comes before Citadel, so the intruder appears after the new weapons. The secret artwork notes come from the same page."}},{"slug":"magellanica","kind":"archetype","name":"Magellanica","badge":{"es":"La ciudad submarina de las artes y el debut de una diva","en":"The deep sea city of the arts and a diva's debut"},"origin":{"es":"The Valuable Book EX (guía oficial de historias de cartas)","en":"The Valuable Book EX (official card storylines guide)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Una ciudad de artistas en el fondo","en":"An artists' city on the seabed"},"p":{"es":"En lo más profundo del mar, vedado a quienes caminan en tierra, los que prefieren las aguas administran una ciudad en la que nacieron la música, la pintura, la arquitectura y muchas otras artes. Es Magellanica, the Deep Sea City. Se rumorea que monstruos de otras zonas del océano la visitan solo por lo hermoso de sus calles y edificios.","en":"At the very bottom of the sea, off limits to anyone who walks on land, those who favor the waters run a city where music, painting, architecture and many other arts were born. It is Magellanica, the Deep Sea City. Rumor has it that monsters from other parts of the ocean visit it just for the beauty of its streets and buildings."},"cards":["Magellanica, the Deep Sea City"]},{"h":{"es":"La sala de música y sus artistas","en":"The music hall and its artists"},"p":{"es":"En el centro de la ciudad se construyó una sala de música soberbia, el símbolo de la capital de las artes. Los músicos acuáticos entrenan todos los días con la esperanza de actuar allí algún día. Entre los artistas de Magellanica figuran Deep Sea Diva, Deep Sea Minstrel y Guitar Gurnards Duonigis. Una de ellas, Diva, llegará a pararse en ese escenario.","en":"In the middle of the city stands a superb music hall, the symbol of the capital of the arts. Water musicians train daily, hoping to perform there one day. Among the artists of Magellanica are Deep Sea Diva, Deep Sea Minstrel and Guitar Gurnards Duonigis. One of them, Diva, will get to stand on that stage."},"cards":["Deep Sea Diva","Deep Sea Minstrel","Guitar Gurnards Duonigis"]},{"h":{"es":"Un regalo de la infancia","en":"A gift from childhood"},"p":{"es":"Deep Sea Artisan es un artesano en ascenso que abrió un taller modesto en Magellanica. Todavía no se hizo un nombre, pero su habilidad es auténtica. Se rumorea que puso todo su esfuerzo en una sola pieza, un regalo para su amiga de la infancia, la que llegaría a ser la Prima Donna. Esa pieza son los accesorios que hace para Diva, y con ellos ella se acerca a ese escenario.","en":"Deep Sea Artisan is a rising craftsman who opened a modest workshop in Magellanica. He has not made a name for himself yet, but his skill is the real deal. Rumor has it that he put all his effort into a single piece, a present for his childhood friend, the one who would become the Prima Donna. That piece is the accessories he makes for Diva, and with them she moves closer to that stage."},"cards":["Deep Sea Artisan"]},{"h":{"es":"La noche de la Prima Donna","en":"The Prima Donna's night"},"p":{"es":"Un día llega una noticia que revoluciona a los artistas del fondo del mar: a Diva por fin le permiten pararse en la sala de música. Con los accesorios que, según se dice, le dio su amiga de la infancia, la apariencia de niña desaparece y su voz hermosa y cautivante conquista a todo el público. Eso abre un capítulo nuevo para las artes del mar profundo, y ella es Deep Sea Prima Donna.","en":"One day news arrives that stirs up the artists of the deep sea: Diva is finally allowed to stand in the music hall. Wearing the accessories she reportedly received from her childhood friend, the look of a young girl disappears, and her beautiful, captivating singing voice wins over the whole audience. That opens a new chapter for the arts of the deep sea, and she is Deep Sea Prima Donna."},"cards":["Deep Sea Prima Donna"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness","title":"[VBEX] Number 7: Magellanica, the Deep Sea City","url":"https://ygorganization.com/underdasea/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"El relato traducido con la ilustración de cada carta y las descripciones de Diva, Minstrel y Duonigis.","en":"The storyline translated, with each card's artwork and descriptions of Diva, Minstrel and Duonigis."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"El relato sale de la historia oficial de Magellanica en The Valuable Book EX y termina con el debut de Deep Sea Prima Donna. Diva, Minstrel y Duonigis aparecen sin más detalle porque el texto de Yugipedia solo los nombra; el artículo enlazado sí los describe. En la página, Artisan se presenta después del debut de Diva; aquí va antes para contar primero el regalo y después la noche en que Diva lo luce.","en":"The account comes from the official Magellanica storyline in The Valuable Book EX and ends with Deep Sea Prima Donna's debut. Diva, Minstrel and Duonigis appear without further detail because the Yugipedia text only names them; the linked article does describe them. On the page, Artisan is introduced after Diva's debut; here he comes first so the gift is told before the night Diva wears it."}},{"slug":"marik-ishtar","kind":"character","name":"Marik Ishtar","badge":{"es":"De vengador del Faraón a guardián de su tumba","en":"From avenger of the Pharaoh to keeper of his tomb"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (anime y manga)","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (anime and manga)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Los Ishtar y el origen de Yami Marik (anime)","en":"The Ishtars and the origin of Yami Marik (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, la familia Ishtar custodia por generaciones la tumba del Faraón y dos Millennium Items, el Rod y el Necklace. A Marik no lo dejan salir, y cuando lo obligan al ritual de iniciación de Tombkeeper, el dolor da origen a su otra personalidad, Yami Marik. Un año después, tras una salida prohibida a la superficie, su padre castiga a Odion y Yami Marik emerge, toma el Rod y mata al padre. Odion sella a Yami Marik dentro de Marik y le dice que lo mató Shadi. Marik culpa al Faraón y funda los Rare Hunters.","en":"In the anime, the Ishtar family guards the Pharaoh's tomb and two Millennium Items, the Rod and the Necklace, across generations. Marik is not allowed to leave, and when he is forced through the Tombkeeper initiation ritual, the pain gives rise to his other personality, Yami Marik. A year later, after a forbidden trip to the surface, his father punishes Odion and Yami Marik emerges, takes the Rod and kills the father. Odion seals Yami Marik inside Marik and tells him Shadi did it. Marik blames the Pharaoh and founds the Rare Hunters."},"cards":["Millennium Necklace (Skill Card)"]},{"h":{"es":"Rare Hunters y el God Five de Strings (anime)","en":"The Rare Hunters and Strings' God Five (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Marik lidera a los Rare Hunters: con el Rod quiere las tres God Cards para usar su poder, ser el nuevo Faraón y liberar a su familia, y vengarse del Faraón sin nombre. Sus hombres hallan Slifer y Ra donde las escondió Pegasus, pero Ishizu le da Obelisk a Kaiba. En Battle City, Marik controla a Strings, que arma el God Five con Slifer, Revival Jam, Jam Defender, Card of Safe Return e Infinite Cards. Yami Yugi y Kaiba ven el fallo: con Brain Control, Yami Yugi se queda con Revival Jam y Strings pierde por Deck Out.","en":"Marik leads the Rare Hunters: with the Rod he wants the three God Cards to use their power, become the new Pharaoh and free his family, and to take revenge on the Nameless Pharaoh. His men find Slifer and Ra where Pegasus hid them, but Ishizu gives Obelisk to Kaiba. In Battle City, Marik controls Strings, who sets up the God Five with Slifer, Revival Jam, Jam Defender, Card of Safe Return and Infinite Cards. Yami Yugi and Kaiba spot the flaw: with Brain Control, Yami Yugi takes Revival Jam and Strings loses by Deck Out."},"cards":["Revival Jam","Card of Safe Return","Brain Control"]},{"h":{"es":"Namu, Joey y el Ra falso (anime)","en":"Namu, Joey and the counterfeit Ra (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Marik usa el Rod para controlar a Joey y a Téa y enfrentarlos a Yami Yugi, con un mazo de Joey que incluye cartas prohibidas por las reglas de Battle City, como Hinotama y Raigeki. Joey se libera con su fuerza de voluntad. Marik se hace pasar por Namu y pone a Odion a jugar como Marik en los cuartos de final. Contra Joey, Odion invoca un Ra falso para demostrar quién es y el verdadero Ra, furioso, los fulmina a ambos. Odion revela la verdad y Marik se muestra, hasta que sus dolores de cabeza lo dejan en manos de Yami Marik.","en":"Marik uses the Rod to control Joey and Téa and set them against Yami Yugi, with a Joey Deck that includes cards banned by the Battle City rules, such as Hinotama and Raigeki. Joey breaks free through willpower. Marik poses as Namu and has Odion play as Marik in the quarter-finals. Against Joey, Odion uses a counterfeit Ra to prove who he is, and the real Ra, enraged, strikes them both with lightning. Odion reveals the truth and Marik shows himself, until his headaches leave him in Yami Marik's hands."},"cards":["Hinotama","Raigeki","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"Yami Marik en Battle City (anime)","en":"Yami Marik in Battle City (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Yami Marik despierta cuando Odion cae inconsciente. Cambia el mazo de Marik y descubre los poderes ocultos de Ra. En un Shadow Game contra Mai, donde cada Life Point perdido borra recuerdos, ella consigue a Ra, pero queda bloqueado en Sphere Mode; Yami Marik lo libera y deja el alma de Mai atrapada en un reloj de arena. Luego, tras ver el duelo de Ishizu y Kaiba, Yami Bakura se hace con Ra mediante Exchange; Yami Marik trae de vuelta a Ra con Monster Reborn, le transfiere casi todos sus Life Points y se queda con el Millennium Ring.","en":"Yami Marik wakes when Odion falls unconscious. He changes Marik's Deck and learns Ra's hidden powers. In a Shadow Game against Mai, where each lost Life Point erases memories, she gets hold of Ra, but it is locked in Sphere Mode; Yami Marik frees it and leaves Mai's soul trapped in an hourglass. Later, after watching Ishizu and Kaiba's Duel, Yami Bakura takes Ra with Exchange; Yami Marik brings Ra back with Monster Reborn, transfers almost all his Life Points to it and takes the Millennium Ring."},"cards":["The Winged Dragon of Ra - Sphere Mode","Monster Reborn"]},{"h":{"es":"La final y la redención de Marik (anime)","en":"The final and Marik's redemption (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En la final, Yami Marik convierte el duelo en un Shadow Game: cada Life Point que pierde Yami Yugi desvanece a Yugi y los de Yami Marik desvanecen al Marik original. Ra destruye a Slifer, Yami Yugi usa Fiend's Sanctuary, Obelisk golpea y Yami Marik crea Egyptian God Slime. Con el aliento de Odion, Marik acepta su deber de Tombkeeper, domina a su lado oscuro y se retira, destruyendo a Yami Marik. Le entrega el Rod y Ra al Faraón y vuelve a Egipto, desde donde después guía a Yugi hasta la Tablet of Memories.","en":"In the final, Yami Marik turns the Duel into a Shadow Game: each Life Point Yami Yugi loses fades Yugi away, and Yami Marik's fade the original Marik. Ra destroys Slifer, Yami Yugi uses Fiend's Sanctuary, Obelisk strikes and Yami Marik creates Egyptian God Slime. Encouraged by Odion, Marik accepts his duty as a Tombkeeper, overpowers his dark side and forfeits, destroying Yami Marik. He gives the Pharaoh the Rod and Ra and returns to Egypt, from where he later leads Yugi to the Tablet of Memories."},"cards":["Egyptian God Slime","Fiend's Sanctuary","Slifer the Sky Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"La familia Ishtar y la venganza (manga)","en":"The Ishtar family and the revenge (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Marik crece bajo tierra con Ishizu y el sirviente Rishid. Poco antes de cumplir diez años le espera el rito que graba en su espalda los secretos del rey; pide que Rishid lo haga por él, pero el padre se niega, y el afecto de Rishid sella a Dark Marik. Tras una salida a la superficie, el padre castiga a Rishid, Dark Marik emerge y lo mata. Shadi dice que fue voluntad del faraón y Marik funda los Ghouls. Roban Slifer y Ra, pero Ishizu guarda Obelisk. Con falsas God Cards, los Ghouls enloquecen o mueren.","en":"In the manga, Marik grows up underground with Ishizu and the servant Rishid. Shortly before he turns ten, the rite that carves the king's secrets into his back awaits him; he asks Rishid to take it for him, but the father refuses, and Rishid's devotion seals Dark Marik away. After a trip to the surface, the father punishes Rishid, Dark Marik emerges and kills him. Shadi says it was the pharaoh's will and Marik founds the Ghouls. They steal Slifer and Ra, but Ishizu keeps Obelisk. With counterfeit God Cards, Ghouls go mad or die."},"cards":["Obelisk the Tormentor"]},{"h":{"es":"Battle City: Slifer y el muelle (manga)","en":"Battle City: Slifer and the pier (manga)"},"p":{"es":"Marik envía a Doll, un Rare Hunter bajo control total, a enfrentarse a Dark Yugi con Slifer. Con Jam Breeding Machine arma el God Five, pero Dark Yugi toma control de Revival Jam y Marik pierde por Deck Out. Pacta con Dark Bakura, se hace pasar por Namu y controla a Jonouchi para que se enfrente a Yugi, esposados a un ancla con una bomba. Jonouchi desobedece y no toma Red-Eyes Black Dragon con Exchange. Marik lo fuerza a jugar Meteor of Destruction, pero Yugi se elige como objetivo y Jonouchi, ya libre, lo salva.","en":"Marik uses Doll, a fully controlled Rare Hunter, to Duel Dark Yugi with Slifer. With Jam Breeding Machine he sets up the God Five, but Dark Yugi takes control of Revival Jam and Marik loses by Deck Out. He strikes a deal with Dark Bakura, poses as Namu and controls Jonouchi so he Duels Yugi while handcuffed to an anchor rigged with a bomb. Jonouchi disobeys and does not take Red-Eyes Black Dragon with Exchange. Marik forces him to play Meteor of Destruction, but Yugi picks himself as the target and Jonouchi, now free, saves him."},"cards":["Jam Breeding Machine","Red-Eyes Black Dragon","Meteor of Destruction"]},{"h":{"es":"La Battle Ship y el final (manga)","en":"The Battle Ship and the ending (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En la Battle Ship, Marik asesora desde la mente de Bakura a Dark Bakura, que arma un combo de Destiny Board con Dark Necrofear y pierde ante Dark Yugi. Rishid juega como Marik contra Jonouchi y Marik le cuela un Ra falso; el verdadero Ra los fulmina y Dark Marik toma el control. Por Anzu, Marik se entera de que Dark Marik mató a su padre. En la final con Dark Yugi, Marik se impone con ayuda de Rishid, se retira y destruye a Dark Marik. Entrega el Rod y a Ra y vuelve a Egipto. Con Ishizu y Rishid lleva después a Yugi al Rite of the Duel.","en":"On the Battle Ship, Marik advises Dark Bakura from inside Bakura's mind; Dark Bakura builds a Destiny Board combo with Dark Necrofear and loses to Dark Yugi. Rishid plays as Marik against Jonouchi and Marik slips a counterfeit Ra into his Deck; the real Ra strikes them down and Dark Marik takes control. Through Anzu, Marik learns that Dark Marik killed his father. In the final against Dark Yugi, Marik prevails with Rishid's help, forfeits and destroys Dark Marik. He hands over the Rod and Ra and returns to Egypt. With Ishizu and Rishid he later leads Yugi to the Rite of the Duel."},"cards":["Destiny Board","Dark Necrofear"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Marik Ishtar","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Marik_Ishtar","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yami Marik","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yami_Marik","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Marik Ishtar (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Marik_Ishtar_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los bloques siguen el anime y el manga por separado: cambian los nombres (Odion y Yami Marik en el anime, Rishid y Dark Marik en el manga) y los duelos. Millennium Necklace (Skill Card) es una ilustración de Skill Card de videojuego, no una carta impresa. Los videojuegos no se cubren. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido sobre este lore que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The blocks follow the anime and the manga separately: names change (Odion and Yami Marik in the anime, Rishid and Dark Marik in the manga) and so do the Duels. Millennium Necklace (Skill Card) is a video-game Skill Card illustration, not a printed card. Video games are not covered. We did not find a content-creator piece on this lore that could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"maximillion-pegasus","kind":"character","name":"Maximillion J. Pegasus","badge":{"es":"El creador de Duel Monsters que buscó recuperar a su amada","en":"The creator of Duel Monsters who sought to bring back his love"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (anime y manga) y los juegos de cartas","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! (anime and manga) and the card game"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Cecelia y el Millennium Eye (anime)","en":"Cecelia and the Millennium Eye (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Cecelia muere de una enfermedad a los 17 años, y Pegasus, que la conoció en una fiesta de su padre, un empresario de Las Vegas, catorce años antes de Duelist Kingdom y solía pintarla (en el doblaje se casaron), no se resigna. Recorre el mundo buscando cómo traerla de vuelta y en Egipto lo intriga la idea de una vida después de la muerte. Shadi le advierte que no hallará nada, pero Pegasus lo sigue a un templo subterráneo, donde lo someten a la prueba del Millennium Eye. Con el Eye en la cuenca izquierda, ve a Cecelia un instante y la abraza.","en":"In the anime, Cecelia dies of an illness at 17, and Pegasus, who met her at a party his father, a Las Vegas businessman, threw fourteen years before Duelist Kingdom and used to paint her (in the dub they married), cannot accept it. He roams the world for a way to bring her back, and in Egypt the idea of life after death intrigues him. Shadi warns him he will find nothing, but Pegasus follows him to an underground temple, where he is put through the Millennium Eye's test. With the Eye in his left socket, he sees Cecelia for a moment and hugs her."},"cards":["Millennium Eye (Skill Card)"]},{"h":{"es":"Duel Monsters y las God Cards (anime)","en":"Duel Monsters and the God Cards (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Con el Eye, Pegasus se obsesiona con los antiguos Shadow Games. Funda Industrial Illusions y lanza en Estados Unidos Duel Monsters, un juego que traslada a cartas aquellos Duelos antiguos; los Millennium Items conservan su poder sobre ellas como lo tenían sobre las piedras. En un segundo viaje, Shadi lo lleva a una cámara subterránea con una tablilla de las Egyptian Gods y Pegasus crea las God Cards a partir de ella. Un sueño donde esas deidades arrasan una ciudad egipcia, con Shadi avisándole, lo asusta. Vuelve a Egipto y le pide a Ishizu Ishtar que entierre las God Cards en la tumba del Faraón.","en":"With the Eye, Pegasus becomes obsessed with the ancient Shadow Games. He founds Industrial Illusions and launches Duel Monsters in the United States, a game that moves those ancient Duels onto cards; the Millennium Items keep their power over them as they had over the stones. On a second trip, Shadi takes him to an underground chamber with a tablet of the Egyptian Gods and Pegasus makes the God Cards from it. A dream in which those deities destroy an Egyptian city, with Shadi warning him, frightens him. He returns to Egypt and has Ishizu Ishtar bury the God Cards in the Pharaoh's tomb."},"cards":["Slifer the Sky Dragon","Obelisk the Tormentor","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"Kaiba, Keith y el plan contra Yugi (anime)","en":"Kaiba, Keith and the plan against Yugi (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Pegasus recibe de Seto Kaiba una propuesta para desarrollar arenas de Duelo. La acepta mientras un chico llamado Sam, guiado por notas que Pegasus escribe leyendo la mente de Bandit Keith con el Eye, humilla a Keith en la final de un torneo. También aprueba Dungeon Dice Monsters, de Duke Devlin, y le agrega en secreto a Dark Magician. Cuando Yugi derrota a Kaiba, pacta con los Big Five para derrocarlo y planea Duelist Kingdom para vencer a Yugi. Quiere usar el Solid Vision de KaibaCorp para crear una Cecelia holográfica (en el doblaje, para revivirla).","en":"Pegasus receives a proposal from Seto Kaiba to develop Dueling Arenas. He accepts it while a boy named Sam, following notes Pegasus writes by reading Bandit Keith's mind with the Eye, humiliates Keith in a tournament final. He also approves Duke Devlin's Dungeon Dice Monsters and secretly adds Dark Magician to it. When Yugi defeats Kaiba, he strikes a deal with the Big Five to overthrow him and plans Duelist Kingdom to beat Yugi. He wants to use KaibaCorp's Solid Vision to create a holographic Cecelia (in the dub, to revive her)."},"cards":["Dark Magician"]},{"h":{"es":"Duelist Kingdom: la derrota (anime)","en":"Duelist Kingdom: the defeat (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Por videocinta, Pegasus vence a Yugi en un Duelo y le roba el alma a su abuelo Solomon como Penalty Game, para obligarlo a ir a la isla. Allí sella el alma de Mokuba en una carta Soul Prison y, leyendo la mente de Kaiba, también lo derrota. Contra Yugi y Yami Yugi, el Eye le da ventaja hasta que ellos usan el Mind Shuffle. Tras caer Toon World, Pegasus los arrastra a un Shadow Game, pero Yami Yugi gana. Pegasus libera las almas y, debilitado, pierde un Shadow Game contra Yami Bakura, que se queda con el Eye y lo deja en coma.","en":"By videotape, Pegasus beats Yugi in a Duel and steals the soul of his grandfather Solomon as a Penalty Game, to force him onto the island. There he seals Mokuba's soul in a Soul Prison card and, reading Kaiba's mind, defeats him too. Against Yugi and Yami Yugi, the Eye gives him an edge until they use Mind Shuffle. After Toon World falls, Pegasus drags them into a Shadow Game, but Yami Yugi wins. Pegasus frees the souls and, weakened, loses a Shadow Game to Yami Bakura, who takes the Eye and leaves him in a coma."},"cards":["Toon World"]},{"h":{"es":"Waking the Dragons y GX (anime)","en":"Waking the Dragons and GX (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En Waking the Dragons, Pegasus averigua las verdaderas intenciones de Paradius, avisa a Yugi y le da Legend of Heart, clave para vencer a Dartz. Mai le quita el alma, que recupera al final del arco. En GX contrata a Chumley por su carta Ayers Rock Sunrise. Sigue a Franz, que robó la última copia de The Winged Dragon of Ra, hasta Duel Academy y ve a Jaden salvar al monstruo. Gana un Triangle Duel donde aparece Toon Kingdom. Con la academia en otra dimensión, crea en el momento Rainbow Dragon para Jesse. En 5D's, una fundación con su nombre sugiere que murió.","en":"In Waking the Dragons, Pegasus learns Paradius's true intentions, warns Yugi and gives him Legend of Heart, key to beating Dartz. Mai takes his soul, and it comes back before the arc ends. In GX he hires Chumley for his card Ayers Rock Sunrise. He follows Franz, who stole the last copy of The Winged Dragon of Ra, to Duel Academy and watches Jaden save the monster. He wins a Triangle Duel in which Toon Kingdom appears. With the academy trapped in another dimension, he creates Rainbow Dragon on the spot for Jesse. In 5D's, a foundation bearing his name suggests he died."},"cards":["Legend of Heart","Ayers Rock Sunrise","Rainbow Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Cyndia y el origen de Duel Monsters (manga)","en":"Cyndia and the origin of Duel Monsters (manga)"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, el padre de Pegasus administra casinos. A los 10 años conoce a Cyndia, hija de un amigo de su padre, y se prometen una vida juntos. Ella muere a los 17 y él cae en una depresión. En Egipto ve cómo el Millennium Ring mata a un ladrón; lo descubren y le arrancan el ojo izquierdo para ponerle el Millennium Eye. Pasa la prueba y Cyndia lo abraza. De las leyendas de magos que sellaban monstruos en tablillas surge Duel Monsters. Crea las Egyptian Gods, se arrepiente y las manda enterrar. Según el spin-off Yu-Gi-Oh! R, diseñó los Wicked Gods y no los creó.","en":"In the manga, Pegasus's father manages casinos. At 10 he meets Cyndia, the daughter of a friend of his father, and they promise to share their lives. She dies at 17 and he falls into depression. In Egypt he watches the Millennium Ring kill a thief; he is caught and has his left eye cut out to set in the Millennium Eye. He passes the test and Cyndia embraces him. Legends of magicians who sealed monsters in tablets give rise to Duel Monsters. He makes the Egyptian Gods, regrets it and has them buried. According to the Yu-Gi-Oh! R spin-off, he designed the Wicked Gods but never made them."},"cards":["The Wicked Avatar","The Wicked Dreadroot","The Wicked Eraser"]},{"h":{"es":"KaibaCorp y Duelist Kingdom (manga)","en":"KaibaCorp and Duelist Kingdom (manga)"},"p":{"es":"Con Duel Monsters en auge, Pegasus acepta que KaibaCorp desarrolle Battle Boxes con él. Quiere el Solid Vision para proyectar a Cyndia, así que, con Kaiba en coma tras Death-T, pacta con los Big Five y arma Duelist Kingdom. Vence a Yugi por videocinta (sella el alma de Sugoroku) y, en la isla, sella a Mokuba en una Soul Prison. Contra Kaiba usa Dragon Capture Jar con Dragon Piper para capturar su Blue-Eyes y copia con Doppelganger el Crush Card Virus de Kaiba, que infecta el propio mazo de Kaiba. Su alma también termina presa.","en":"With Duel Monsters booming, Pegasus accepts KaibaCorp developing Battle Boxes with him. He wants Solid Vision to project Cyndia, so, with Kaiba in a coma after Death-T, he strikes a deal with the Big Five and sets up Duelist Kingdom. He beats Yugi by videotape (sealing Sugoroku's soul) and, on the island, seals Mokuba in a Soul Prison. Against Kaiba he uses Dragon Capture Jar with Dragon Piper to capture his Blue-Eyes and copies Kaiba's Crush Card Virus with Doppelganger, which infects Kaiba's own Deck. His soul ends up imprisoned too."},"cards":["Dragon Capture Jar","Dragon Piper","Crush Card Virus"]},{"h":{"es":"El Duelo final, la muerte y Project R.A. (manga)","en":"The final Duel, death and Project R.A. (manga)"},"p":{"es":"Contra Yugi y Dark Yugi, Pegasus sigue leyéndoles la mente hasta que ellos alternan turnos con el Mind Shuffle. Convierte el Duelo en Shadow Game y usa Relinquished para absorber monstruos, y Thousand-Eyes Restrict para paralizar al rival, pero un enjambre de Kuriboh explota dentro de sus ojos y pierde. Libera las almas, cuenta la historia de Cyndia y Dark Bakura le arranca el Eye, matándolo. Según Yu-Gi-Oh! R, su heredero Yako Tenma usa Project R.A. para revivirlo en el cuerpo de Anzu, pero Kaiba corta el servidor y el espíritu de Pegasus se desvanece.","en":"Against Yugi and Dark Yugi, Pegasus keeps reading their minds until they alternate turns with the Mind Shuffle. He turns the Duel into a Shadow Game and uses Relinquished to absorb monsters and Thousand-Eyes Restrict to paralyze his opponent, but a swarm of Kuriboh explodes inside its eyes and he loses. He frees the souls, tells the story of Cyndia and Dark Bakura pulls out his Eye, killing him. In Yu-Gi-Oh! R, his heir Yako Tenma uses Project R.A. to revive him in Anzu's body, but Kaiba cuts the server and Pegasus's spirit fades away."},"cards":["Relinquished","Thousand-Eyes Restrict","Kuriboh"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Maximillion Pegasus","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Maximillion_Pegasus","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Maximillion J. Pegasus (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Maximillion_J._Pegasus_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los bloques siguen el anime y el manga por separado: cambian los nombres (Cecelia en el anime, Cyndia en el manga) y los hechos (en el manga muere a manos de Dark Bakura). El final con Yako Tenma y Project R.A. y la línea de los Wicked Gods vienen del spin-off Yu-Gi-Oh! R, cuyo canon la wiki marca como discutido. Millennium Eye (Skill Card) es una ilustración de Skill Card de videojuego, no una carta impresa. Las películas y los videojuegos no se cubren. No encontramos una pieza de un creador de contenido sobre este lore que se pudiera abrir y comprobar, así que no se enlaza ninguna.","en":"The blocks follow the anime and the manga separately: names change (Cecelia in the anime, Cyndia in the manga) and so do events (in the manga he is killed by Dark Bakura). The ending with Yako Tenma and Project R.A. and the Wicked Gods line come from the Yu-Gi-Oh! R spin-off, whose canon the wiki marks as disputed. Millennium Eye (Skill Card) is a video-game Skill Card illustration, not a printed card. Movies and video games are not covered. We did not find a content-creator piece on this lore that could be opened and checked, so none is linked."}},{"slug":"ritual-beast","kind":"archetype","name":"Ritual Beast","badge":{"es":"La tribu que defiende el Árbol Sagrado hasta la caída de Tierra","en":"The tribe that defends the Sacred Tree until Tierra falls"},"origin":{"es":"Duel Terminal: Master Guide 5 y The Valuable Book EX 4 (guías oficiales)","en":"Duel Terminal: Master Guide 5 and The Valuable Book EX 4 (official guides)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Guardianes desde la guerra anterior","en":"Guardians since the previous war"},"p":{"es":"Toda la vida del planeta sale del Naturia Sacred Tree y vuelve a él al morir. En el Árbol conviven dos sistemas: el de la creación, de Sophia, y el de la destrucción, de Tierra. Sophia venció en la Batalla de los Dioses y selló a Tierra. Desde la guerra anterior, los Ritual Beast, una tribu que vive unida a sus bestias, y los Nekroz cuidan esa tierra. Cuando Sombre y Kerykeion sienten una interferencia en sus poderes, bajan al Árbol, se reencuentran con ellos y refuerzan a Leodrake y Roach.","en":"All life on the planet springs from the Naturia Sacred Tree and returns to it at death. The Tree holds two systems: creation, run by Sophia, and destruction, run by Tierra. Sophia won the Battle of the Gods and sealed Tierra away. Since the previous war, the Ritual Beast, a tribe that lives bonded to its beasts, and the Nekroz have looked after that land. When Sombre and Kerykeion sense interference with their powers, they go down to the Tree, meet them again and strengthen Leodrake and Roach."},"cards":["Naturia Sacred Tree"]},{"h":{"es":"Una barrera alrededor del Árbol","en":"A barrier around the Tree"},"p":{"es":"Obedeciendo a Tierra, El Shaddoll Grysta empieza a atacar el Árbol. Los Tellarknights, ni siquiera con dos Stellarknights al frente, pueden con los Shaddolls y retroceden hasta el Naturia Sacred Tree. Allí los esperan quienes lo defienden. Con el poder de Evilswarm Exciton Knight, de Leo y de los Ritual Beast y los Nekroz, levantan una barrera como última línea de defensa. En esa línea están Ritual Beast Tamer Elder y Great Sorcerer of the Nekroz.","en":"Obeying Tierra, El Shaddoll Grysta starts attacking the Tree. Not even with two Stellarknights in front can the Tellarknights hold against the Shaddolls, and they fall back to the Naturia Sacred Tree. Its defenders are waiting there. With the power of Evilswarm Exciton Knight, of Leo, and of the Ritual Beast and the Nekroz, they raise a barrier as the last line of defense. Ritual Beast Tamer Elder and Great Sorcerer of the Nekroz stand on that line."},"cards":["Ritual Beast Tamer Elder","Great Sorcerer of the Nekroz"]},{"h":{"es":"Wen, la elegida de los Shaddolls","en":"Wen, chosen by the Shaddolls"},"p":{"es":"Los Tellarknights, los Ritual Beast y los Nekroz chocan con los Shaddolls en la barrera, y Tierra no logra cruzarla. Entonces busca a alguien con un gran poder espiritual para convertirlo en Shaddoll. Elige a Ritual Beast Tamer Wen, que nació con ese don, asustó a los suyos y fue abandonada por sus padres. La crió el Elder de los Tamers, como hermana de Pilica, y mantiene los ojos cerrados para contener un poder que detesta. Los Shaddolls la transforman en El Shaddoll Wendigo.","en":"The Tellarknight, Ritual Beast and Nekroz forces clash with the Shaddolls at the barrier, and Tierra cannot get through. So it looks for someone with great spiritual power to turn into a Shaddoll. It picks Ritual Beast Tamer Wen, who was born with that gift, frightened her people and was abandoned by her parents. The Tamers' Elder raised her as a sister to Pilica, and she keeps her eyes closed to hold back a power she hates. The Shaddolls turn her into El Shaddoll Wendigo."},"cards":["Ritual Beast Ambush","Ritual Beast Tamer Wen","El Shaddoll Wendigo"]},{"h":{"es":"Winda abre el sistema del Árbol","en":"Winda opens the Tree's system"},"p":{"es":"Mientras los Tellarknights derriban a Grysta, Wendigo rompe la barrera, tal como lo quería Tierra. Por ahí pasa El Shaddoll Winda, que en vida fue Winda, Priestess of Gusto. Murió cuando el aura divina de Sophia, al revivir, la golpeó de cerca, y Tierra la revivió a propósito: necesitaba esa aura para entrar al Árbol. Winda la usa para tomar el control del sistema del Árbol y despertar el sistema de los Qliphorts, que dormía en su interior.","en":"While the Tellarknights bring Grysta down, Wendigo breaks the barrier, just as Tierra wanted. El Shaddoll Winda gets through, who in life was Winda, Priestess of Gusto. She died when the divine aura of Sophia, reviving, struck her at close range, and Tierra revived her on purpose: it needed that aura to get into the Tree. Winda uses it to take control of the Tree's system and wake the Qliphort system that slept inside."},"cards":["El Shaddoll Winda","Winda, Priestess of Gusto"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Infernoids y el regreso de Tierra","en":"The Infernoids and Tierra's return"},"p":{"es":"Los Qliphorts persiguen a los Shaddolls hasta que Qliphort Scout atrapa y absorbe a Winda. Su aura divina le abre el poder de Tierra repartido entre los Qliphorts, y bajo su control Winda rompe el sello y revive a los Infernoids. Ellos inundan el mundo con llamas del purgatorio, y los Qliphorts empiezan a eliminar la vida de la superficie. Más tarde, con el poder guardado en los tubos de vacío de los Infernoids, despierta el cuerpo verdadero de Tierra, que vuelve como Infernoid Tierra para arrasar con la vida del sistema de Sophia.","en":"The Qliphorts hunt the Shaddolls until Qliphort Scout traps and absorbs Winda. Her divine aura opens up Tierra's power, split among the Qliphorts, and under its control Winda breaks the seal and revives the Infernoids. They flood the world with purgatory flames, and the Qliphorts start eliminating life on the surface. Later, with the power stored in the Infernoids' vacuum tubes, Tierra's true body awakens and returns as Infernoid Tierra to wipe out the life of Sophia's system."},"cards":["Qliphort Scout","Infernoid Tierra"]},{"h":{"es":"Lara hereda el poder de Gaiapelio","en":"Lara inherits Gaiapelio's power"},"p":{"es":"Cuando Tierra ataca, Spiritual Beast Gaiapelio y su jinete Lara cubren a sus compañeros y quedan casi muertos. Gaiapelio le deja a Lara lo que le queda de poder y su alma se une a la de ella. Así Lara hereda también el poder de Guardiana del Árbol Sagrado y maneja a la vez la creación y la destrucción. Mientras tanto, la sombra de fuego azul que escapó del Árbol es Evil, el undécimo Infernoid, que se alimenta de los restos vacíos de los otros.","en":"When Tierra attacks, Spiritual Beast Gaiapelio and its rider Lara shield their comrades and are left nearly dead. Gaiapelio leaves Lara what remains of its power, and its soul merges with hers. That way Lara also inherits the power of Keeper of the Sacred Tree and wields creation and destruction together. Meanwhile, the blue-fire shadow that escaped the Tree is Evil, the eleventh Infernoid, feeding on the empty remains of the others."},"cards":["Ritual Beast Ulti-Gaiapelio","Ritual Beast Inheritance","Spiritual Beast Tamer Lara"]},{"h":{"es":"Las llamas azules y las alas de Sophia","en":"The blue flames and Sophia's wings"},"p":{"es":"El poder que despierta en Lara atrae a dos sombras: el Agua y la Sombra de los Yang Zing, que habían peleado contra ella. Gastaron todo su poder en activar a Zefraath, el protector del Árbol, pero se funden otra vez y juran luchar a su lado. Evil, en cambio, absorbe a diez Infernoids y se vuelve Flood, y hace llover sobre Lara las llamas azules del purgatorio. Acorralada, Lara suelta los dos poderes que sostienen su vida, y unas alas como las de Sophia le brotan y repelen las llamas.","en":"The power awakening in Lara draws two shadows: the Water and the Shadow of the Yang Zing, who had fought her. They spent all their strength activating Zefraath, protector of the Tree, but fuse together again and swear to fight at her side. Evil, meanwhile, absorbs ten Infernoids and becomes Flood, raining the blue flames of purgatory on Lara. Cornered, Lara releases the two powers that hold her life together, and wings like Sophia's sprout from her back and drive the flames away."},"cards":["Taotie, Shadow of the Yang Zing","Ritual Beast Ulti-Nochiudrago","Ritual Beast Ulti-Reirautari"]},{"h":{"es":"El fin de la guerra y los que vuelven","en":"The war ends and the lost return"},"p":{"es":"Zefraath se enfrenta a Tierra en una batalla de mil días y mil noches que sacude el planeta. Al amanecer del último día no quedan ni uno ni otro, solo los restos del Árbol y dos Gem-Knights. Al caer Tierra se liberan los atrapados en los tubos de vacío de los Infernoids. Ritual Beast Tamer Elder llora sin consuelo al ver volver a Gusto Falco, como lloraba de joven siendo Kamui, y también vuelven Winda, ahora Spiritual Beast Tamer Winda, y Ariel, Priestess of the Nekroz.","en":"Zefraath faces Tierra in a battle of a thousand days and a thousand nights that shakes the planet. At dawn on the last day neither is left, only the Tree's charred remains and two Gem-Knights. With Tierra's fall, those trapped in the Infernoids' vacuum tubes are freed. Ritual Beast Tamer Elder weeps uncontrollably at seeing Gusto Falco return, as he wept in his youth as Kamui, and Winda, now Spiritual Beast Tamer Winda, and Ariel, Priestess of the Nekroz come back too."},"cards":["Ritual Beast Return","Ariel, Priestess of the Nekroz","Spiritual Beast Tamer Winda"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Eva","title":"Master Guide 5 Lore Translation","url":"https://ygorganization.com/thelorethatendsinasearcher/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"La traducción de la historia de Duel Terminal en dos versiones, con nombres japoneses literales y con los nombres del TCG.","en":"The Duel Terminal storyline translated in two versions, with literal Japanese names and with the TCG names."}},{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"Story 11: DT Addendum: The Purgatory Working in the Shadows [VBEX4]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-11-dt-addendum-the-purgatory-working-in-the-shadows-vbex4/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"El relato de Lara, Gaiapelio y las llamas del purgatorio traducido, con las cartas en orden.","en":"The story of Lara, Gaiapelio and the purgatory flames translated, with the cards in order."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Ritual Beast","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Ritual_Beast","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 4 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_4_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Resume solo los tramos de Master Guide 5 y de The Valuable Book EX 4 (No. 11) donde aparecen los Ritual Beast; el resto de la historia de Duel Terminal (Gem-Knights, Zefra, Tellarknights) se menciona apenas lo necesario. The Valuable Book EX 4 no ubica en el tiempo el relato de Lara: aquí va durante el ataque de Tierra porque ahí lo cuenta la guía. La página no dice qué fue de Wen tras convertirse en Shaddoll.","en":"It summarizes only the parts of Master Guide 5 and The Valuable Book EX 4 (No. 11) where the Ritual Beast appear; the rest of the Duel Terminal story (Gem-Knights, Zefra, Tellarknights) is mentioned only as needed. The Valuable Book EX 4 does not place Lara's story in time: here it sits during Tierra's attack because that is where the guide tells it. The page does not say what became of Wen after she became a Shaddoll."}},{"slug":"s-force","kind":"archetype","name":"S-Force","badge":{"es":"Una organización secreta que viaja por épocas y dimensiones","en":"A secret organization that travels across eras and dimensions"},"origin":{"es":"Historias de las cartas: Valuable Book EX, EX 4 y Master Duel","en":"Card storylines: Valuable Book EX, EX 4 and Master Duel"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Chiyomaru presenta a la S-Force","en":"Chiyomaru introduces the S-Force"},"p":{"es":"El relato lo cuenta Rappa Chiyomaru, la integrante más joven de la S-Force, una ninja que pelea con un shuriken de rayos gigante y una ninjato. El comandante le encargó presentar al equipo. Empieza por su asunto pendiente: su objetivo de misión es I:P Masquerena, que se le escapó el otro día cuando estaba por atraparla. Desde ahí pasa a contar cómo es la organización donde trabaja.","en":"The story is told by Rappa Chiyomaru, the youngest member of the S-Force, a ninja who fights with a giant beam shuriken and a ninjato. The commander had her introduce the team. She starts with her unfinished business: her mission target is I:P Masquerena, who slipped away the other day just as she was about to catch her. From there she goes on to describe the organization she works for."},"cards":["S-Force Chase","S-Force Rappa Chiyomaru"]},{"h":{"es":"Justify y el profesor","en":"Justify and the Professor"},"p":{"es":"Chiyomaru presenta primero a la cúpula. La S-Force viaja por épocas y dimensiones con tecnología de punta para frenar crímenes y desastres antes de que ocurran. Su comandante, Justify, es calmo y reparte al personal según su estrategia; ella nunca le vio la cara. En combate usa una armadura de unos tres metros y pelea cuerpo a cuerpo, sin armas. El profesor DiGamma lidera la ciencia y remodela la base a su antojo, entre quejas. Tiene un vínculo con los PSY-Frame, su objetivo, aunque le gusta que lo manden de misión.","en":"Chiyomaru first presents the leadership. The S-Force travels across eras and dimensions with cutting-edge technology to stop crimes and disasters before they happen. Its commander, Justify, is calm and assigns staff according to his strategy; she has never seen his face. In combat he wears a power suit about three meters tall and fights hand to hand, with no weapons. Professor DiGamma leads the science side and remodels the base on a whim, amid complaints. He has a connection to the PSY-Frames, his target, though he likes being sent on missions."},"cards":["S-Force Justify","S-Force Professor DiGamma"]},{"h":{"es":"Los agentes de campo","en":"The field agents"},"p":{"es":"Después vienen los agentes de campo. Pla-Tina manipula espacio y tiempo y sigue sonriendo aun enojada, lo que asusta. Orrafist es el as de los arrestos, un vaquero de aire futurista con una pistola de rayos adornada con motivos del tiempo; se unió para averiguar sobre los Time Thieves y es el eterno rival de Time Thief Redoer. Edge Razor, el samurái, es casi tan bueno y rinde en misiones de equipo. Gravitino, el recién llegado, lo eligió Justify: maneja el espacio y el tiempo como Pla-Tina y también investiga el tema.","en":"Next come the field agents. Pla-Tina manipulates space and time and keeps smiling even when angry, which is frightening. Orrafist is the ace of arrests, a cowboy with a futuristic look and a beam pistol decorated with time motifs; he joined to learn about the Time Thieves and is the eternal rival of Time Thief Redoer. Edge Razor, the samurai, is almost as good and shines in team missions. Gravitino, the newcomer, was picked by Justify: he handles space and time like Pla-Tina and also researches the subject."},"cards":["S-Force Pla-Tina","S-Force Orrafist","S-Force Gravitino"]},{"h":{"es":"Bridgehead y la presentación final","en":"Bridgehead and the closing introduction"},"p":{"es":"El centro de todo es Bridgehead, la base que nació del poder de Pla-Tina y que se desplaza por el espacio y el tiempo. Hay instalaciones y mechas de alta gama, como los Dog Tag que desarrolló el profesor. Son autómatas de producción en serie, tan grandes que un adulto puede montarlos, y llevan gente y equipo en las misiones. Chiyomaru cierra presentándose: es una shinobi y, como le pidió el jefe de su aldea, castiga a los malhechores por el mundo. Todavía no atrapó a su objetivo.","en":"The center of it all is Bridgehead, the base born from Pla-Tina's power, which moves through space and time. It holds facilities and high-end mechas, such as the Dog Tags the Professor developed. They are mass-produced autonomous machines, big enough for an adult to ride, and carry people and gear on missions. Chiyomaru closes by introducing herself: she is a shinobi and, as the head of her village asked of her, punishes wrongdoers for the world. She still has not captured her target."},"cards":["S-Force Dog Tag","S-Force Bridgehead"]},{"h":{"es":"Otra historia (EX 4): Chiyomaru y Masquerena","en":"Another storyline (EX 4): Chiyomaru and Masquerena"},"p":{"es":"Una historia distinta, de la Valuable Book EX 4, vuelve sobre la persecución. Justify manda a Chiyomaru tras Masquerena. El día anterior ella tropezó, falló y le dejó una curita. Su técnica de husmear indica que el objetivo no parece una villana, y al revisar en la base de datos cómo se aprobaron los objetivos solo encuentra jerga incomprensible. Justify no explica nada y suma a otro perseguidor, Nightchaser. Chiyomaru le da la espalda a la misión para proteger a Masquerena, sin saber que eso traerá un problema mayor al mundo.","en":"A separate storyline, from Valuable Book EX 4, revisits the chase. Justify sends Chiyomaru after Masquerena. The day before, she tripped, failed and left a band-aid for her. Her snooping technique suggests the target does not seem like a villain, and when she checks how targets were approved in the databank she finds only baffling jargon. Justify explains nothing and adds another chaser, Nightchaser. Chiyomaru turns her back on the mission to protect Masquerena, not knowing that this will bring a bigger turmoil to the world."},"cards":["S-Force Nightchaser","I:P Masquerena"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: la bienvenida a los reclutas","en":"Master Duel: welcoming the recruits"},"p":{"es":"En la versión de Master Duel, la S-Force es una sociedad secreta de ciencia avanzada, y Chiyomaru recibe a los reclutas nuevos como guía. Ella sabe que cada uno llegó por una razón distinta: un incidente, una captación, objetivos en común o un contrato con otra organización. Ella está ahí por orden del jefe de su aldea. Sus habilidades definen sus destinos, y las de ella son los shuriken y las técnicas para esconderse en cualquier lado. En su base, Bridgehead, se observan muchas dimensiones.","en":"In the Master Duel version, the S-Force is a secret society of advanced science, and Chiyomaru welcomes the new recruits as their guide. She knows each came for a different reason: an incident, being scouted, shared goals or a contract from another organization. She herself is there on her village head's orders. Abilities decide assignments, and hers are shuriken and techniques to hide anywhere. At their base, Bridgehead, many dimensions are observed."},"cards":["S-Force Bridgehead"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: el entrenamiento","en":"Master Duel: training"},"p":{"es":"Cuando la base detecta un problema, Justify manda al agente más adecuado por la puerta de teletransporte. Las misiones pueden ser auxiliar en desastres, salvar vidas o incluso seguir y capturar sospechosos, y nadie sabe cuándo van a necesitarlos. Por eso Chiyomaru insiste en entrenar siempre, con las instalaciones de la base, y aprovecha para hacerlo antes de la siguiente lección. Después aclara que ella se siente segura en misiones en solitario, aunque igual sale con sus mayores por orden del comandante.","en":"When the base detects a problem, Justify sends the most suitable agent through the warp gate. Missions can be disaster response, saving lives or even tailing and apprehending suspects, and nobody knows when they will be needed. That is why Chiyomaru insists on constant training, using the base's facilities, and she takes the time to do it before the next lesson. She then adds that she feels confident on solo missions, though she still goes out with her seniors on the commander's orders."},"cards":["S-Force Rappa Chiyomaru"]},{"h":{"es":"Master Duel: los veteranos","en":"Master Duel: the veterans"},"p":{"es":"Chiyomaru presenta a los veteranos. De Justify repite que nunca le vio la cara. Lapcewell, que vuela y dispara rayos, llegó de una dimensión lejana hace mucho, es el más antiguo después de Justify y le enseñó hasta cosas ajenas a las misiones. DiGamma dirige los equipos científicos y creó el Dog Tag; hay quejas porque pasillos y salas cambian de lugar. Pla-Tina interfiere con las dimensiones, y nunca hay que hacerla enojar. Sospecha que ellos van a las misiones sabiendo más que el resto.","en":"Chiyomaru introduces the veterans. Of Justify she repeats that she has never seen his face. Lapcewell, who flies and shoots beams, came from a distant dimension long ago, is the longest-serving member after Justify and taught her even things unrelated to missions. DiGamma runs the science teams and created the Dog Tag; there are complaints because hallways and rooms change places. Pla-Tina interferes with dimensions, and she must never be angered. Chiyomaru suspects they enter missions better informed than the others."},"cards":["S-Force Lapcewell","S-Force Professor DiGamma","S-Force Pla-Tina"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"[VBEX] Number 2: S-Force","url":"https://ygorganization.com/vbex-number-2-s-force/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de esta historia de la Valuable Book EX, para leerla completa","en":"English translation of this Valuable Book EX story, to read it in full"}},{"author":"NeoArkadia (YGOrganization)","title":"Story 14: Various Cards [VBEX4]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-14-various-cards-vbex4/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de la historia de Chiyomaru y Masquerena de la Valuable Book EX 4","en":"English translation of the Chiyomaru and Masquerena story from Valuable Book EX 4"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: S-Force","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/S-Force","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 4 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_4_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Duel card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Duel_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los bloques 1 a 4 son la historia de la Valuable Book EX; el 5 es otra historia, de la Valuable Book EX 4, y los últimos tres son la versión de Master Duel. La wiki no indica cómo encajan en el tiempo estas historias, así que se cuentan por separado y no forman una sola línea. La historia de Masquerena queda abierta: el texto solo anuncia un problema mayor.","en":"Blocks 1 to 4 are the Valuable Book EX story; block 5 is a separate story from Valuable Book EX 4, and the last three are the Master Duel version. The wiki does not say how these stories fit together in time, so they are told separately and do not form one timeline. The Masquerena story is left open: the text only announces a bigger problem."}},{"slug":"seto-kaiba","kind":"character","name":"Seto Kaiba","badge":{"es":"Del orfanato a KaibaCorp, siempre detrás de un duelo con Yugi","en":"From orphanage to KaibaCorp, always chasing a Duel with Yugi"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters (anime) y el manga original","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters (anime) and the original manga"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Dos huérfanos y una partida de ajedrez (anime)","en":"Two orphans and a chess game (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, Seto y Mokuba quedan huérfanos y (en la versión japonesa) los parientes se quedan con la herencia, así que terminan en un orfanato. Allí Seto le promete a Mokuba que será su padre y lo cuidará. Cuando Gozaburo Kaiba visita el lugar, Seto lo reta al ajedrez: si gana, los adopta a los dos. Gana porque había estudiado sus métodos. Ya adoptado, Gozaburo lo somete a un estudio acelerado y le confisca los juguetes. Mokuba esconde su mazo de Duel Monsters en un libro, con el dibujo de un Blue-Eyes White Dragon, y Seto jura conseguir uno de verdad.","en":"In the anime, Seto and Mokuba are orphaned and (in the Japanese version) their relatives keep the inheritance, so they end up in an orphanage. There Seto promises Mokuba he will be his father and protect him. When Gozaburo Kaiba visits, Seto challenges him to chess: if Seto wins, Gozaburo adopts them both. He wins because he had studied Gozaburo's methods. Once adopted, he is put through an accelerated education and his toys are confiscated. Mokuba hides his Duel Monsters Deck in a book, with a sketch of the Blue-Eyes White Dragon card, and Seto vows to get a real one."},"cards":["Blue-Eyes White Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"KaibaCorp y el primer golpe de Yugi (anime)","en":"KaibaCorp and Yugi's first blow (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Seto inventa un software de realidad virtual para jugar, pero Gozaburo quiere usarlo para la guerra. Seto pierde el respeto por él, pacta con los Big Five y, con el 49% que reúne junto a los Big Five más el 2% de Mokuba, llega al 51% y toma KaibaCorp. Pasa de las armas a los juegos y empieza Kaiba Land. Ya campeón mundial y con tres de las cuatro Blue-Eyes (en la versión japonesa las reúne después), secuestra a Solomon, le gana la cuarta y la rompe. Yugi lo reta, y Yami Yugi lo derrota con Exodia the Forbidden One.","en":"Seto invents virtual software for playing games, but Gozaburo wants it for war. Seto loses respect for him, makes a deal with the Big Five and, with the 49% he holds alongside the Big Five plus Mokuba's 2%, reaches 51% and takes KaibaCorp. He shifts from weapons to games and starts Kaiba Land. Already World Champion and holding three of the four Blue-Eyes (in the Japanese version he gets them later), he kidnaps Solomon, wins the fourth and tears it up. Yugi challenges him, and Yami Yugi defeats him with Exodia the Forbidden One."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"Duelist Kingdom: salvar a Mokuba (anime)","en":"Duelist Kingdom: saving Mokuba (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Tras perder, Kaiba deja de jugar, y Pegasus se alía con los Big Five para quedarse con KaibaCorp. Secuestran a Mokuba y le roban el mazo. Kaiba salta por la ventana de su oficina, se aferra al acantilado y llega a Duelist Kingdom, donde le gana a Joey cuando su Red-Eyes Black Dragon cae ante un Blue-Eyes. Contra Yami Yugi invoca a Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon, que Yami Yugi debilita con Mammoth Graveyard; Kaiba se para al borde del castillo, Yugi cancela el ataque y Kaiba gana. Pegasus lo vence y encierra su alma; al perder contra Yugi, la libera.","en":"After losing, Kaiba quits playing, and Pegasus allies with the Big Five to take KaibaCorp. They kidnap Mokuba and steal his Deck. Kaiba jumps out of his office window, clings to the cliff side and reaches Duelist Kingdom, where he beats Joey when his Red-Eyes Black Dragon falls to a Blue-Eyes. Against Yami Yugi he summons Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon, which Yami Yugi weakens with Mammoth Graveyard; Kaiba stands on the castle edge, Yugi calls off the attack and Kaiba wins. Pegasus beats him and locks away his soul; when Pegasus loses to Yugi, he frees it."},"cards":["Red-Eyes Black Dragon","Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon","Mammoth Graveyard"]},{"h":{"es":"Battle City: el torneo de Kaiba (anime)","en":"Battle City: Kaiba's tournament (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Ishizu quiere atraer a los ladrones de los Dioses, así que le entrega a Kaiba Obelisk the Tormentor y le muestra visiones de un sacerdote idéntico a él frente a un faraón. Kaiba acepta organizar el torneo para juntar los tres Dioses y recuperar su título frente a Yugi. Antes prueba la carta contra un robot con su mazo de Duelist Kingdom; Obelisk vence a Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon y la máquina arde. Battle City arranca con Duel Disks nuevos, y los Rare Hunters se cuelan. Más adelante, el texto de The Winged Dragon of Ra le resulta legible, y no entiende por qué.","en":"Ishizu wants to lure the thieves who took the Gods, so she gives Kaiba Obelisk the Tormentor and shows him visions of a priest who looks just like him facing a pharaoh. Kaiba agrees to host a tournament to gather all three Gods and retake his title from Yugi. First he tries the card on a robot running his Duelist Kingdom Deck; Obelisk beats Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon and the machine burns out. Battle City starts with new Duel Disks, and the Rare Hunters sneak in. Later he finds he can read the text on The Winged Dragon of Ra, and can't tell why."},"cards":["Obelisk the Tormentor","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"El mundo virtual de Noah y Gozaburo (anime)","en":"Noah and Gozaburo's virtual world (anime)"},"p":{"es":"De camino a las finales, Noah arrastra el dirigible hasta su fortaleza virtual. Los Big Five, atrapados allí por no haber logrado encerrar a Kaiba, odian a Yugi y a sus amigos por haberlo ayudado. Noah, hijo de Gozaburo, quiere el cuerpo de Seto para dirigir KaibaCorp. Seto acepta el duelo con Kaiser Sea Horse como su Deck Master; Noah usa a Mokuba de escudo, Seto se niega a atacar y Yugi retoma el duelo. Después, Gozaburo, con la mente digitalizada, lo desafía con Exodia Necross, y Seto la anula sacando del Cementerio las piezas de Exodia.","en":"On the way to the finals, Noah drags the blimp into his virtual fortress. The Big Five, trapped there after failing to lock Kaiba in, hate Yugi and his friends for helping him. Noah, Gozaburo's son, wants Seto's body to run KaibaCorp. Seto accepts the Duel with Kaiser Sea Horse as his own Deck Master; Noah uses Mokuba as a shield, Seto refuses to attack and Yugi takes the Duel over. Afterwards Gozaburo, his mind digitized, challenges him with Exodia Necross, and Seto shuts it down by removing the Exodia pieces from the Graveyard."},"cards":["Kaiser Sea Horse","Exodia Necross"]},{"h":{"es":"La final de Battle City (anime)","en":"The Battle City finals (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Kaiba se enfrenta a Yugi en la semifinal, con Obelisk contra Slifer, incluso con Lullaby of Obedience para robarle a Slifer. Una visión muestra al sacerdote Seto y al faraón. Yami Yugi lo vence con Dark Paladin y De-Fusion, y Kaiba entrega Obelisk por la regla. Más tarde, Ishizu le dice una frase egipcia que entiende. Kaiba decide ayudar a Yugi contra Marik con Fiend's Sanctuary. Cuando termina, él y Mokuba destruyen la isla y se van en el Blue-Eyes White Jet.","en":"Kaiba faces Yugi in the semi-final, Obelisk against Slifer, even using Lullaby of Obedience to steal Slifer. A vision shows Priest Seto and the Pharaoh. Yami Yugi beats him with Dark Paladin and De-Fusion, and Kaiba hands over Obelisk under the tournament rules. Later, Ishizu says an Egyptian phrase he understands. Kaiba decides to help Yugi against Marik with Fiend's Sanctuary. Afterwards, he and Mokuba blow up the island and leave in the Blue-Eyes White Jet."},"cards":["Dark Paladin","Lullaby of Obedience","Fiend's Sanctuary"]},{"h":{"es":"El vínculo con Atem (anime)","en":"The bond with Atem (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Yami Bakura lo reta a un Juego de Sombras y le muestra una visión del sacerdote Seto con Kisara, y le tira el Millennium Eye. Con eso Kaiba viaja a Egipto, y Yami Bakura lo arrastra al Mundo de los Recuerdos. Frente a Zorc invoca su Blue-Eyes, y Atem, con la armadura de Black Luster Soldier, se fusiona con él. Luego Kaiba bloquea un ataque de Zorc con Ring of Defense. Al final, mira el Ritual de Batalla en el que Yugi derrota a Atem.","en":"Yami Bakura challenges him to a Shadow Game, shows him a vision of Priest Seto with Kisara, and tosses him the Millennium Eye. With that Kaiba travels to Egypt, where Yami Bakura drags him into the World of Memories. Facing Zorc he summons his Blue-Eyes, and Atem, wearing Black Luster Soldier's armor, fuses with him. Later Kaiba blocks a Zorc attack with Ring of Defense. At the end, he watches the Battle Ritual in which Yugi defeats Atem."},"cards":["Black Luster Soldier","Ring of Defense"]},{"h":{"es":"El manga: Death-T y el coma","en":"The manga: Death-T and the coma"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Seto tenía diez años cuando ganó el ajedrez haciendo trampa, y tomó KaibaCorp seis años después. Dark Yugi lo derrota en un Juego de Sombras y el Blue-Eyes de Sugoroku que Kaiba había robado se destruye solo. En Death-T, Kaiba domina al principio con Saggi the Dark Clown, pero Dark Yugi arma Exodia y le aplica el Mind Crush: seis meses en coma, y despierta en Duelist Kingdom. Más tarde, en The Dark Side of Dimensions, invoca a Neo Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon.","en":"In the manga, Seto was ten when he won the chess game by cheating, and took KaibaCorp six years later. Dark Yugi defeats him in a Shadow Game and Sugoroku's Blue-Eyes that Kaiba had stolen destroys itself. In Death-T, Kaiba dominates early with Saggi the Dark Clown, but Dark Yugi assembles Exodia and applies the Mind Crush: six months in a coma, and he wakes up in Duelist Kingdom. Later, in The Dark Side of Dimensions, he summons Neo Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon."},"cards":["Saggi the Dark Clown","Neo Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Seto Kaiba","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Seto_Kaiba","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Seto Kaiba (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Seto_Kaiba_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yugi Muto","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yugi_Muto","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Los bloques 1 a 7 siguen el anime (con diferencias de doblaje cuando la wiki las marca) y el último, el manga, donde el abuelo de Yugi es Sugoroku y no Solomon. Las películas (Pyramid of Light, Bonds Beyond Time) no se cubren; solo el último bloque toca The Dark Side of Dimensions, tal como lo cuenta la página del manga. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"Blocks 1 to 7 follow the anime (with dub differences where the wiki notes them) and the last one follows the manga, where Yugi's grandfather is Sugoroku rather than Solomon. The films (Pyramid of Light, Bonds Beyond Time) are not covered; only the last block touches The Dark Side of Dimensions, as told on the manga page. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}},{"slug":"shaddoll","kind":"archetype","name":"Shaddoll","badge":{"es":"Los muertos de una guerra, convertidos en sombras que buscan volver al Árbol","en":"The dead of a war, turned into shadows that seek the Tree"},"origin":{"es":"Historias de las cartas: Master Guide 5 y The Valuable Book EX 6","en":"Card storylines: Master Guide 5 and The Valuable Book EX 6"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Del Árbol Sagrado a Shaddoll Core","en":"From the Sacred Tree to Shaddoll Core"},"p":{"es":"Toda la vida nace del Naturia Sacred Tree y vuelve a él al morir. Sophia y Tierra regían la creación y la destrucción; Sophia venció, selló a Tierra con un Núcleo y partió ese Núcleo en diez fragmentos. Con los eones, Tierra recuperó fuerzas y busca reunirlos para revivir. En ese clima, Evilswarm Kerykeion va a ver si Master Diamond volvió y lo halla convertido en Cairngorgon, que absorbe almas. Kerykeion no puede usar todo su poder contra su amigo y es absorbido, y Cairngorgon muta en Shaddoll Core.","en":"All life is born from the Naturia Sacred Tree and returns to it at death. Sophia and Tierra ran creation and destruction; Sophia won, sealed Tierra with a Core and broke that Core into ten fragments. Over the aeons, Tierra regained strength and seeks to gather them to revive. In that climate, Evilswarm Kerykeion goes to see whether Master Diamond has returned and finds him turned into Cairngorgon, who absorbs souls. Kerykeion cannot use his full power against his friend and is absorbed, and Cairngorgon mutates into Shaddoll Core."},"cards":["Naturia Sacred Tree","Evilswarm Kerykeion","Shaddoll Core"]},{"h":{"es":"Qué son los Shaddoll","en":"What the Shaddolls are"},"p":{"es":"Shaddoll Core da a luz a los Shaddoll. En el fondo son quienes murieron en la guerra anterior y debían volver al Árbol para renacer con la energía de Sophia. Tierra los atrapó dentro del Árbol y los encerró en los tubos de vacío de los Infernoid, y su energía fue cambiando a la de Tierra. El sistema del Árbol los trata entonces como errores y los escupe al mundo solo con el cuerpo. Casi sin conciencia, conservan el deseo de volver al Árbol. El Shaddoll Construct los maneja con hilos de sombra.","en":"Shaddoll Core gives birth to the Shaddolls. At heart they are those who died in the previous war and were meant to return to the Tree to be reborn with Sophia's energy. Tierra trapped them inside the Tree and locked them in the Infernoids' vacuum tubes, and their energy slowly changed into Tierra's. The Tree's system then treats them as bugs and spits them into the world with only a body. Barely conscious, they keep the urge to return to the Tree. El Shaddoll Construct controls them with strings of shadow."},"cards":["El Shaddoll Construct"]},{"h":{"es":"La marcha y los Yang Zing","en":"The march and the Yang Zing"},"p":{"es":"Constellar Sombre percibe el apuro de Kerykeion y lleva a los Yang Zing a detener la marcha. Pulao y Suanni pierden sus sombras y pasan a ser Shaddoll. Llega Chiwen, que reúne a los Yang Zing en Baxia, y bajan del cielo los Tellarknight, guerreros de luz herederos de los Constellar. Aun así los ocho Yang Zing terminan convertidos en Shaddoll. Unukalhai nota dentro de las sombras el poder de Kerykeion e intenta liberarlo, pero lo atrapan y lo vuelven Shaddoll Squamata.","en":"Constellar Sombre senses Kerykeion's plight and leads the Yang Zing to halt the march. Pulao and Suanni lose their shadows and become Shaddolls. Chiwen arrives and gathers the Yang Zing into Baxia, and the Tellarknights descend from the sky, warriors of light descended from the Constellar. Even so, all eight Yang Zing end up turned into Shaddolls. Unukalhai notices Kerykeion's power inside the shadows and tries to free him, but is captured and turned into Shaddoll Squamata."},"cards":["Baxia, Brightness of the Yang Zing","Satellarknight Unukalhai","Shaddoll Squamata"]},{"h":{"es":"El error de los Tellarknight","en":"The Tellarknights' mistake"},"p":{"es":"Desde dentro de las sombras, Kerykeion entrega la sombra de su báculo a los Tellarknight, y con ese poder nace Stellarknight Delteros. Pero el costo ya estaba hecho: al absorber a Unukalhai, los Shaddoll obtuvieron el poder de conectar estrellas. Fusionan a Squamata con Bixi en Jiaotu y a Jiaotu con Taotie en Yazi, y la guerra pasa a ser de los Tellarknight contra Yang Zing y Shaddoll. Después juntan diez Núcleos, entre ellos el Pyroxene de Gem-Knight Lapis que guarda Construct, y Shaddoll Core evoluciona en El Shaddoll Grysta, que ataca el Árbol.","en":"From within the shadows, Kerykeion hands the shadow of his staff to the Tellarknights, and with that power Stellarknight Delteros is born. But the damage was done: by absorbing Unukalhai, the Shaddolls gained the power of connecting the stars. They fuse Squamata with Bixi into Jiaotu and Jiaotu with Taotie into Yazi, and the war becomes the Tellarknights against both Yang Zing and Shaddolls. They then gather ten Cores, including the Pyroxene of Gem-Knight Lapis held in Construct, and Shaddoll Core evolves into El Shaddoll Grysta, who attacks the Tree."},"cards":["Stellarknight Delteros","Jiaotu, Darkness of the Yang Zing","El Shaddoll Grysta"]},{"h":{"es":"La batalla ante el Árbol","en":"The battle at the Tree"},"p":{"es":"Los Tellarknight, sin poder frenar a Construct ni a Grysta, se repliegan al Árbol, donde Ritual Beast y Nekroz levantan una barrera final. Tierra no logra romperla y cambia de plan: convertir en Shaddoll a alguien de gran poder espiritual, y elige a Ritual Beast Tamer Wen, que se vuelve El Shaddoll Wendigo. Wendigo destruye la barrera, y El Shaddoll Winda, que fue Winda, Priestess of Gusto, llega al Árbol y enciende los Qliphort dormidos. Grysta cae, y una historia aparte cuenta que El Shaddoll Apkallone lo manejó como marioneta.","en":"Unable to stop Construct or Grysta, the Tellarknights fall back to the Tree, where the Ritual Beasts and Nekroz raise a final barrier. Tierra cannot break it and changes plan: turn someone of great spiritual power into a Shaddoll, and it picks Ritual Beast Tamer Wen, who becomes El Shaddoll Wendigo. Wendigo destroys the barrier, and El Shaddoll Winda, once Winda, Priestess of Gusto, reaches the Tree and boots up the sleeping Qliphorts. Grysta falls, and a separate story says El Shaddoll Apkallone worked it like a puppet."},"cards":["El Shaddoll Wendigo","El Shaddoll Winda","El Shaddoll Apkallone"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Qliphort cazan a los Shaddoll","en":"The Qliphorts hunt the Shaddolls"},"p":{"es":"Una vez activos, los Qliphort ven a los Shaddoll como un elemento ajeno al sistema del Árbol y salen a eliminarlos. Aun así Construct es demasiado fuerte. Kerykeion lo suprime desde adentro, Delteros junta su poder en Apoqliphort Towers y Construct queda detenido. Para fijar la contención, Shurit, de los Nekroz, congela a El Shaddoll Shekhinaga con el poder de tres dragones de Ice Barrier. Pero Qliphort Scout absorbe a Winda y, con esa aura divina, libera el poder de Tierra: despiertan los Infernoid, que inundan el mundo de fuego.","en":"Once active, the Qliphorts see the Shaddolls as an element foreign to the Tree's system and go out to eliminate them. Even so, Construct is too strong. Kerykeion suppresses it from inside, Delteros gathers his power at Apoqliphort Towers, and Construct is stopped. To hold it in place, Shurit of the Nekroz freezes El Shaddoll Shekhinaga with the power of three Ice Barrier dragons. But Qliphort Scout absorbs Winda and, with that divine aura, releases Tierra's power: the Infernoids awaken and flood the world with fire."},"cards":["Apoqliphort Towers","El Shaddoll Shekhinaga","Qliphort Scout"]},{"h":{"es":"Ptolemaeus, Anoyatyllis y la lanza","en":"Ptolemaeus, Anoyatyllis and the lance"},"p":{"es":"Los Nekroz revivieron a Gem-Knight Master Diamond con Nekroz Cycle, y él se sumó a la guerra para expiar su pasado como Shaddoll. Fusionado con Tellarknights y Constellar, se volvió Stellarknight Constellar Diamond, y con Constellar Sombre nació Tellarknight Ptolemaeus. Entonces Infernoid Devyaty absorbió a tres dragones de Ice Barrier, liberó a Shekhinaga y lo tragó: surgió El Shaddoll Anoyatyllis. Ptolemaeus y Dance Princess, con Nekroz of Sophia, salieron a detener a Anoyatyllis, y la Dragunity Divine Lance, junto a diez guerreros Zefra, la destruyó.","en":"The Nekroz revived Gem-Knight Master Diamond with Nekroz Cycle, and he joined the war to atone for his past as a Shaddoll. Fused with Tellarknights and Constellar, he became Stellarknight Constellar Diamond, and with Constellar Sombre, Tellarknight Ptolemaeus was born. Then Infernoid Devyaty absorbed three Ice Barrier dragons, freed Shekhinaga and swallowed it: El Shaddoll Anoyatyllis emerged. Ptolemaeus and Dance Princess, with Nekroz of Sophia, set out to stop Anoyatyllis, and the Dragunity Divine Lance, together with ten Zefra warriors, destroyed it."},"cards":["Nekroz Cycle","Tellarknight Ptolemaeus","El Shaddoll Anoyatyllis"]},{"h":{"es":"El fin de Tierra y el descanso de los Shaddoll","en":"The end of Tierra and the Shaddolls' rest"},"p":{"es":"De los restos de Anoyatyllis sale Infernoid Decatron, que despierta a Tierra, y para recuperar la creación Tierra revive a Gem-Knight Lapis, dormida en Construct. Con todos sus poderes de vuelta, renace. Ptolemaeus libera a los nueve Yang Zing y despierta al undécimo Zefra, que se funde con Zefracore. Zefraath enfrenta a Tierra mil días y mil noches; al amanecer del último ya no hay rastro de ninguno, solo el Árbol quemado y dos Gem-Knights. Crystal y Lapis, muertos y Shaddoll, entran en la luz del Árbol y hallan su descanso.","en":"From the remains of Anoyatyllis comes Infernoid Decatron, which awakens Tierra, and to regain creation Tierra revives Gem-Knight Lapis, asleep in Construct. With all its powers back, it is reborn. Ptolemaeus releases the nine Yang Zing and awakens the eleventh Zefra, which fuses with Zefracore. Zefraath faces Tierra for a thousand days and nights; at dawn of the last, neither is anywhere to be seen, only the charred Tree and two Gem-Knights. Crystal and Lapis, dead and Shaddolls, enter the Tree's light and find their rest."},"cards":["Zefraath","Gem-Knight Crystal","Gem-Knight Lapis"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Eva (YGOrganization)","title":"Master Guide 5 Lore Translation","url":"https://ygorganization.com/thelorethatendsinasearcher/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción al inglés de toda la saga de Master Guide 5, donde está la historia completa","en":"English translation of the whole Master Guide 5 saga, where the full story is"}},{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"Story 14: DT World Story Addendum Story [VBEX6]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-14-dt-world-story-addendum-story-vbex6/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción del apéndice sobre la batalla del Árbol Sagrado de la Valuable Book EX 6","en":"Translation of the Sacred Tree battle addendum from Valuable Book EX 6"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Shaddoll","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Shaddoll","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia sale de Master Guide 5, que cuenta una guerra mayor en la que los Shaddoll son una parte; solo se tomó el hilo de los Shaddoll y sus encuentros con Yang Zing, Tellarknight, Ritual Beast, Nekroz y Zefra. El apéndice de la Valuable Book EX 6 agrega el control de Grysta por Apkallone. La wiki no precisa cuánto tiempo pasa entre los episodios. Por el límite de bloques se comprimieron la fusión de Master Diamond, Tierra con Batlamyus y los diez Qliphort, y el viaje de Ptolemaeus.","en":"The story comes from Master Guide 5, which tells a larger war in which the Shaddolls are one part; only the Shaddoll thread and its encounters with the Yang Zing, Tellarknights, Ritual Beasts, Nekroz and Zefra were taken. The Valuable Book EX 6 addendum adds Apkallone's control of Grysta. The wiki does not say how much time passes between the episodes. Because of the block limit, Master Diamond's fusion, Tierra with Batlamyus and the ten Qliphorts, and Ptolemaeus' journey were compressed."}},{"slug":"sky-striker","kind":"archetype","name":"Sky Striker","badge":{"es":"Raye, una espadachina que lanza mechas contra un imperio, y la rival que la iguala","en":"Raye, a swordswoman who launches mecha against an empire, and the rival who matches her"},"origin":{"es":"OCG: guías Master Guide 6 y Valuable Book EX 6; también en el manga OCG Stories","en":"OCG: Master Guide 6 and Valuable Book EX 6 guides; also in the OCG Stories manga"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Raye y el imperio","en":"Raye and the empire"},"p":{"es":"Un imperio militar enorme amenazaba a una nación pequeña, y la respuesta fue el Sky Striker Mecha, armamento hecho con tecnología avanzada. Según las guías oficiales de cartas del OCG, el control de esos mechas depende de una espada llamada Sky Striker, y la tiene Raye. A simple vista es una chica común, pero su talento natural y un entrenamiento especial le permiten sacarle el poder a la espada y abrir portales por donde salen los mechas. Su habilidad hizo posible el sistema Multirole, que mueve armas gigantes. Raye recorre el frente a toda velocidad para defender su tierra.","en":"A huge military empire threatened a smaller nation, and the answer was the Sky Striker Mecha, weaponry built with advanced technology. According to the official OCG card guides, control of those mecha depends on a sword called Sky Striker, and Raye holds it. At first glance she is an ordinary girl, but natural talent and special training let her draw out the sword's power and open gates through which the mecha emerge. Her ability made the Multirole system possible, which moves giant weapons. Raye runs along the front at top speed to defend her land."},"cards":["Sky Striker Ace - Raye","Sky Striker Mecha Modules - Multirole"]},{"h":{"es":"Cuatro modos, cuatro oficios","en":"Four modes, four trades"},"p":{"es":"Raye elige modo según lo que pida el combate, y cada uno trae su propia Maniobra. Para atacar está Kagari: parte la espada en ocho para armar unas alas ardientes y destruye todo con fuego masivo. Para resistir está Shizuku, que levanta barreras contra balas y disparos de energía, ideal para cuidar una posición. Kaina sirve en distancias cortas o medias, con cuatro brazos enormes. Hayate dispara con un riel gigante desde lejos y quita del medio a las fuerzas principales del rival con puntería exacta.","en":"Raye chooses a mode according to what the fight demands, and each brings its own Maneuver. For offense there is Kagari: it splits the sword in eight to form blazing wings and destroys everything with massive fire. For endurance there is Shizuku, which raises barriers against bullets and energy shots, ideal for guarding a position. Kaina works at short or medium range, with four enormous arms. Hayate fires a giant railgun from afar and removes the rival's main forces with exact aim."},"cards":["Sky Striker Ace - Kagari","Sky Striker Ace - Shizuku","Sky Striker Ace - Hayate"]},{"h":{"es":"Misiones, apoyo y un prototipo descartado","en":"Missions, support and a discarded prototype"},"p":{"es":"Cuando llegan los informes de un combate, Raye sube al avión Hercules Base y sale a cumplir la misión. Desde ahí el Multirole le despacha los mechas de apoyo al instante. Eagle Booster le da alas y propulsores, y esa velocidad la protege de misiles supersónicos. Widow Anchor sujeta armas enemigas y las anula con ondas electromagnéticas débiles, o toma el mando si son máquinas autónomas. Hornet Drones son mini máquinas que se mueven según lo que ella piensa, reciben golpes por ella y averiguan dónde está el enemigo. Antes existió el prototipo Amatsu, que reunía todo en un solo traje, pero pesaba demasiado para Raye.","en":"When reports of a fight arrive, Raye boards the Hercules Base aircraft and heads out on the mission. From there Multirole dispatches support mecha instantly. Eagle Booster gives her wings and thrusters, and that speed shields her from supersonic missiles. Widow Anchor grips enemy weapons and shuts them down with weak electromagnetic waves, or takes command if they are autonomous machines. Hornet Drones are tiny machines that move by what she thinks, take hits for her and find out where the enemy is. Before them came the Amatsu prototype, which packed everything into one suit, but it was too heavy a burden for Raye."},"cards":["Sky Striker Mecharmory - Hercules Base","Sky Striker Mecha - Widow Anchor","Sky Striker Mecha - Hornet Drones"]},{"h":{"es":"Roze, la Ace del otro bando","en":"Roze, the Ace on the other side"},"p":{"es":"El imperio contraatacó con su propia Sky Striker Ace: Roze, que sirve a la Spectra Union. Raye se desconcierta al ver a otra chica igual a ella. Roze, con un gesto de reojo, sube a Zeke, un arma reforzada gigantesca y poco convencional, y Raye queda al borde del abismo. En esa pelea se quitan los limitadores de Kagari. Mientras chocan las espadas, Raye percibe por medio de Sky Striker el dolor que carga Roze, y su ataque final libera el corazón de la rival. La guerra, igual, seguía empatada.","en":"The empire hit back with its own Sky Striker Ace: Roze, who serves the Spectra Union. Raye is thrown off by the sight of another girl just like her. Roze, with a glance aside, climbs onto Zeke, a gigantic and unconventional reinforced weapon, and Raye ends up at the edge of the abyss. In that fight Kagari's limiters are removed. As the swords clash, Raye perceives through Sky Striker the pain Roze carries, and her final attack frees the rival's heart. The war, all the same, stayed at a stalemate."},"cards":["Sky Striker Ace - Roze","Sky Striker Ace - Zeke"]},{"h":{"es":"Zero: una guerrera hecha de dos","en":"Zero: one warrior made of two"},"p":{"es":"Justo cuando Raye y Roze empezaban a entenderse, el imperio largó un ejército de H.A.M.P., su arma más nueva, como si lo hubiera previsto. Querían matar a Raye y, de paso, deshacerse de Roze, que ya no les servía. Los sentimientos de las dos, que ambas pueden convertir en poder, resonaron: se volvieron energía pura de Sky Striker y aparecieron en el campo como una sola guerrera, a través de un portal Multirole. Es Ace = Zero, inestable y muy frágil, pero con fuerza para cortarlo todo. Su Maniobra Lemnisgate comprime miles de portales en una hoja y parte en dos a las máquinas enemigas.","en":"Just as Raye and Roze were beginning to understand each other, the empire unleashed an army of H.A.M.P., its newest weapon, as if it had foreseen this. They meant to kill Raye and, in passing, get rid of Roze, who was no longer of use. The feelings of both, which each can turn into power, resonated: they became pure Sky Striker energy and showed up on the field as a single warrior, through a Multirole gate. She is Ace = Zero, unstable and very fragile, yet strong enough to cut through anything. Her Lemnisgate Maneuver compresses thousands of gates into one blade and bisects enemy machines."},"cards":["Sky Striker Ace = Zero","Sky Striker Special Maneuver - Lemnisgate!","Surgical Striker - H.A.M.P."]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness (YGOrganization)","title":"Story 11: Sky Striker [VBEX6]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-11-sky-striker-vbex6/","platform":"Blog","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Traducción de la historia de Sky Striker de la Valuable Book EX 6","en":"Translation of the Sky Striker story from Valuable Book EX 6"}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Sky Striker","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Sky_Striker","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Es lore de cartas y libros oficiales del OCG (Master Guide 6, Valuable Book EX 6) y del manga OCG Stories. No aparece en el anime de VRAINS.","en":"This is lore from official OCG cards and books (Master Guide 6, Valuable Book EX 6) and the OCG Stories manga. It does not appear in the VRAINS anime."}},{"slug":"snake-eye","kind":"archetype","name":"Snake-Eye, White Forest and Azamina","badge":{"es":"Una manzana maldita, un ojo en las ruinas y dos hermanas brujas contra Azamina","en":"A cursed apple, an eye in the ruins and two witch sisters against Azamina"},"origin":{"es":"Historia de las cartas (guías oficiales), no de la serie","en":"Card storyline (official guidebooks), not from the series"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"El bosque y la manzana","en":"The forest and the apple"},"p":{"es":"Según The Valuable Book EX 5, los demonios arrancan almas humanas y las vuelven Sinful Spoils. En el Bosque Blanco vive la bruja Diabell, que cría a niñas abandonadas: Silvy, Rucia, Astellar y Elzette. Las dos menores, aburridas, encuentran una manzana roja y se la llevan de regalo a Diabell. Era un Sinful Fruit que había traído un demonio. La maldición se apodera de la bruja, llena el bosque de espinas y mata a Silvy y a Rucia. Astellar y Elzette sobreviven repartiéndose el poder que le quedaba a Diabell.","en":"Per The Valuable Book EX 5, demons pull out human souls and turn them into Sinful Spoils. In the White Forest lives the witch Diabell, who raises abandoned girls: Silvy, Rucia, Astellar and Elzette. The two youngest, bored, find a red apple and bring it to Diabell as a gift. It was a Sinful Fruit that a demon had planted. The curse takes hold of the witch, fills the forest with thorns and kills Silvy and Rucia. Astellar and Elzette survive by splitting the power Diabell had left."},"cards":["Tales of the White Forest","Diabell, Queen of the White Forest","Susurrus of the Sinful Spoils"]},{"h":{"es":"Las almas perdidas y la cazadora","en":"The lost souls and the hunter"},"p":{"es":"El libro explica que el demonio es Azamina y que su fruta convierte el alma de quien la prueba en Sinful Spoils. Los cuerpos de Silvy y Rucia quedan como marionetas del demonio, y sus almas pasan a manos de Astellar. Ella se culpa por haber llevado la manzana y se dedica a buscar las almas de su familia, hasta que la conocen como la Seeker of Sinful Spoils: Diabellstar. Según EX 4, nadie sabe de su pasado y, mediante un hechizo propio, usa estos objetos pese a que a los humanos les debería ser imposible.","en":"The book explains that the demon is Azamina and that its fruit turns the soul of whoever tastes it into Sinful Spoils. The bodies of Silvy and Rucia stay behind as the demon's puppets, while their souls end up with Astellar. She blames herself for bringing the apple and sets out to find her family's souls, until she is known as the Seeker of Sinful Spoils: Diabellstar. Per EX 4, nobody knows her past, and through a spell of her own she uses these objects even though humans should not be able to."},"cards":["Deception of the Sinful Spoils","Like the Diabell","Diabellstar the Black Witch"]},{"h":{"es":"El ojo en las ruinas","en":"The eye in the ruins"},"p":{"es":"EX 4 la muestra en una taberna subterránea donde corre el rumor de un ojo extraño en unas ruinas al sudeste. Allí, el Divine Temple que veneraba a la deidad guardiana de la zona quedó deformado por un Sinful Spoil, el Snake-Eye. Diabellstar abate a las criaturas de un solo ojo hasta llegar a un ojo gigante y rojo, del que sale un dragón de llamas azules, Snake-Eyes Flamberge Dragon. Gana tras un combate más duro de lo previsto. Al recoger el Spoil, este se agrieta y nace un dragón pequeño, Poplar, que ella se lleva.","en":"EX 4 shows her in an underground tavern where word goes around of a strange eye in ruins to the southeast. There, the Divine Temple that honored the area's guardian deity has been warped by a Sinful Spoil, the Snake-Eye. Diabellstar cuts down the one-eyed creatures until she reaches a giant red eye, from which a dragon of blue flames, Snake-Eyes Flamberge Dragon, emerges. She wins after a harder fight than expected. When she picks up the Spoil, it cracks and a small dragon, Poplar, is born, and she takes it with her."},"cards":["Divine Temple of the Snake-Eye","Snake-Eyes Flamberge Dragon","Snake-Eyes Poplar"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Goblins y la bestia","en":"The Goblins and the beast"},"p":{"es":"De vuelta en su base subterránea, Diabellstar recibe a los Goblin Bikers, que quieren cobrar la recompensa por su cabeza. Los goblins creen que Poplar es uno de los Spoils de los carteles y se lo roban mientras un grupo la distrae. Su líder, Gabonga, suelta como último recurso a una bestia que lleva dentro el Spoil Aethon. Poplar despierta con hambre y se la traga entera, y se vuelve un gran demonio de fuego, Snake-Eyes Diabellstar. Ella lo encadena y lo lanza contra los goblins. Los goblins huyen.","en":"Back at her underground base, Diabellstar meets the Goblin Bikers, who want the bounty on her head. The goblins take Poplar for one of the Spoils from their posters and steal it while a decoy group keeps her busy. Their leader, Gabonga, releases as a last resort a beast that carries the Sinful Spoil Aethon inside it. Poplar wakes up hungry and swallows it whole, becoming a great fire demon, Snake-Eyes Diabellstar. She chains it and hurls it at the goblins. The goblins flee."},"cards":["Dramatic Snake-Eye Chase","Snake-Eyes Diabellstar","Goblin Biker Big Gabonga"]},{"h":{"es":"La Sinkeeper y la prisión","en":"The Sinkeeper and the prison"},"p":{"es":"Cuando los goblins se van, una sombra blanca sella el poder del demonio de fuego. Es Elzette, ahora Diabellze the Original Sinkeeper, que con su propio Sinful Spoil duerme a Poplar y a Diabellstar y se lleva a Poplar. Según EX 5, Diabellstar despierta prisionera en la Great Fortress Castle. Algunos goblins quedan atrapados en la pelea y otros derriban los muros para rescatarlos, pero salen monstruos de las paredes. Cuando ella intenta escapar, dos santas Azamina le cierran el paso, y sus Spoils, Silvera y Rciela, reaccionan: son los cuerpos transformados de Silvy y Rucia. Escapa por poco de su ataque.","en":"When the goblins leave, a white shadow seals the fire demon's power. It is Elzette, now Diabellze the Original Sinkeeper, who with her own Sinful Spoil puts Poplar and Diabellstar to sleep and takes Poplar away. According to EX 5, Diabellstar wakes up as a prisoner in the Great Fortress Castle. Some goblins get caught up in the fighting and others tear down the walls to rescue them, but monsters pour out of them. As she tries to escape, two Azamina saints block her way, and her Spoils, Silvera and Rciela, react: they are the transformed bodies of Silvy and Rucia. She narrowly escapes their attack."},"cards":["Diabellze the Original Sinkeeper","Azamina Debtors","Azamina Ilia Silvia"]},{"h":{"es":"Diabellze en el bosque negro","en":"Diabellze in the black forest"},"p":{"es":"Mientras tanto, Diabellze llega con Poplar al hogar de su infancia, convertido en un bosque negro lleno de santas Azamina. Con el poder del Original Sinful Spoils derriba a la más fuerte, Regina, y se encuentra con Queen Azamina, el cuerpo de Diabell dominado por el demonio y obligado a producir frutos malditos. Finge estar bajo control de Azamina, pero flaquea frente a quien fue su madre. Decidida a vengarse, se deja consumir por el Spoil y se convierte en Snake-Eyes Doomed Dragon. Es un último recurso que se ejecuta con su cuerpo.","en":"Meanwhile, Diabellze arrives with Poplar at the home of her childhood, now a black forest swarming with Azamina saints. With the power of the Original Sinful Spoils she brings down the strongest one, Regina, and meets Queen Azamina, Diabell's body taken over by the demon and forced to produce cursed fruit. She pretends to be under Azamina's control, but wavers before the woman who was like a mother. Set on revenge, she lets the Spoil consume her and becomes Snake-Eyes Doomed Dragon. It is a last resort carried out with her own body."},"cards":["Azamina Moa Regina","Queen Azamina","Snake-Eyes Doomed Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"La Saint Azamina","en":"Saint Azamina"},"p":{"es":"El ataque del dragón no sirve. El espíritu se burla, se transforma en Saint Azamina y con un golpe deshace la forma de dragón. Cuando va a rematar a la herida Diabellze, llega Diabellstar, vestida de negro. Diabellze, sorprendida por la madurez de su hermana menor, acepta unirse a ella. Invoca fantasmas del bosque y las almas recogidas hasta entonces y se las viste encima, y así se vuelve una verdadera bruja, Diabellze the White Witch. Según EX 5, el cuerpo de Elzette estuvo controlado por una santa Azamina y quedó libre al vencer a Morgana. La batalla sigue.","en":"The dragon's attack fails. The spirit sneers, transforms into Saint Azamina and undoes the dragon form with a single blow. As she is about to finish off the wounded Diabellze, Diabellstar arrives, dressed in black. Diabellze, struck by how much her younger sister has matured, agrees to team up. She calls the forest's ghosts and the souls gathered so far and wears them, becoming a true witch, Diabellze the White Witch. According to EX 5, Elzette's body was controlled by an Azamina saint and she was freed on beating Morgana. The battle goes on."},"cards":["Saint Azamina","Filia Diabell","Diabellze the White Witch"]},{"h":{"es":"La venganza y el final","en":"Vengeance and the ending"},"p":{"es":"Diabellstar usa su magia de unión para controlar la separación de alma y cuerpo y fusiona los Spoils de Silvy y Rucia: así nace Diabellstar Vengeance. Saint Azamina descarta el cuerpo y el alma de Diabell y muestra su verdadera naturaleza, una semidiosa que purifica los pecados humanos convirtiéndolos en Spoils. Poplar sirve de canal para el resto del poder de Diabell, y Diabellstar se transforma en el Vengeance Dragon y destruye a la diosa. Con ella cae la maldición: Diabell, Silvy y Rucia suben al cielo. En el epílogo, el bosque vuelve a ser tranquilo y se habla de una brujita blanca.","en":"Diabellstar uses her attachment magic to control the split of soul and body, and fuses the Spoils of Silvy and Rucia: Diabellstar Vengeance is born. Saint Azamina casts off Diabell's body and soul and shows her true nature, a demigod who purifies human sins by turning them into Spoils. Poplar acts as a channel for what is left of Diabell's power, and Diabellstar transforms into the Vengeance Dragon and destroys the goddess. The curse ends with her: Diabell, Silvy and Rucia ascend to heaven. In the epilogue the forest is peaceful again and people talk of a little white witch."},"cards":["Diabellstar Vengeance","Snake-Eyes Vengeance Dragon","Witch of the White Forest"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"Story 15: The Mysterious Sinful Spoils [VBEX4]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-15-the-mysterious-sinful-spoils-vbex4/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-08","why":{"es":"La traducción de la historia de Diabellstar y el Snake-Eye en The Valuable Book EX 4, que cita la wiki.","en":"The translation of the Diabellstar and Snake-Eye story in The Valuable Book EX 4 that the wiki cites."}},{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"Story 01: The Witch of the White Forest [VBEX5]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-01-the-witch-of-the-white-forest-vbex5/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-08","why":{"es":"La traducción de la historia del Bosque Blanco y Azamina en The Valuable Book EX 5, que cita la wiki.","en":"The translation of the White Forest and Azamina story in The Valuable Book EX 5 that the wiki cites."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Snake-Eye","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Snake-Eye","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: White Forest","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/White_Forest","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Azamina","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Azamina","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Sinful Spoils","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Sinful_Spoils","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 4 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_4_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-08"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-08"}],"notes":{"es":"Es una sola historia: Snake-Eye (EX 4, historia 15), White Forest y Azamina (EX 5, historia 1) son partes de la misma trama de los Sinful Spoils. Viene de guías de cartas, no de la serie. En el OCG, Sinful Spoils se llama Sinful Treasure. La wiki marca como desconocidos el dueño original del Snake-Eye y los cuerpos de ciertos Azamina; no los inventamos. El Spoil Aethon solo se toca de pasada. Fiendsmith y la sinergia de juego son aparte. Este texto no cubre la historia de Morganite ni los detalles de Morgana.","en":"This is one story: Snake-Eye (EX 4, story 15), White Forest and Azamina (EX 5, story 1) are parts of the same Sinful Spoils plot. It comes from card guidebooks, not from the series. In the OCG, Sinful Spoils is called Sinful Treasure. The wiki marks the Snake-Eye's original owner and the bodies of certain Azamina as unknown; we do not invent them. The Spoil Aethon is only touched on in passing. Fiendsmith and game synergy are separate. This entry does not cover the Morganite story or the details of Morgana."}},{"slug":"forbidden-maiden","kind":"archetype","name":"The Forbidden Maiden: Solemn, Forbidden and Darklord","badge":{"es":"Una doncella robó los tesoros de Dios y terminó como Darklord","en":"A maiden stole God's treasures and ended up a Darklord"},"origin":{"es":"Historia de las cartas (guías oficiales), no de la serie","en":"Card storyline (official guidebooks), not from the series"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"La sala del tesoro","en":"The treasure room"},"p":{"es":"Según la Master Guide 4, una doncella santa del Paraíso, agotada por una vida de penurias, entró por error en la sala del tesoro de Dios y se llevó una reliquia. Al acercar los labios al Cáliz sintió una dicha que no conocía. Volvió varias veces a sacar más cosas, sabiendo que estaba prohibido: la Lanza, que cortaba cualquier poder demoníaco, y el Vestido, que protegía de desastres y destrucción. Dios se dio cuenta.","en":"According to Master Guide 4, a holy maiden of Paradise, worn out by a hard life, wandered into God's treasure room by mistake and carried off a relic. Putting her lips to the Chalice gave her a joy she had never known. She kept coming back for more, fully aware it was forbidden: the Lance, which could cut through any demonic power, and the Dress, which shielded its wearer from disaster and destruction. God noticed."},"cards":["Forbidden Chalice","Forbidden Lance","Forbidden Dress"]},{"h":{"es":"La ira de Dios","en":"God's wrath"},"p":{"es":"Un día volvió a entrar sin saber que Dios le daba su última oportunidad. Su enojo fue enorme y la expulsó del Paraíso. La guía muestra en ese punto la Forbidden Scripture, un libro de profecías que Dios mismo escribió, y a Solemn Judgment. El arquetipo Solemn agrega que Solemn Strike muestra a Dios castigándola por haber tomado esos objetos.","en":"One day she went in again, unaware that it was God's final chance for her. His anger was great, and he cast her out of Paradise. At that point the guide shows the Forbidden Scripture, a volume of prophecies that God penned personally, along with Solemn Judgment. The Solemn archetype page adds that Solemn Strike shows God punishing her for taking those items."},"cards":["Forbidden Scripture","Solemn Judgment","Solemn Strike"]},{"h":{"es":"Doncella y bruja","en":"Maiden and witch"},"p":{"es":"El castigo la dejó como Condemned Maiden: no será perdonada hasta que se apaguen los poderes divinos que aún lleva dentro, y mientras tanto vaga por el mundo. The Valuable Book EX sigue desde ahí. Nunca recorrió el camino de expiación que Dios le marcó y se entregó a su destino, y, según el libro, su aspecto empeoraba día a día; lo ilustra con Condemned Witch.","en":"The punishment left her as Condemned Maiden: unforgiven until the divine powers still inside her fade away, and until then she wanders the world. The Valuable Book EX picks up from there. She never walked the path of atonement God set for her and gave herself over to her fate, and, per the book, her appearance worsened by the day; it illustrates this with Condemned Witch."},"cards":["Condemned Maiden","Condemned Witch"]},{"h":{"es":"La rebelión","en":"The revolt"},"p":{"es":"Despreció la última muestra de compasión de Dios y empezó a tramar en secreto derrocarlo y someterlo. Con sus palabras hizo caer a otras doncellas, y el libro ilustra ese momento con Indulged Darklord y Capricious Darklord. Así nació Condemned Darklord, para quien rebelarse ya era el mayor placer. Esa locura alcanzó a otros Darklord y aumentó su influencia. El arquetipo Solemn sitúa su venganza en Witch's Strike.","en":"She spurned God's last act of mercy and began secretly plotting to overthrow and subjugate him. Her words made other maidens fall, and the book illustrates that moment with Indulged Darklord and Capricious Darklord. Thus came Condemned Darklord, for whom rebelling had become the greatest pleasure. That madness reached other Darklords and widened her influence. The Solemn archetype page places her revenge in Witch's Strike."},"cards":["Indulged Darklord","Capricious Darklord","Condemned Darklord"]},{"h":{"es":"Morningstar entra en juego","en":"Morningstar enters"},"p":{"es":"El libro sigue con Morningstar, que aparece como The First Darklord. Absorbió a los Darklord que perdieron su poder por culpa de Condemned Darklord, algo que también entraba en los cálculos de ella. Aun sabiéndolo, no se detendrá hasta derribar a Dios. Para Condemned Darklord la jugada era usarlo: según el pie de la Forbidden Crown, se le acercó con la intención de aprovecharlo.","en":"The book continues with Morningstar, who appears as The First Darklord. He absorbed the Darklords that lost their power because of Condemned Darklord, which was also within her calculations. Even knowing this, he will stop at nothing to bring God down. For Condemned Darklord the play was to use him: according to the Forbidden Crown's caption, she approached him intending to take advantage of him."},"cards":["The First Darklord","Condemned Darklord"]},{"h":{"es":"La Corona Prohibida","en":"The Forbidden Crown"},"p":{"es":"En The Valuable Book EX 6, Morningstar quiso quedarse con el poder de todos los Darklord y volvió a atacar a los ejércitos de Dios. No pudo con ellos y se retiró con heridas incurables. Entonces apareció Condemned Darklord con la Santa Corona. Él solo quería derribar a Dios; ella, gozar. Tomó la corona, la llamó mujer perversa y se fue. Ella le deseó suerte, y las alas negras volaron al ocaso para un tercer intento. La sección cierra mostrando la carta Darklord Eveningstar, sin texto adicional.","en":"In The Valuable Book EX 6, Morningstar set out to take all the Darklords' power and attacked God's armies again. He could not hold against them and retreated with incurable wounds. Then Condemned Darklord appeared holding the Holy Crown. His only aim was to bring God down; hers was bliss. He took the crown, called her a deeply perverse woman and left. She wished him luck, and the black wings flew toward twilight for a third try. The section closes by showing the card Darklord Eveningstar, with no further text."},"cards":["Forbidden Crown","Darklord Eveningstar"]},{"h":{"es":"Nota: nombres y diseño","en":"Note: names and design"},"p":{"es":"Esto es diseño, no relato. Según la wiki, Indulged Darklord y Capricious Darklord no se basan en figuras teológicas sino en las dos figuras de Solemn Scolding, izquierda y derecha. Las cartas Solemn se llaman en japonés Kami no ○koku, como Senkoku en Judgment, Tsūkoku en Strike y Chūkoku en Scolding. El anime va aparte: Solemn Judgment aparece en Duel Monsters, en el mazo de Bandit Keith, y la wiki no lo vincula con esta cadena.","en":"This is design, not plot. Per the wiki, Indulged Darklord and Capricious Darklord are not based on theological figures but on the two figures in Solemn Scolding, left and right. In Japanese the Solemn cards are Kami no ○koku, such as Senkoku for Judgment, Tsūkoku for Strike and Chūkoku for Scolding. The anime is separate: Solemn Judgment appears in Duel Monsters, in Bandit Keith's Deck, and the wiki does not tie it to this chain."},"cards":["Solemn Scolding","Solemn Judgment"]}],"creators":[{"author":"Ness","title":"[VBEX] Number 8: Condemned Witch/Darklords","url":"https://ygorganization.com/activatingmydivinealmonds/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"El texto de Ness que usa la wiki para la historia de Condemned Witch y los Darklord.","en":"Ness's write-up that the wiki cites for the Condemned Witch and Darklord story."}},{"author":"Ness","title":"Story 15: Other Cards [VBEX6]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-15-other-cards-vbex6/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Reúne la historia de la Forbidden Crown y Condemned Darklord del libro EX 6.","en":"Collects the Forbidden Crown and Condemned Darklord story from the EX 6 book."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 4 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_4_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Solemn","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Solemn","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Forbidden (archetype)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Forbidden_(archetype)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Solemn Scolding","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Solemn_Scolding","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Solemn Judgment","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Solemn_Judgment","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Solemn Judgment (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Solemn_Judgment_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Solemn Strike","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Solemn_Strike","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Fallen Sanctuary","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Fallen_Sanctuary","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Celestial Knightlord Parshath","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Celestial_Knightlord_Parshath","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia sale de tres guías de cartas (Master Guide 4, The Valuable Book EX y EX 6), no de la serie; lo que dicen los arquetipos Solemn, Forbidden y Darklord se marca como tal. El anime va aparte. La wiki une The Sanctuary in the Sky a esta cadena solo por sinergia de juego (Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath y Divine Punishment en la lista del arquetipo Darklord), no por historia.","en":"The story comes from three card guidebooks (Master Guide 4, The Valuable Book EX and EX 6), not from the series; what the Solemn, Forbidden and Darklord archetype pages say is marked as such. The anime is separate. The wiki ties The Sanctuary in the Sky to this chain only through game synergy (Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath and Divine Punishment in the Darklord archetype's list), not through story."}},{"slug":"sanctuary-in-the-sky","kind":"archetype","name":"The Sanctuary in the Sky","badge":{"es":"Un campo de Hadas que protege a su dueño en la batalla","en":"A Fairy Field Spell that shields its owner in battle"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX y ARC-V (anime) y el juego de cartas","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX and ARC-V (anime) and the card game"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Poca historia en la wiki","en":"Little story on the wiki"},"p":{"es":"Yugipedia tiene muy poco relato sobre The Sanctuary in the Sky: es una Mágica de Campo que protege del daño de batalla a quien controla Hadas, y lo que se conserva de su paso por el anime es una lista corta de apariciones y mazos. En japonés se llama Tenkū no Seiiki. No hay una historia de personajes ligada a la carta que la wiki cuente.","en":"Yugipedia holds very little story about The Sanctuary in the Sky: it is a Field Spell that guards whoever controls Fairies from battle damage, and what survives of its time in the anime is a short list of appearances and Decks. In Japanese it is called Tenkū no Seiiki. There is no character story tied to the card that the wiki tells."},"cards":["The Sanctuary in the Sky"]},{"h":{"es":"Dos mazos del anime","en":"Two anime Decks"},"p":{"es":"La ficha animada anota apariciones en GX y en otra serie, y asigna la carta a los mazos de Aster Phoenix y de Zuzu Boyle. Según sus páginas, Aster sale en Yu-Gi-Oh! GX y Zuzu en Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V. El mazo de Aster en GX se armó con cuarenta cartas de ocho sobres al azar, treinta de ellas del set The Sanctuary in the Sky.","en":"The anime entry lists appearances in GX and in another series, and assigns the card to the Decks of Aster Phoenix and Zuzu Boyle. According to their pages, Aster appears in Yu-Gi-Oh! GX and Zuzu in Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V. Aster's GX Deck was put together from forty cards out of eight random packs, thirty of them from the set The Sanctuary in the Sky."},"cards":["The Sanctuary in the Sky"]},{"h":{"es":"Una serie con su nombre","en":"A series with its name"},"p":{"es":"La página de la serie define The Sanctuary in the Sky como la Mágica de Campo más las cartas que copian su nombre. La conecta con The Agent, Parshath y Counter Fairy, que dependen de tenerla en el campo; por ejemplo The Agent of Creation - Venus y Airknight Parshath. Ninguna página de Solemn, Forbidden o Darklord la menciona. El único lazo es de juego: la lista del mazo Darklord incluye Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath y Divine Punishment.","en":"The series page defines The Sanctuary in the Sky as the Field Spell plus the cards that copy its name. It connects it with The Agent, Parshath and Counter Fairy, which depend on having it on the field; for example The Agent of Creation - Venus and Airknight Parshath. No Solemn, Forbidden or Darklord page mentions it. The only tie is in play: the Darklord Deck list includes Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath and Divine Punishment."},"cards":["The Agent of Creation - Venus","Airknight Parshath"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: The Sanctuary in the Sky","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Sanctuary_in_the_Sky","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Sanctuary in the Sky (anime)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Sanctuary_in_the_Sky_(anime)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Sanctuary in the Sky (series)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Sanctuary_in_the_Sky_(series)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Aster Phoenix","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Aster_Phoenix","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Zuzu Boyle","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Zuzu_Boyle","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Agent","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Agent","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Parshath","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Parshath","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Darklord","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Darklord","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Fallen Sanctuary","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Fallen_Sanctuary","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Celestial Knightlord Parshath","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Celestial_Knightlord_Parshath","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Cubre el efecto, las apariciones en el anime y la serie, según las diez páginas de Yugipedia citadas. La wiki une esta carta con la cadena de Solemn, Forbidden y Darklord solo por sinergia de juego (Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath y Divine Punishment en la lista del arquetipo Darklord), no por historia. No se encontró una pieza de un creador que se pudiera comprobar.","en":"Covers the effect, the anime appearances and the series, per the ten Yugipedia pages cited. The wiki ties this card to the Solemn, Forbidden and Darklord chain only through game synergy (Fallen Sanctuary, Celestial Knightlord Parshath and Divine Punishment in the Darklord archetype's list), not through story. No verifiable creator piece was found."}},{"slug":"virtual-world","kind":"archetype","name":"Virtual World","badge":{"es":"Una metrópolis digital vigilada por cuatro guardianes divinos","en":"A digital metropolis watched by four divine guardians"},"origin":{"es":"Historia oficial de las cartas (The Valuable Book EX)","en":"Official card storyline (The Valuable Book EX)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Una metrópolis en el ciberespacio","en":"A metropolis in cyberspace"},"p":{"es":"Virtual World es una gigantesca metrópolis digital que existe en el ciberespacio. Su capital es Kauwloon, la carta Virtual World City - Kauwloon. Allí, unos algoritmos especiales examinan el torrente de información y de señales que llega, y de eso depende que todo se procese de forma correcta y adecuada. Sus habitantes tienen un aspecto elegante y cibernético, inspirado en animales y figuras de la mitología china y japonesa.","en":"Virtual World is a gigantic digital metropolis living in cyberspace. The capital city is Kauwloon, the card Virtual World City - Kauwloon. There, special algorithms examine the flood of information and signals that comes in, which is what keeps everything being processed correctly and properly. Its inhabitants have a sleek, cybernetic look, based on animals and figures from Chinese and Japanese mythology."},"cards":["Virtual World City - Kauwloon"]},{"h":{"es":"Cuatro puertas para revisar las señales","en":"Four gates to check the signals"},"p":{"es":"Kauwloon está rodeada por cuatro puertas gigantes, ubicadas en el norte, el este, el sur y el oeste, que sirven para investigar las señales de cualquier procedencia. Entre ellas figuran Virtual World Gate - Chuche, Virtual World Gate - Qinglong y Virtual World Gate - Xuanwu. En cada puerta hay apostada una bestia guardiana sagrada, de un grupo llamado los Cuatro Grandes Dragones Divinos.","en":"Kauwloon is surrounded by four giant gates, located at north, east, south and west, which serve to investigate signals of any origin. Among them are Virtual World Gate - Chuche, Virtual World Gate - Qinglong and Virtual World Gate - Xuanwu. At each gate a sacred guardian beast is posted, from a group called the Four Great Divine Dragons."},"cards":["Virtual World Gate - Chuche","Virtual World Gate - Qinglong","Virtual World Gate - Xuanwu"]},{"h":{"es":"Los guardianes de las puertas","en":"The guardians of the gates"},"p":{"es":"Los Cuatro Grandes Dragones Divinos inspeccionan las señales que llegan y, si resultan maliciosas o peligrosas, las rebotan. Procesan tanto que hacen un trillón de cálculos por segundo. Figuran el Phoenix, Fanfan (Virtual World Phoenix - Fanfan), el Dragon, Longlong (Virtual World Dragon - Longlong) y la Shell, Jaja (Virtual World Shell - Jaja). Según la wiki, parten de animales míticos chinos: Longlong, del Dragón Azul; Fanfan, del Ave Bermellón; y Jaja, de la Tortuga-Serpiente Negra.","en":"The Four Great Divine Dragons inspect the signals that arrive and, if they turn out malicious or dangerous, bounce them back. They process so much that they perform a quintillion calculations per second. They include the Phoenix, Fanfan (Virtual World Phoenix - Fanfan), the Dragon, Longlong (Virtual World Dragon - Longlong) and the Shell, Jaja (Virtual World Shell - Jaja). According to the wiki, they come from Chinese mythical animals: Longlong from the Azure Dragon, Fanfan from the Vermilion Bird and Jaja from the Black Turtle-Snake."},"cards":["Virtual World Phoenix - Fanfan","Virtual World Dragon - Longlong","Virtual World Shell - Jaja"]},{"h":{"es":"Shenshen, Laolao y sus discípulas","en":"Shenshen, Laolao and the disciples"},"p":{"es":"La suprema Kami Shenshen (Virtual World Kyubi - Shenshen) está a cargo del centro de Kauwloon. Quien despierte su ira no podrá volver a entrar en Virtual World. Su mano derecha es Laolao (Virtual World Roshi - Laolao), a quien tres discípulas ruegan que les enseñe: Toutou (Virtual World Oto-Hime - Toutou), Lulu y Nyannyan. Se esfuerzan por proteger el futuro de Virtual World.","en":"The supreme Kami Shenshen (Virtual World Kyubi - Shenshen) runs the heart of Kauwloon. Whoever incurs its wrath will never be allowed into Virtual World again. Its right hand is Laolao (Virtual World Roshi - Laolao), whom three disciples beg to teach them: Toutou (Virtual World Oto-Hime - Toutou), Lulu and Nyannyan. They strive to protect Virtual World's future."},"cards":["Virtual World Kyubi - Shenshen","Virtual World Roshi - Laolao","Virtual World Oto-Hime - Toutou"]},{"h":{"es":"Otras bestias guardianas y cómo se ven","en":"Other guardian beasts and how they look"},"p":{"es":"Más allá de los Cuatro Grandes Dragones Divinos hay muchas otras bestias guardianas, cada una con su función propia: Jiujiu (Virtual World Beast - Jiujiu), Lili (Virtual World Kirin - Lili) y Jiji (Virtual World Xiezhi - Jiji). Todos los habitantes de Virtual World parecen robots, sean humanoides o bestias, y emiten energía de forma electrónica. En Shenshen se nota más: sus colas parecen hechas de un torrente de energía intensa.","en":"Beyond the Four Great Divine Dragons, many more guardian beasts exist, and each has a role of its own: Jiujiu (Virtual World Beast - Jiujiu), Lili (Virtual World Kirin - Lili) and Jiji (Virtual World Xiezhi - Jiji). All of Virtual World's inhabitants look like robots, whether humanoid or beast, and give off energy electronically. It shows most in Shenshen, whose tails look made of a torrent of intense energy."},"cards":["Virtual World Beast - Jiujiu","Virtual World Kirin - Lili","Virtual World Xiezhi - Jiji"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"[VBEX Lore] Number 6: Virtual World","url":"https://ygorganization.com/vbex-lore-number-6-virtual-world/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"Relato original en inglés con la galería de ilustraciones de cada carta.","en":"Original story in English, with the illustration gallery of every card."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Virtual World","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Virtual_World","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia sale del relato oficial número 6 de The Valuable Book EX. Es una descripción del lugar y de sus habitantes, no una trama con sucesos. El texto de las cartas es aparte: acá solo se cuenta el relato. Los animales míticos de cada diseño vienen de la página del arquetipo. El relato no dice qué puerta queda en qué punto cardinal ni qué guardián está en cuál.","en":"The story comes from official storyline number 6 of The Valuable Book EX. It is a description of the place and its inhabitants, not a plot of events. Card text is a separate matter: only the story is told here. The mythical animals behind each design come from the archetype page. The storyline does not say which gate sits at which cardinal point or which guardian is at which gate."}},{"slug":"world-chalice","kind":"archetype","name":"World Chalice","badge":{"es":"La caída y el renacer de un mundo, desde el Bosque Celestial","en":"The fall and rebirth of a world, from the Celestial Forest"},"origin":{"es":"Master Guide 6 (guía oficial de historias de cartas)","en":"Master Guide 6 (official card storylines guide)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Lee, la Llave y la Gran Oscuridad","en":"Lee, the Key and the Great Darkness"},"p":{"es":"Según el mito del Bosque Celestial, Dios encerró la fuerza de destrucción, la Gran Oscuridad, bajo la corteza del planeta y dejó a la vida una Llave para enfrentarla. Millones de años después, la humanidad la desentierra. La científica Lee guarda un secreto: la Llave controla creación y destrucción, así que también pudo crear a la Gran Oscuridad. Su proyecto Mekk-Knight, Mekk-Knight of the Morning Star, invierte la energía y calcina la superficie. Siete Mekk-Knights lo destruyen y resellan la Gran Oscuridad. Se descubre que Lee murió, y según la guía los Mekk-Knights la habían sellado dentro del World Chalice.","en":"According to the Celestial Forest myth, God shut the force of destruction, the Great Darkness, beneath the planet's crust and left life a Key to face it. Millions of years later, humanity unearths it. The scientist Lee hides a secret: the Key controls creation and destruction, so it may also have created the Great Darkness. Her Mekk-Knight project, Mekk-Knight of the Morning Star, inverts the energy and scorches the surface. Seven Mekk-Knights destroy it and reseal the Great Darkness. Lee is found to have died, and the guide says the Mekk-Knights had sealed her inside the World Chalice."},"cards":["Mekk-Knight of the Morning Star","World Legacy - \"World Chalice\""]},{"h":{"es":"Los Héroes del Mundo","en":"The World Heroes"},"p":{"es":"En el Bosque Celestial, una aldea se protege con la barrera de un báculo sagrado que hereda Ib. Con ella viven su hermano Ningirsu, el joven Auram y la cría de dragón Imduk. Una voz misteriosa los lleva hasta una estructura que reacciona al báculo, y aparece Lee, un hada sellada por los Mekk-Knights, que les pide ser los Héroes del Mundo. Con el poder del World Chalice parten a reunir los otros World Legacies. Junto al World Armor, los Mekk-Knights aparecen y se llevan a Ib.","en":"In the Celestial Forest, a village is protected by the barrier of a sacred staff that Ib inherits. Her brother Ningirsu, the young Auram and the dragon whelp Imduk live alongside her. A mysterious voice leads them to a structure that responds to the staff, and Lee appears, a fairy sealed by the Mekk-Knights, who asks them to be the World Heroes. With the power of the World Chalice they set out to gather the other World Legacies. At the World Armor, the Mekk-Knights appear and take Ib away."},"cards":["Lee the World Chalice Fairy","Ib the World Chalice Priestess","World Legacy - \"World Armor\""]},{"h":{"es":"Iblee y la Llave en dos espadas","en":"Iblee and the Key as two swords"},"p":{"es":"Ib, secuestrada, duda de que los Mekk-Knights sean la Gran Oscuridad. Auram y los suyos atacan por sorpresa las ruinas y ellos se fusionan en Mekk-Knight Spectrum Supreme. Lee llega hasta Ib, se quita la máscara y toma su cuerpo: ambas renacen como Iblee, que anula el poder del World Chalice de los héroes. Los Mekk-Knights se vuelven contra ella, y Mekk-Knight Blue Sky hace a Auram heredero de la Llave, que se vuelve dos espadas. Iblee activa antes la World Lance, e Imduk la paraliza y Ib despierta y se clava la espada.","en":"Ib, kidnapped, doubts the Mekk-Knights are the Great Darkness. Auram and his friends launch a surprise attack on the ruins and the Mekk-Knights merge into Mekk-Knight Spectrum Supreme. Lee reaches Ib, drops her mask and takes over her body: the two are reborn as Iblee, who cancels the heroes' World Chalice power. The Mekk-Knights turn against her, and Mekk-Knight Blue Sky makes Auram heir to the Key, which becomes two swords. Iblee activates the World Lance first, then Imduk paralyzes her and Ib awakens and impales herself with the sword."},"cards":["Knightmare Corruptor Iblee","Mekk-Knight Blue Sky","World Legacy - \"World Lance\""]},{"h":{"es":"Babel, la muñeca y Crusadia","en":"Babel, the doll and Crusadia"},"p":{"es":"Pasan los años. Ningirsu noquea a Auram, herido, y se lleva el cuerpo de Ib con la espada. Solo quiere verla sonreír otra vez: con tecnología perdida arma una muñeca mecánica para alojar su alma, y los experimentos dejan de subproducto a los Orcust, mientras levanta la torre Babel. Auram, por su lado, se une mentalmente a un Krawler, recorre las tribus y funda la alianza Crusadia, que reactiva el World Crown. Empieza la Guerra del Mundo.","en":"Years pass. Ningirsu knocks out the wounded Auram and takes Ib's body and the sword. He only wants to see her smile again: with lost technology he assembles a mechanical doll to house her soul, and the experiments leave the Orcust as a byproduct, while he raises the tower Babel. Auram, for his part, links minds with a Krawler, travels among the tribes and founds the Crusadia alliance, which reactivates the World Crown. The World War begins."},"cards":["Orcustrated Babel","Crusadia Maximus"]},{"h":{"es":"El World Wand y los Guardragons","en":"The World Wand and the Guardragons"},"p":{"es":"Auram llega a Babel y se abre paso entre los Orcust. Ningirsu no quería llegar al cielo: quería dejar caer el World Wand desde la órbita para destruir el núcleo del planeta y despertar al World Ark, que manda sobre la vida y la muerte. El Wand cae. Imduk protege a todos con una barrera y muere; el World Ark lo rehace como Andrake. La sacudida despierta a los dragones y cada World Legacy se vuelve un Guardragon.","en":"Auram reaches Babel and fights through the Orcust. Ningirsu did not mean to reach the sky: he meant to drop the World Wand from orbit to destroy the planet's core and awaken the World Ark, which rules life and death. The Wand falls. Imduk shields everyone with a barrier and dies; the World Ark remakes him as Andrake. The shock wakes the dragons and each World Legacy becomes a Guardragon."},"cards":["World Legacy - \"World Wand\"","Guardragon Andrake","World Legacy - \"World Ark\""]},{"h":{"es":"Idlee, Justicia y Galatea","en":"Idlee, Justicia and Galatea"},"p":{"es":"Con el poder del World Ark, Ningirsu revive el alma de Ib en la muñeca. Pero Lee, que seguía dentro, toma el control y parece borrar a Ib; con el cuerpo de Ib y cinco Guardragons se vuelve Knightmare Incarnation Idlee. Guardragon Justicia llega del Bosque Celestial y se fusiona con Ib: nace Ib the World Chalice Justiciar. En verdad se borró el alma de la muñeca, Galatea, que se sacrificó por Ib, cuya alma estaba en el World Chalice.","en":"With the World Ark's power, Ningirsu revives Ib's soul in the doll. But Lee, who was still inside, takes control and seems to erase Ib; with Ib's body and five Guardragons she becomes Knightmare Incarnation Idlee. Guardragon Justicia arrives from the Celestial Forest and fuses with Ib: Ib the World Chalice Justiciar is born. In truth it was the doll's soul, Galatea, that was erased, sacrificing herself for Ib, whose soul was in the World Chalice."},"cards":["Knightmare Incarnation Idlee","Ib the World Chalice Justiciar","Galatea, the Orcust Automaton"]},{"h":{"es":"Almarduke y Dingirsu contra Idlee","en":"Almarduke and Dingirsu against Idlee"},"p":{"es":"Ib, ya revivida, se une a Auram y recupera el alma de Imduk, que se vuelve World Chalice Guardragon Almarduke. De las profundidades surgen los World Gears, recipiente del poder divino. Ante el último ataque de Idlee, Ningirsu usa lo que queda de Babel y de sus Orcust para forjar a Dingirsu, por el último deseo de Galatea, y destruye el cuerpo de Idlee. Su alma se funde con los World Gears, que se desbocan.","en":"Ib, now revived, joins Auram and recovers Imduk's soul, which becomes World Chalice Guardragon Almarduke. From the depths rise the World Gears, a container of divine power. Facing Idlee's last attack, Ningirsu uses what remains of Babel and his Orcust to forge Dingirsu, for Galatea's last wish, and destroys Idlee's body. Her soul fuses with the World Gears, which go out of control."},"cards":["World Chalice Guardragon Almarduke","Dingirsu, the Orcust of the Evening Star"]},{"h":{"es":"Avida y quienes cuidan a Ib","en":"Avida and those who watch over Ib"},"p":{"es":"Auram, que heredó por completo la Llave, es Mekk-Knight Crusadia Avramax, el Héroe del Mundo. Decide fundirse con los World Gears en vez de destruirlos y nace Avida, Rebuilder of Worlds, que restaura el mundo y se pierde con él. La Llave queda como espada y Ib viaja con ella. Ningirsu renace como Girsu, caballero guardián que la cuida sin mostrarse, y Galatea, que quiso renacer como alma y no como vasija, recupera un cuerpo de acero como Galatea-I.","en":"Auram, who has fully inherited the Key, is Mekk-Knight Crusadia Avramax, the World Hero. He chooses to merge with the World Gears rather than destroy them and Avida, Rebuilder of Worlds is born, restoring the world and vanishing with it. The Key remains as a sword and Ib travels with it. Ningirsu is reborn as Girsu, a guardian knight who watches over her unseen, and Galatea, who wished to be reborn as a soul and not a vessel, regains a steel body as Galatea-I."},"cards":["Avida, Rebuilder of Worlds","Girsu, the Orcust Mekk-Knight","Galatea-I, the Orcust Automaton"]}],"creators":[{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"[Card Lore] The World Legacy","url":"https://ygorganization.com/atinytaleoftimeconcerningwarbetweenfriends/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"La historia traducida en un solo artículo, con notas del traductor sobre términos japoneses como el báculo sagrado.","en":"The storyline translated in one article, with translator notes on Japanese terms such as the sacred staff."}},{"author":"NeoArkadia","title":"Story 11: The Knight of the Evening Star & The Automaton [VBEX5]","url":"https://ygorganization.com/story-11-the-knight-of-the-evening-star-the-automaton-vbex5/","platform":"YGOrganization","checked":"2026-11-07","why":{"es":"El epílogo traducido: Girsu, Galatea-I y la ilustración de cada carta, con la historia de cierre de Ib.","en":"The translated epilogue: Girsu, Galatea-I and each card's artwork, with the closing story of Ib."}}],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Master Guide 6 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Master_Guide_6_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: The Valuable Book EX 5 card storylines","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/The_Valuable_Book_EX_5_card_storylines","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Resume la historia de Master Guide 6 y el cierre de The Valuable Book EX 5 (No. 11); faltan los otros World Legacies, las tribus de Crusadia y varios giros intermedios. La guía cuenta el pasado de Lee entre las dos partes; acá va primero para ordenar causa y efecto. El mito de la creación se resume de la versión que cuentan en el Bosque Celestial.","en":"Summarizes the Master Guide 6 storyline and the closing of The Valuable Book EX 5 (No. 11); the other World Legacies, the Crusadia tribes and several intermediate turns are left out. The guide tells Lee's past between the two parts; here it comes first to keep cause and effect in order. The creation myth is summarized from the version told in the Celestial Forest."}},{"slug":"yubel","kind":"character","name":"Yubel","badge":{"es":"El espíritu de una carta que quiso quedarse con Jaden y terminó fusionado con él","en":"A card spirit that wanted Jaden all to itself and ended fused with him"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (anime): arco de Dimension World, y la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! GX (anime): the Dimension World arc, and the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Un guardián para el futuro Supreme King","en":"A guardian for the future Supreme King"},"p":{"es":"En el anime de GX, antes de ser carta, Yubel vivía como persona en un reino sin nombre. Un chico tenía el poder gentil de la Oscuridad (Gentle Darkness) y necesitaba protección hasta saber controlarlo; Yubel se ofreció de guardián y la transformación le dio forma de dragón. Ese chico, el futuro Supreme King, prometió amar solo a Yubel (en el doblaje inglés, no olvidar a Yubel ni alejarse de su lado). Mucho después, Industrial Illusions convirtió el espíritu de Yubel en una carta.","en":"In the GX anime, before it was a card, Yubel lived as a person in an unnamed kingdom. A boy held the Gentle Darkness power and needed protection until he could control it; Yubel volunteered as his guardian, and the change into a dragon form followed. The boy, the future Supreme King, vowed to love only Yubel (in the English dub, never to forget Yubel or leave their side). Much later, Industrial Illusions turned Yubel's spirit into a card."},"cards":["Yubel"]},{"h":{"es":"La carta de la infancia de Jaden","en":"The card from Jaden's childhood"},"p":{"es":"El padre de Jaden encuentra la carta y Jaden, reencarnación de aquel chico, vuelve a tener a Yubel como guardián. Yubel lo cuida de toda amenaza real o imaginada, y quien duela con Jaden termina en coma, como su conocido Osamu; los demás le tienen miedo. Jaden pide que KaibaCorp mande la carta al espacio, en un satélite aparte de sus diseños del concurso, los Neo-Spacians, con la esperanza de que adquiera los poderes de justicia que después tendría Elemental HERO Neos.","en":"Jaden's father finds the card, and Jaden, the reincarnation of that boy, has Yubel as a guardian once again. Yubel protects him from every threat, real or perceived, and anyone who Duels Jaden ends up in a coma, like his acquaintance Osamu; the others become afraid of him. Jaden asks KaibaCorp to send the card into space, in a separate satellite from his contest designs, the Neo-Spacians, hoping it would pick up the justice powers Elemental HERO Neos was later to gain."},"cards":["Elemental HERO Neos"]},{"h":{"es":"Locura en el espacio y el pacto con Viper","en":"Madness in space and the pact with Viper"},"p":{"es":"A diferencia de los Neo-Spacians, el satélite de Yubel queda expuesto a la Luz de la Destrucción (Light of Destruction), que enloquece a Yubel. En el japonés, Yubel cree que el envío fue un acto de amor de Jaden y disfruta del dolor, con rasgos de psicópata; en el doblaje lo vive como una traición. Al volver a la Tierra, el impacto destruye todo salvo un antebrazo, que encuentra Thelonious Viper. Yubel le promete revivir a su hijo adoptivo Pierce y lo lleva a crear los Bio-Bands y los Survival Duels, para absorber energía y rehacerse. En el juego, Yubel - Terror Incarnate solo se invoca desde Yubel.","en":"Unlike the Neo-Spacians, Yubel's satellite is exposed to the Light of Destruction, which drives Yubel insane. In the Japanese version, Yubel believes being sent away was an act of love from Jaden and relishes pain, with psychopathic traits; in the dub, Yubel takes it as a betrayal. When the capsule returns to Earth, the impact destroys everything but a forearm, which Thelonious Viper finds. Yubel promises to bring back his adopted son Pierce and pushes him to build the Bio-Bands and the Survival Duels, to absorb energy and rebuild a body. In the card game, Yubel - Terror Incarnate can only be Summoned by Yubel."},"cards":["Yubel - Terror Incarnate"]},{"h":{"es":"Duel Academy en otra dimensión","en":"Duel Academy in another dimension"},"p":{"es":"Cuando Jaden vence a Viper, Yubel ya no lo necesita: en el japonés le hace creer que su hijo vive y Viper cae de la arena. Luego lleva el Duel Academy a otra dimensión, posee a Marcel Bonaparte y convierte a los alumnos y profesores desplazados en zombis que alimentan su cuerpo. Con Marcel desafía a Jaden. Al recuperar la energía deja a Marcel y casi gana con Chaos Phantasm Armityle, hasta que la carta Rainbow Dragon de Jesse lo frena. La explosión se lleva a Jesse y a Yubel.","en":"After Jaden defeats Viper, Yubel no longer needs him: in the Japanese version Yubel makes him believe his son lives, and Viper falls off the arena. Yubel then moves Duel Academy to another dimension, possesses Marcel Bonaparte and turns the displaced students and teachers into zombies that fuel the restoration of their body. Through Marcel, Yubel challenges Jaden. Once the energy is back, Yubel leaves Marcel and nearly wins with Chaos Phantasm Armityle, until Jesse's Rainbow Dragon card stops it. The explosion consumes Jesse and Yubel."},"cards":["Armityle the Chaos Phantasm","Rainbow Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"El camino de Jaden al Supreme King","en":"Jaden's road to the Supreme King"},"p":{"es":"Para completar Super Polymerization y hacer que Jaden entienda su idea del amor, Yubel orquesta los hechos que lo hunden en la oscuridad como Supreme King. En esa dimensión, Brron sacrifica a amigos de Jaden para crear la carta, el Supreme King lo posee y comete atrocidades. Axel lo libera con el Eye of Orichalcum de Jim, pero Jaden queda atormentado y evita las Fusiones.","en":"To complete Super Polymerization and make Jaden understand their idea of love, Yubel orchestrates the events that sink him into darkness as the Supreme King. In that dimension, Brron sacrifices Jaden's friends to create the card, the Supreme King possesses him and he commits atrocities. Axel frees him with Jim's Eye of Orichalcum, but Jaden is left tormented and avoids Fusions."},"cards":["Super Polymerization"]},{"h":{"es":"El cuerpo de Jesse, Zane y Adrian","en":"Jesse's body, Zane and Adrian"},"p":{"es":"Yubel reaparece en el mundo de los espíritus dentro de Jesse, para destruir a quien lo separe de Jaden y unir las doce dimensiones con Super Polymerization. Zane desafía a Yubel, que usa los Advanced Crystal Beasts y gana aunque Zane invoca a Cyber End Dragon con 16000 de ATK, por el efecto de Power Bond. En su palacio, Adrian Gecko se rebeló. Yubel responde con las Sacred Beasts a su Exodia y lo derrota con el espíritu de Echo (en el doblaje, Adrian es enviado a las estrellas). Jaden duela después con Yubel por Jesse: Yubel fuerza un empate y le roba Super Polymerization con Last Trick.","en":"Yubel reappears in the Duel Spirit world inside Jesse, to destroy those who separate them from Jaden and unite the twelve dimensions with Super Polymerization. Zane challenges Yubel, who uses the Advanced Crystal Beasts and wins even though Zane Summons Cyber End Dragon with 16000 ATK, because of the effect of Power Bond. At their palace, Adrian Gecko has turned on them. Yubel answers his Exodia with the Sacred Beasts and defeats him with Echo's spirit (in the dub, Adrian is sent to the stars). Jaden later Duels Yubel over Jesse: Yubel forces a draw and takes Super Polymerization with Last Trick."},"cards":["Cyber End Dragon","Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"El último duelo y la fusión","en":"The last Duel and the fusion"},"p":{"es":"En su duelo final, Yubel se enfurece con los Neo-Spacians de Jaden, que siente como reemplazos. Yubel cree que Jaden nunca aceptará su amor y decide destruir las dimensiones con él. Jaden recupera los recuerdos de su vida pasada, perdona y vuelve a jurar su amor. Usa Super Polymerization para fusionar sus almas, con lo que la Luz de la Destrucción deja de influir en Yubel. En el doblaje, Yubel nunca abandona sus metas y Jaden promete luchar a su lado.","en":"In their final Duel, Yubel is angered by Jaden's Neo-Spacians, which Yubel sees as replacing them. Yubel believes Jaden will never accept their love and decides to destroy the dimensions along with him. Jaden regains the memories of his past life, forgives and vows his love once more. He uses Super Polymerization to fuse their souls, and the Light of Destruction stops influencing Yubel. In the dub, Yubel never gives up those goals and Jaden promises to fight together with them."},"cards":["Neo-Spacian Air Hummingbird"]},{"h":{"es":"Compañero de Jaden contra Nightshroud","en":"Jaden's partner against Nightshroud"},"p":{"es":"De vuelta en la Tierra, Jaden usa los poderes de Yubel y su espíritu aparece cuando enfrenta a Nightshroud. Nightshroud invoca a Yubel contra él; Jaden lo recupera fusionándolo con Neos en Neos Wiseman, que Nightshroud destruye con Darkness Neosphere. Yubel le pide usar su efecto para traer de vuelta a Neos, lo que destierra a Yubel del duelo, y le dice que no está solo. Después Yubel está en su duelo con Yugi, y en 3D Bonds Beyond Time lo ayuda a enfrentar a Paradox.","en":"Back on Earth, Jaden uses Yubel's powers and their spirit appears when he faces Nightshroud. Nightshroud Summons Yubel against him; Jaden gets Yubel back by fusing them with Neos into Neos Wiseman, which Nightshroud destroys with Darkness Neosphere. Yubel urges him to use Neos Wiseman's effect to bring Neos back, which banishes Yubel from the Duel, and tells him he is not alone. Later Yubel is present in his Duel with Yugi, and in 3D Bonds Beyond Time helps him face Paradox."},"cards":["Neos Wiseman","Darkness Neosphere"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Yubel (character)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yubel_(character)","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Jaden Yuki","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Jaden_Yuki","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yubel (card)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yubel","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yubel - Terror Incarnate","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yubel_-_Terror_Incarnate","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"La historia sigue el anime de GX y la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time; en la versión japonesa y en el doblaje inglés cambian los motivos de Yubel y el destino de Viper y Adrian, y se avisa cuando importa. La wiki nombra Chaos Phantasm Armityle en el anime; se ilustra con la carta Armityle the Chaos Phantasm. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"The story follows the GX anime and the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time; Yubel's motives and the fates of Viper and Adrian differ between the Japanese version and the English dub, and this is flagged where it matters. The wiki names Chaos Phantasm Armityle in the anime; it is illustrated with the card Armityle the Chaos Phantasm. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}},{"slug":"yugi-muto","kind":"character","name":"Yugi Muto","badge":{"es":"El chico que armó el Puzzle y despidió al faraón","en":"The kid who solved the Puzzle and said goodbye to the Pharaoh"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters (anime) y el manga original","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters (anime) and the original manga"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Un chico tímido y un Puzzle (anime)","en":"A shy kid and a Puzzle (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En el anime, Yugi vive con su madre y su abuelo Solomon en la tienda Kame Game, y el abuelo le enseñó Duel Monsters. Joey y Tristan lo molestaban, hasta que Yugi los defendió de Ushio y se hicieron amigos. Al terminar el Puzzle del Milenio, Yugi pasa a alojar sin saberlo a Yami Yugi, el espíritu del faraón Atem. Cuando Kaiba rompe delante de todos el Blue-Eyes White Dragon de Solomon, Yugi lo reta y Yami Yugi lo vence con Exodia, quedándose con el título de campeón mundial.","en":"In the anime, Yugi lives with his mother and his grandfather Solomon above the Kame Game Store, and his grandfather taught him Duel Monsters. Joey and Tristan used to pick on him, until Yugi defended them from Ushio and they became friends. Once the Millennium Puzzle is finished, Yugi unknowingly hosts Yami Yugi, the spirit of Pharaoh Atem. When Kaiba tears up Solomon's Blue-Eyes White Dragon in front of everyone, Yugi challenges him and Yami Yugi wins with Exodia, taking the World Champion title."},"cards":["Blue-Eyes White Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Duelist Kingdom: rescatar a Solomon (anime)","en":"Duelist Kingdom: saving Solomon (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Pegasus le gana a Yugi por tiempo y se lleva el alma de Solomon, así que Yugi entra al torneo de Duelist Kingdom para recuperarla. Allí elige a Dark Magician como su carta. En la versión japonesa ya sabía de Yami Yugi; en el doblaje se entera recién en el campamento. Frente al castillo, Kaiba se para al borde y Yugi cancela el ataque, así que Kaiba gana. Contra Pegasus, que lee mentes, Yugi y Yami Yugi cambian de lugar con cada carta boca abajo. Destruyen Toon World, Yami Yugi gana, y Yugi le da el premio a Joey.","en":"Pegasus beats Yugi on time and takes Solomon's soul, so Yugi enters the Duelist Kingdom tournament to get it back. There he picks Dark Magician as his own card. In the Japanese version he already knew about Yami Yugi; in the dub he only learns it at the campsite. Outside the castle, Kaiba stands on the edge and Yugi calls off the attack, so Kaiba wins. Against Pegasus, who reads minds, Yugi and Yami Yugi swap places with every face-down card. They destroy Toon World, Yami Yugi wins, and Yugi gives the prize to Joey."},"cards":["Dark Magician","Toon World"]},{"h":{"es":"Battle City: un faraón sin memoria (anime)","en":"Battle City: a Pharaoh without memories (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En Battle City, Marik controla a Keith y le roba el Puzzle; Yugi se queda en un edificio en llamas para rearmarlo. Yami Yugi no recuerda quién fue, hasta que Ishizu le cuenta que fue un faraón. Joey pierde un Juego de Sombras contra Marik, pero Yugi y Yami Yugi vencen a Kaiba en las semifinales y se quedan con Obelisk the Tormentor. Kaiba le da Fiend's Sanctuary antes del duelo final. Yami Yugi vence a Marik con Yugi alentándolo, y la regla de apuesta le da The Winged Dragon of Ra.","en":"In Battle City, Marik controls Keith and steals the Puzzle; Yugi stays inside a burning building to put it back together. Yami Yugi doesn't remember who he was, until Ishizu tells him he was a pharaoh. Joey loses a Shadow Game against Marik, but Yugi and Yami Yugi beat Kaiba in the semi-finals and keep Obelisk the Tormentor. Kaiba hands him Fiend's Sanctuary before the final Duel. Yami Yugi beats Marik with Yugi cheering him on, and the ante rule gives him The Winged Dragon of Ra."},"cards":["Obelisk the Tormentor","Fiend's Sanctuary","The Winged Dragon of Ra"]},{"h":{"es":"El nombre del faraón (anime)","en":"The Pharaoh's name (anime)"},"p":{"es":"En Egipto, el espíritu de Yami Yugi es absorbido por el Mundo de los Recuerdos. Yugi, Joey, Téa y Tristan lo siguen por un laberinto dentro del Puzzle para buscar su nombre. Yami Bakura, que posee a Tristan, desafía a Yugi a un Juego de Sombras con mazos creados desde la mente: Marshmallon protege a Silent Swordsman, y Gandora the Dragon of Destruction despeja el campo para que Silent Swordsman, con 4500 de ATK, remate. Con sus amigos hace aparecer en el cartucho el nombre Atem, y los Dioses se fusionan en Horakhty y destruyen a Zorc. Yugi admite sentirse algo solo, pero seguirán siendo un equipo.","en":"In Egypt, Yami Yugi's spirit is pulled into the World of Memories. Yugi, Joey, Téa and Tristan follow him through a maze inside the Puzzle to look for his name. Yami Bakura, who possesses Tristan, challenges Yugi to a Shadow Game with Decks made from their minds: Marshmallon protects Silent Swordsman, and Gandora the Dragon of Destruction clears the field so that Silent Swordsman, at 4500 ATK, finishes it. With his friends he makes the name Atem appear on the cartouche, and the Gods merge into Horakhty and destroy Zorc. Yugi admits he feels a bit lonely, but they will still be a team."},"cards":["Gandora the Dragon of Destruction","Marshmallon"]},{"h":{"es":"El Ritual de Batalla: ganarle a Atem (anime)","en":"The Battle Ritual: beating Atem (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Atem solo puede irse si pierde un duelo, y Yugi insiste en ser quien lo enfrente, con un mazo propio. Los Objetos del Milenio los separan en dos cuerpos. Atem invoca a los tres Dioses egipcios, pero Yugi usa Valkyrion the Magna Warrior y Magnet Force para devolverles el ataque de Slifer. Con Gold Sarcophagus elige Monster Reborn por adelantado y anula la revivida de Atem; Silent Magician cierra el duelo. Yugi llora y se llama débil, pero Atem le dice que ya es solo él mismo, Yugi Muto.","en":"Atem can only leave if he loses a Duel, and Yugi insists on being the one to face him, with a Deck of his own. The Millennium Items split them into two bodies. Atem summons all three Egyptian Gods, but Yugi uses Valkyrion the Magna Warrior and Magnet Force to turn Slifer's attack back on them. With Gold Sarcophagus he picks Monster Reborn in advance and negates Atem's revival; Silent Magician ends the Duel. Yugi weeps and calls himself weak, but Atem tells him he is now simply himself, Yugi Muto."},"cards":["Valkyrion the Magna Warrior","Gold Sarcophagus","Silent Magician"]},{"h":{"es":"El manga: ocho años armando el Puzzle","en":"The manga: eight years on the Puzzle"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Yugi tarda ocho años en terminar el Puzzle; al lograrlo queda como Guardián de los Juegos de Sombras, y en su cuerpo vive Dark Yugi, el faraón sin memoria, aunque él no lo sabe. Dark Yugi le gana a Ushio y a Kaiba, quien había cambiado por una copia el Blue-Eyes del abuelo. En Death-T, Yugi les confiesa a sus amigos que cree que hay otro Yugi en su interior. En el duelo contra Kaiba, la imagen de su abuelo comparando las cartas con piezas de un puzzle lleva a Dark Yugi a armar Exodia the Forbidden One.","en":"In the manga, Yugi takes eight years to finish the Puzzle; once he does, he becomes the Guardian of the Shadow Games, and the amnesiac Pharaoh Dark Yugi lives in his body without his knowing it. Dark Yugi beats Ushio and Kaiba, who had swapped his grandfather's Blue-Eyes for a copy. In Death-T, Yugi tells his friends he believes there is another Yugi inside him. In the Duel against Kaiba, the image of his grandfather comparing cards to puzzle pieces leads Dark Yugi to assemble Exodia the Forbidden One."},"cards":["Exodia the Forbidden One"]},{"h":{"es":"El manga: el nombre y el Ritual del Duelo","en":"The manga: the name and the Rite of the Duel"},"p":{"es":"En el manga, Yugi y sus amigos llegan al Mundo de los Recuerdos por la habitación del alma de Dark Yugi. Allí Anzu les indica que se concentren en los jeroglíficos hasta que aparecen en el cartucho que le dio al faraón: es Atem. Un mes después, en Egipto, Yugi arma un mazo para el Ritual del Duelo. Usa Stronghold the Moving Fortress y Magician's Circle, y vuelve a elegir Monster Reborn con Gold Sarcophagus. Al ganar, Atem le dice que es el único Yugi Muto del mundo.","en":"In the manga, Yugi and his friends reach the World of Memories through Dark Yugi's soul room. There Anzu tells them to concentrate on the hieroglyphs until they appear on the cartouche she gave the Pharaoh: it is Atem. A month later, in Egypt, Yugi builds a Deck for the Rite of the Duel. He uses Stronghold the Moving Fortress and Magician's Circle, and again picks Monster Reborn with Gold Sarcophagus. When he wins, Atem tells him he is the only Yugi Muto in the world."},"cards":["Stronghold the Moving Fortress","Magician's Circle"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yugipedia: Yugi Muto","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yugi_Muto","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yugipedia: Yugi Muto (manga)","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yugi_Muto_(manga)","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Cada bloque aclara si sigue el anime (con diferencias de doblaje cuando la wiki las marca) o el manga. El abuelo de Yugi es Solomon en el anime y Sugoroku en el manga. Las películas (Pyramid of Light, The Dark Side of Dimensions, Bonds Beyond Time) no se cubren. Los nombres cambian: Téa en el anime y Anzu en el manga; el apellido se escribe Muto en todo el texto. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"Each block states whether it follows the anime (with dub differences where the wiki notes them) or the manga. Yugi's grandfather is Solomon in the anime and Sugoroku in the manga. The films (Pyramid of Light, The Dark Side of Dimensions, Bonds Beyond Time) are not covered. Names differ: Téa in the anime and Anzu in the manga; the surname is spelled Muto throughout. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}},{"slug":"yusei-fudo","kind":"character","name":"Yusei Fudo","badge":{"es":"Del barrio marginal de Satellite a enfrentar a Z-one","en":"From the slums of Satellite to facing Z-one"},"origin":{"es":"Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's (anime)","en":"Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's (anime)"},"blocks":[{"h":{"es":"Satellite tras el Zero Reverse (anime)","en":"Satellite after the Zero Reverse (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Diecisiete años antes de la serie, una sobrecarga del sistema Ener-D, el Zero Reverse, partió Domino City: la zona más golpeada quedó aislada como Satellite y el público oyó que fue un desastre natural. Los padres de Yusei, desarrolladores del proyecto en KaibaCorp, murieron ahí. Yusei creció en Satellite con Jack Atlas y Crow Hogan, criados por Martha. De adolescentes formaron los Enforcers con Kalin Kessler; cuando Sector Security capturó a Kalin, el equipo se disolvió. Poco después Jack consiguió Red Dragon Archfiend.","en":"Seventeen years before the series, an overload of the Ener-D system, the Zero Reverse, split Domino City in two: the hardest-hit area was left isolated as Satellite, and the public heard it was a natural disaster. Yusei's parents, developers of the project at KaibaCorp, died there. Yusei grew up in Satellite with Jack Atlas and Crow Hogan, raised by Martha. As teens they formed the Enforcers with Kalin Kessler; when Sector Security captured Kalin, the team broke up. Soon after, Jack got Red Dragon Archfiend."},"cards":["Red Dragon Archfiend"]},{"h":{"es":"Stardust Dragon y la marca (anime)","en":"Stardust Dragon and the Mark (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Años después, Jack Atlas le robó a Yusei su Duel Runner y su Stardust Dragon y se fue a New Domino City, donde se volvió campeón de Turbo Duelos. Yusei cruzó para recuperar la carta y lo retó, pero el duelo se interrumpió cuando apareció el Crimson Dragon y ambos quedaron con una marca brillante en el brazo. Sector Security, dirigida por Rex Goodwin, arrestó a Yusei y lo condenó a rehabilitación en un centro, donde se enteró de la leyenda de los Signers. En la Fortune Cup, Yusei derrotó a Jack y quedó como nuevo rey de los Turbo Duelos.","en":"Years later, Jack Atlas stole Yusei's Duel Runner and Stardust Dragon and left for New Domino City, where he became Turbo Dueling champion. Yusei crossed over to recover the card and challenged him, but the Duel was cut short when the Crimson Dragon appeared and both ended up with a glowing mark on their arm. Sector Security, led by Rex Goodwin, arrested Yusei and sentenced him to rehabilitation at a facility, where he learned the legend of the Signers. In the Fortune Cup, Yusei beat Jack and became the new King of Turbo Duels."},"cards":["Stardust Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Los Dark Signers (anime)","en":"The Dark Signers (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Tras la Fortune Cup aparecieron los Dark Signers, muertos que volvieron por poder, venganza o asuntos pendientes, entre ellos Kalin. En sus Shadow Duels sacrificaban almas para liberar a las Earthbound Immortals. Yusei, Crow y los demás Signers los vencieron, pero no activaron a tiempo las unidades de control y revivió el King of the Netherworld. Rex Goodwin, que reunió el poder de un Dark Signer y el de un Signer, desafió a Yusei a un Shadow Turbo Duel. Yusei ganó, su marca pasó a Crow, y el Crimson Dragon destruyó al King usando a Majestic Star Dragon.","en":"After the Fortune Cup the Dark Signers appeared, dead people who came back for power, revenge or unfinished business, Kalin among them. In their Shadow Duels they sacrificed souls to unleash the Earthbound Immortals. Yusei, Crow and the other Signers beat them, but they did not activate the control units in time and the King of the Netherworld revived. Rex Goodwin, who held the powers of a Dark Signer along with those of a Signer, challenged Yusei to a Shadow Turbo Duel. Yusei won, his mark passed to Crow, and the Crimson Dragon destroyed the King using Majestic Star Dragon."},"cards":["Majestic Star Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Ghost, Lester y Crash Town (anime)","en":"Ghost, Lester and Crash Town (anime)"},"p":{"es":"La segunda temporada empezó con Ghost, un piloto que hacía chocar a los que perdían contra él. Invocó a Meklord Emperor Wisel, su monstruo Synchro Killer, y Yusei lo venció antes de descubrir que Ghost era un Duelbot. Después Vizor usó Accel Synchro contra Yusei, y Lester apareció con Meklord Emperor Skiel, derrotó a Luna y mandó a Leo al vacío, hasta que el Crimson Dragon lo salvó. En Crash Town, Yusei y Kalin se unieron en un duelo en equipo contra Lawton para liberar el pueblo y recuperar a los chicos secuestrados.","en":"The second season began with Ghost, a rider who made his opponents crash after beating them. He Summoned Meklord Emperor Wisel, his Synchro Killer monster, and Yusei beat him before learning that Ghost was a Duelbot. Later Vizor used Accel Synchro against Yusei, and Lester appeared with Meklord Emperor Skiel, beat Luna and sent Leo plunging off the road until the Crimson Dragon saved him. In Crash Town, Yusei and Kalin teamed up in a tag Duel against Lawton to free the town and recover the kidnapped kids."},"cards":["Meklord Emperor Wisel","Meklord Emperor Skiel"]},{"h":{"es":"World Racing Grand Prix (anime)","en":"World Racing Grand Prix (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Para el World Racing Grand Prix, Yusei armó el Team 5D's con Jack y Crow; Crow, que ya tenía Black-Winged Dragon desde su duelo con Bolton, se lesionó el hombro y lo reemplazó Akiza. En pleno torneo, Yusei alcanzó el Clear Mind con ayuda de Bruno y obtuvo Shooting Star Dragon para vencer a Primo. Jack consiguió Red Nova Dragon en Nazca gracias al Blazing Soul. En la final contra el Team New World, los tres juntaron esos dragones para superar a Aporia, y el Team 5D's se coronó campeón.","en":"For the World Racing Grand Prix, Yusei formed Team 5D's with Jack and Crow; Crow, who already had Black-Winged Dragon from his Duel with Bolton, injured his shoulder and Akiza replaced him. Mid-tournament, Yusei reached Clear Mind with Bruno's help and obtained Shooting Star Dragon to beat Primo. Jack got Red Nova Dragon in Nazca through the Blazing Soul. In the final against Team New World, the three combined those dragons to overcome Aporia, and Team 5D's became champion."},"cards":["Shooting Star Dragon","Red Nova Dragon","Black-Winged Dragon"]},{"h":{"es":"Z-one y el Ark Cradle (anime)","en":"Z-one and the Ark Cradle (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Con el torneo ganado, el Divine Temple bajó sobre la ciudad. Z-one y sus aliados Aporia, Antinomy y Paradox venían de un futuro arrasado por el Meklord Emperor Genocide, y usaban a Iliaster para cambiar la historia. Bruno resultó ser Antinomy: tras su duelo con Yusei se sacrificó para que sus amigos sobrevivieran. Leo despertó como sexto Signer con Life Stream Dragon. En el duelo final, Yusei juntó los dragones Signers, arrasó a los Timelords con Shooting Quasar Dragon y, ante Sephylon, the Ultimate Timelord, ganó con Stardust Dragon y Converging Wishes. Z-one se sacrificó para desintegrar el templo.","en":"With the tournament won, the Divine Temple descended on the city. Z-one and his allies Aporia, Antinomy and Paradox came from a future ravaged by the Meklord Emperor Genocide, and used Iliaster to change history. Bruno turned out to be Antinomy: after his Duel with Yusei, he sacrificed himself so his friends could survive. Leo awakened as the sixth Signer with Life Stream Dragon. In the final Duel, Yusei gathered the Signer Dragons, wiped out the Timelords with Shooting Quasar Dragon and, against Sephylon, the Ultimate Timelord, won with Stardust Dragon and Converging Wishes. Z-one sacrificed himself to disintegrate the temple."},"cards":["Shooting Quasar Dragon","Sephylon, the Ultimate Timelord"]},{"h":{"es":"El futuro del Team 5D's (anime)","en":"The future of Team 5D's (anime)"},"p":{"es":"Meses después, los Signers estaban sin rumbo: Akiza dudaba si irse a estudiar, Crow recibió una oferta de una liga profesional, Jack quería recuperar su título y Yusei terminó el mainframe Fortune, que evita el futuro de Z-one. Para que todos encontraran su camino, Yusei retó a Jack, sacó del campo a ambos ases con Star Excursion y ganó. Decidió quedarse en New Domino City.","en":"Months later, the Signers were adrift: Akiza wondered about going abroad to study, Crow received an offer from a pro league, Jack wanted his title back, and Yusei finished the Fortune mainframe, which prevents Z-one's future. So everyone could find a path, Yusei challenged Jack, removed both aces with Star Excursion and won. He chose to stay in New Domino City."},"cards":["Red Dragon Archfiend"]}],"creators":[],"sources":[{"name":"Yusei Fudo - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yusei_Fudo","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Yu-Gi-Oh! 5D's - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!_5D's","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Zero Reverse - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Zero_Reverse","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Iliaster - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Iliaster","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Crimson Dragon - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Crimson_Dragon","checked":"2026-11-07"},{"name":"Jack Atlas - Yugipedia","url":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Jack_Atlas","checked":"2026-11-07"}],"notes":{"es":"Historia del anime 5D's según Yugipedia; no cubre la película 3D Bonds Beyond Time, que se cuenta en la entrada de Jaden. No se enlaza ninguna pieza de creadores porque no encontramos una que se pudiera abrir y comprobar.","en":"Story of the 5D's anime per Yugipedia; it does not cover the film 3D Bonds Beyond Time, which is told in Jaden's entry. No creator piece is linked because we found none that could be opened and checked."}}]);